          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"6b142d4e3d515bde38d389cb\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cTom!\u201d\\n\\nNo response.\\n\\n\u201cTOM!\u201d\\n\\nSilence.\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s come over that boy, I\u2019d like to know? You, TOM!\u201d\\n\\nStill no reply.\\n\\nThe old lady slid her spectacles down and peered over them around the room; then pushed them back and glanced beneath them. She hardly ever looked straight through them for anything as trifling as a boy; they were her ceremonial pair, the pride of her heart, meant for \u201cstyle\u201d rather than duty\u2014she could have seen through a couple of stove lids just as clearly. She paused, perplexed, then said, not in a harsh tone but loud enough for the furniture to hear:\\n\\n\u201cWell, I swear, if I get hold of you I\u2019ll\u2014\u201d\\n\\nShe did not finish, for she was already stooping and poking beneath the bed with the broom, needing all her breath to punctuate each jab. She dragged out nothing but the cat.\\n\\n\u201cI never saw the like of that boy!\u201d\\n\\nShe moved to the doorway, stood there, and gazed out at the tomato vines and \u201cjimpson\u201d weeds that passed for a garden. No Tom. So she raised her voice at a slant meant to carry and called:\\n\\n\u201cY-o-u-u TOM!\u201d\\n\\nA faint sound came from behind, and she turned just in time to grab a small boy by the slack of his roundabout and halt his dash.\\n\\n\u201cThere now! I might have guessed that closet. What have you been doing in there?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNothing.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNothing! Look at your hands. And look at your mouth. What is that stuff?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t know, aunt.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, I do. It\u2019s jam\u2014that\u2019s what. Forty times I\u2019ve told you if you didn\u2019t leave that jam be I\u2019d skin you. Hand me that switch.\u201d\\n\\nThe switch wavered in the air\u2014the danger was dire\u2014\\n\\n\u201cMy! Look behind you, aunt!\u201d\\n\\nThe old lady spun around, snatching her skirts to