          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"4ba44cea7ad9745719d8fd0e\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cNow,\u201d said Mr. Lorry, lightly resting his hand on the Doctor\u2019s arm again after a short silence, \u201chow would you explain this attack?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI believe,\u201d Doctor Manette replied, \u201cthere was a powerful and sudden revival of the thoughts and memories that first caused his illness. Some intense, painful associations came back vividly, I think. He likely feared for a long time that those memories would return\u2014perhaps under certain conditions, perhaps on a particular occasion. He tried to prepare himself in vain; maybe the effort to prepare only made him less able to endure it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWould he remember what happened during the relapse?\u201d Mr. Lorry asked, hesitant.\\n\\nThe Doctor looked around the room in distress, shook his head, and answered quietly, \u201cNot at all.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNow, about the future,\u201d hinted Mr. Lorry.\\n\\n\u201cAs for the future,\u201d said the Doctor, regaining strength, \u201cI have great hope. Since Heaven was merciful enough to restore him so quickly, I should have great hope. He gave way under the pressure of a complicated something, long feared and vaguely expected and resisted, and after the storm broke and passed, I hope the worst is behind him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, well! That\u2019s reassuring. I\u2019m grateful!\u201d said Mr. Lorry.\\n\\n\u201cI am grateful,\u201d the Doctor echoed, bowing his head reverently.\\n\\n\u201cThere are two other points,\u201d said Mr. Lorry, \u201con which I need guidance. May I continue?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou could do your friend no better service.\u201d The Doctor offered his hand.\\n\\n\u201cTo the first point, then. He is scholarly and unusually driven; he throws himself passionately into gaining professional knowledge, running experiments, many pursuits. Does he do too much?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI think not. His mind may simply need constant occupation. That might be partly his nature, partly the result of suffering. The less it is engaged with healthy work, the more it risks turning toward unhealthy thoughts. He may have noticed this in himself and acted on it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou are sure he isn\u2019t under too much strain?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI think I\u2019m quite sure.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Manette, if he were overworked now\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Lorry, I doubt that would happen easily. There\u2019s been heavy pressure in one direction, and it needs a counterbalance.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cExcuse me, as a persistent man of business. Suppose for a moment he were overworked; would it show up as a return of this disorder?\u201d\"}"
