          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"0046eb013d965a7379a3251f\",\"rewritten_text\":\"They know what a clever boy he is; they\u2019ll give the Artful nothing less than life.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you mean by lagging and a lifer?\u201d demanded Mr. Bolter. \u201cWhat\u2019s the use of talking like that to me? Why don\u2019t you speak so I can understand?\u201d\\n\\nFagin was about to translate these mysterious expressions into plain speech\u2014and, interpreted, Mr. Bolter would have been told they meant \u201ctransportation for life\u201d\u2014when the dialogue was cut short by the entrance of Master Bates, hands shoved in his pockets, face twisted into a semi-comical look of distress.\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s all over, Fagin,\u201d said Charley, once he and his new companion were introduced.\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you mean?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThey\u2019ve found the gentleman who owns the box; two or three more are coming to identify him; and the Artful\u2019s booked for a passage abroad,\u201d replied Master Bates. \u201cI\u2019ll need a full suit of mourning, Fagin, and a hatband to visit him in before he sets out. To think of Jack Dawkins\u2014flash Jack\u2014the Dodger\u2014the Artful Dodger\u2014being sent overseas for a common two-penny-halfpenny snuffbox! I never thought he\u2019d do it for less than a gold watch, chain, and seals at the very least. Oh, why didn\u2019t he rob some rich old gentleman of all his valuables and go out like a gentleman, not like a common thief, without any honor or glory!\u201d\\n\\nWith this outpouring for his unlucky friend, Master Bates dropped into the nearest chair, looking thoroughly dejected.\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you mean by saying he has neither honor nor glory!\u201d cried Fagin, shooting an angry glance at his pupil. \u201cWasn\u2019t he always the best among you? Could any of you touch him or even come near his scent? Eh?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot one,\u201d answered Master Bates, his voice thick with regret. \u201cNot one.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen what are you talking about?\u201d snapped Fagin. \u201cWhat are you blubbering for?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBecause it isn\u2019t on the record, is it?\u201d said Charley, driven to outright defiance of his venerable mentor by the pull of his sorrow. \u201cBecause it won\u2019t show up in the indictment; because nobody will ever know half of what he was. How will he stand in the Newgate Calendar? Maybe he won\u2019t be there at all. Oh, my eyes, what a blow this is!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHa! ha!\u201d laughed Fagin, stretching out his right hand and turning to Mr. Bolter in a fit of chuckling that shook him as if he had the palsy. \u201cLook how proud they are of their trade, my dear.\u201d\"}"
