          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"061bbb035c2643b8cf367c05\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cI\u2019m agreed. It\u2019s the best idea. Just hold hands and swear we\u2014\u201d \u201cOh no, that won\u2019t work for this. That\u2019s fine for little trifling things\u2014especially with girls, because they\u2019ll go back on you and blab if they get mad\u2014but there ought to be writing for something big like this. And blood.\u201d Tom loved the idea. It felt deep, dark, and terrible; the time, the situation, and the surroundings matched it perfectly. He picked up a clean pine shingle in the moonlight, pulled a bit of red keel from his pocket, tilted it toward the moon, and slowly scratched out these lines, biting his tongue on each downstroke and easing up on the upstrokes. \u201cHuck Finn and Tom Sawyer swear they will keep quiet about This and they hope they drop dead on the spot if they ever tell and rot.\u201d Huckleberry admired Tom\u2019s ease with writing and the grandeur of his words. He immediately pulled a pin from his lapel to prick his skin, but Tom stopped him. \u201cHold on! Don\u2019t do that. A pin\u2019s brass. It might have verdigris on it.\u201d \u201cWhat\u2019s verdigris?\u201d \u201cIt\u2019s poison, that\u2019s what. Just swallow some once\u2014you\u2019ll find out.\u201d So Tom unwound the thread from one of his needles, and each boy pricked his thumb and squeezed out a drop of blood. After many squeezes, Tom managed to sign his initials, using the ball of his little finger as a pen. Then he showed Huckleberry how to make an H and an F, and the oath was done. They buried the shingle close to the wall with gloomy rituals and muttered spells, and the chains on their tongues were considered locked with the key thrown away. A figure crept quietly through a gap at the other end of the ruined building just then, but they didn\u2019t see it. \u201cTom,\u201d whispered Huckleberry, \u201cdoes this keep us from ever telling\u2014always?\u201d \u201cOf course it does. No matter what happens, we have to stay quiet. We\u2019d drop dead\u2014you know that.\u201d \u201cYes, I reckon so.\u201d They kept whispering a while. Suddenly a dog let out a long, mournful howl just outside, barely ten feet away. The boys grabbed each other, shaking with fear. \u201cWhich of us is he after?\u201d gasped Huckleberry. \u201cI don\u2019t know\u2014look through the crack. Quick!\u201d \u201cNo, you, Tom!\u201d \u201cI can\u2019t\u2014I can\u2019t do it, Huck!\u201d\"}"
