          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"d922afe8acff1fdc7febc998\",\"rewritten_text\":\"WHEN the wedding day arrived, about three weeks later, St. Peter\u2019s filled to overflowing with a throng of fashionable people. The Dean of Chichester read the service with great solemnity, and everyone declared they had never seen a more striking pair than bride and groom. Yet they were more than simply striking\u2014they were content. Not once did Lord Arthur rue the trials he had endured for Sybil, while she, for her part, offered him the finest gifts a woman can bestow\u2014adoration, gentleness, and affection. Reality had not shredded their romance. They always felt youthful.\\n\\nSome years later, after two beautiful children were born to them, Lady Windermere came down to visit Alton Priory, that charming old estate the Duke had given his son as a wedding present; and one afternoon, as she sat beneath a lime-tree in the garden with Lady Arthur, watching the young boy and girl dart up and down the rose walk like flickering sunbeams, she suddenly clasped her hostess\u2019s hand and asked, \u2018Are you happy, Sybil?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Dear Lady Windermere, naturally I am happy. Aren\u2019t you?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018I have no time for happiness, Sybil. I invariably like the last person introduced to me; but generally, once I get to know people, they bore me.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Don\u2019t your lions amuse you, Lady Windermere?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Oh heavens, no! lions are only entertaining for a single season. Once their manes are trimmed, they are the dullest creatures imaginable. Besides, they misbehave terribly if you treat them really well. Remember that dreadful Mr. Podgers? He turned out a complete fraud. Of course I didn\u2019t mind that in the least, and even when he asked to borrow money I forgave him, but I could not tolerate his making love to me. He has quite soured me on cheiromancy. I am into telepathy now. Far more diverting.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018You mustn\u2019t say a word against cheiromancy here, Lady Windermere; it is the only topic Arthur cannot abide being teased about. I assure you he takes it quite seriously.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Surely he doesn\u2019t actually believe in it, Sybil?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Ask him yourself, Lady Windermere\u2014here he comes,\u2019 and Lord Arthur strolled up the garden carrying a huge bunch of yellow roses, the two children dancing about him.\\n\\n\u2018Lord Arthur?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Yes, Lady Windermere.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018You can\u2019t truly believe in cheiromancy?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Of course I do,\u2019 replied the young man with a smile.\\n\\n\u2018But why?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Because I owe to it all the joy of my life,\u2019 he murmured, dropping into a wicker chair.\"}"
