          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"1fe7c34d60c2455cd4bd0b02\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Soon his voice floated down in a kind of halloo.  \u201cHow much farther do I need to go?\u201d  \u201cHow high are you?\u201d asked Legrand.  \u201cEver so far,\u201d the Black man replied. \u201cI can see the sky through the top of the tree.\u201d  \u201cForget the sky. Listen to me. Look down the trunk and count the branches below you on this side. How many have you passed?\u201d  \u201cOne, two, three, four, five\u2014I just passed five big branches on this side, sir.\u201d  \u201cThen climb one branch higher.\u201d  A few minutes later the voice called out again, saying he had reached the seventh branch.  \u201cNow, Jup,\u201d Legrand shouted, clearly agitated, \u201cwork your way along that branch as far as you can. If you notice anything unusual, tell me.\u201d At that point any lingering doubt I had about my poor friend\u2019s sanity vanished. I had no choice but to conclude he had lost his mind, and I grew seriously concerned about getting him home. While I was debating what to do, Jupiter\u2019s voice rang out again.  \u201cAlmost afraid to go much farther on this branch\u2014it\u2019s dead almost all the way.\u201d  \u201cDid you say it was a dead branch, Jupiter?\u201d cried Legrand, his voice shaking.  \u201cYes, sir, dead as a doornail\u2014done for sure\u2014gone from this world.\u201d  \u201cWhat on earth am I to do?\u201d asked Legrand, sounding utterly distraught.  \u201cDo?\u201d I said, glad for a chance to cut in. \u201cWhy, come home and go to bed. Come now! Be sensible. It\u2019s getting late, and remember your promise.\u201d  \u201cJupiter,\u201d he shouted, ignoring me entirely, \u201cdo you hear me?\u201d  \u201cYes, Master Will, hear you perfectly well.\u201d  \u201cTest the wood with your knife and see if it\u2019s very rotten.\u201d  \u201cIt\u2019s rotten, sir, sure enough,\u201d the man replied after a moment, \u201cbut not as rotten as it could be. I could risk going a little farther on the branch by myself, that\u2019s true.\u201d  \u201cBy yourself! What do you mean?\u201d  \u201cI mean the bug. It\u2019s really heavy. Suppose I drop it first, then the branch won\u2019t break with just the weight of one Black man.\u201d  \u201cYou infernal scoundrel!\u201d Legrand shouted, visibly relieved. \u201cWhat do you mean by saying such nonsense? If you drop that beetle, I\u2019ll wring your neck. Now listen, Jupiter\u2014do you hear me?\u201d  \u201cYes, sir, no need to shout at a poor Black man like that.\u201d  \u201cGood. Now pay attention. If you crawl out on that branch as far as you think is safe and don\u2019t let go of the beetle, I\u2019ll give you a silver dollar the moment you get down.\u201d\"}"
