          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"9d3a8a6294ac112a5a1c1d17\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201c\u2018We went to your lodgings,\u2019 said the first, \u2018and, not having the good fortune to find you at home, and being told you were likely walking this way, we pursued in hopes of overtaking you. Will you be so good as to step into the carriage?\u2019\\n\\n\u201cThe bearing of both was domineering, and as these words were uttered, they shifted so as to station me between themselves and the carriage door. They were armed; I was not.\\n\\n\u201c\u2018Gentlemen,\u2019 I replied, \u2018pardon me; I have a habit of asking who honours me by requesting my aid, and what sort of matter I am expected to attend.\u2019\\n\\n\u201cThe answer came from the one who had spoken second. \u2018Doctor, our clients are persons of quality. For the matter itself, we rely on your ability to discover it more surely than we can explain it. That is sufficient. Will you please to enter the carriage?\u2019\\n\\n\u201cI had no choice but to obey, and stepped in silently. Both followed\u2014one springing in last after raising the steps. The carriage wheeled round and proceeded at its former pace.\\n\\n\u201cI repeat this exchange exactly as it happened. I am confident that it is verbatim. I set down everything precisely as it occurred, forcing my thoughts not to stray from the duty. When I place the broken marks that follow, I stop for the moment and return the paper to its concealment.\\n\\n*****\\n\\n\u201cThe carriage left the city streets, passed through the North Barrier, and came out onto the country road. At two-thirds of a league beyond the Barrier\u2014though I reckoned that distance only afterwards when I went over it again\u2014it turned out of the main avenue and soon halted at an isolated house. The three of us dismounted and walked by a damp, soft garden path, where a forsaken fountain had overflowed, to the house door. It did not open at once when we rang, and one of my two escorts struck the man who admitted us across the face with his heavy riding glove.\\n\\n\u201cThis act hardly caught my special attention, for I had seen common folk beaten more casually than dogs. Yet the other, being angered also, struck the man in the same way with his arm; the likeness in the brothers\u2019 appearance and carriage was then so exact that I realised in that instant they were twins.\\n\\n\u201cFrom the moment we descended at the outer gate (which we found locked, and which one brother opened to admit us and then locked again), I had heard cries issuing from an upper room.\u201d\"}"
