          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"05b6428d988f32c833031def\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWell, monsieur le mauvais sujet,\u201d the old lady exclaimed as he walked in. \u201cWhy haven\u2019t you come to see me all this time?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Lady Clem, I never get a moment to myself,\u201d Lord Arthur said with a smile.\\n\\n\u201cI suppose you mean you spend every day with Miss Sybil Merton, buying chiffons and talking nonsense? I cannot understand why people make such a fuss about getting married. In my day we never dreamed of cooing in public, or in private either.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI promise you I haven\u2019t seen Sybil for twenty-four hours, Lady Clem. As far as I can tell, she belongs entirely to her milliners.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOf course; that\u2019s the only reason you visit an ugly old woman like me. You men should take heed. On a fait des folies pour moi, and now I\u2019m just a poor rheumatic creature, with a false front and a bad temper. If not for dear Lady Jansen sending me all the worst French novels she can find, I don\u2019t think I could get through the day. Doctors are useless except for taking fees. They can\u2019t even cure my heartburn.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019ve brought you a cure for that, Lady Clem,\u201d said Lord Arthur seriously. \u201cIt\u2019s a marvelous thing invented by an American.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t think I like American inventions, Arthur. I\u2019m certain I don\u2019t. I read some American novels lately, and they were pure nonsense.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, but there\u2019s no nonsense here, Lady Clem! I promise it\u2019s a perfect cure. You must agree to try it.\u201d Lord Arthur took a small box from his pocket and handed it to her.\\n\\n\u201cWell, the box is delightful, Arthur. Is it really a gift? That\u2019s very sweet of you. And this is the wonderful medicine? It looks like a bonbon. I\u2019ll take it at once.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGood heavens, Lady Clem,\u201d cried Lord Arthur, grabbing her hand, \u201cyou mustn\u2019t do that. It\u2019s a homeopathic medicine. If you take it without having heartburn, it might do you great harm. Wait until you have an attack and take it then. You\u2019ll be amazed at the effect.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019d like to take it now,\u201d said Lady Clementina, holding the little transparent capsule up to the light, the tiny bubble of liquid aconitine floating inside. \u201cI\u2019m sure it\u2019s delicious. The truth is, although I hate doctors, I adore medicines. Still, I\u2019ll keep it for my next attack.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd when will that be?\u201d Lord Arthur asked eagerly.\"}"
