          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"35be4bf3a52c1309f5b2bd59\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The encircling oaks were the dwelling of a clan of nightingales\u2014there you find me now; Idris, in the sweet bloom of youth, stands beside me\u2014remember, I count but twenty-two years, and scarce seventeen summers have washed over the darling of my soul. The river, swelled by autumn rains, flooded the meadows, and Adrian, in his cherished skiff, occupied himself with the perilous amusement of tearing the highest branch from a drowned oak. Oh Adrian, art thou so weary of existence that thou flirtest thus with peril?\u2014\\n\\nHe gained his prize and steered his boat through the torrent; we watched him anxiously, yet the current drew him away from us; he was compelled to land far below and take a wide circuit before he could reach us. \u201cHe is safe!\u201d cried Idris, when he sprang ashore and waved the branch aloft as a sign of triumph; \u201cwe will await him here.\u201d\\n\\nWe found ourselves alone; the sun had set; the nightingales began their melody; the evening star gleamed clear amid the yet unwaning light in the west. The azure eyes of my heavenly girl rested on that dear emblem of herself: \u201cHow the light quivers,\u201d she murmured, \u201cwhich is the star\u2019s very life. Its flickering brilliance seems to confess that its condition, even like our own on earth, is shifting and unsteady; it fears, meseems, and it loves.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLook not on the star, beloved and generous friend,\u201d I exclaimed, \u201cseek not love in _its_ trembling beams; gaze not on far worlds; speak not of the mere fancy of emotion. Long have I held my peace; long to sickness have I yearned to speak, to offer to you my soul, my life, my whole being. Look not on the star, dear love\u2014or do, and let that immortal spark plead for me; let it be witness and advocate, silent as it glows\u2014love is to me as light to the star; while it remains uneclipsed by nothingness, so shall I adore you.\u201d\\n\\nNever to the world\u2019s hardened eye can the ecstasy of that instant be disclosed. Still I feel her graceful figure resting against my surcharged heart\u2014still do sight, pulse, and breath falter at the recollection of that first kiss. Slowly and wordlessly we went to meet Adrian, whose steps we heard drawing near.\\n\\nI begged Adrian to come back after he had escorted his sister home. That same night, pacing the moonlit woodland paths, I poured my entire heart, its rapture and its promise, into my friend\u2019s keeping. For a moment he seemed troubled\u2014\u201cI might have foreseen this,\u201d he said; \u201cwhat contention must follow now!\u201d\"}"
