          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"208ed0946cc39f17f2cb8676\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Knights and their armored mounts never moved at any great clip. Once they pushed as best they could, with the ground firm now and free of snow or mire, they might manage a seven-mile pace. They\u2019d need to swap horses twice and would likely get in around six, a little after perhaps, but still with daylight enough to spot the white cloth I meant to tie around my right arm, the signal for me to take command. We\u2019d surround the prison and whisk the king out at once. It would look grand and dramatic enough, though I would have chosen noon for the extra theatrical effect.\\n\\nNext, to add more strings to my bow, I decided to hunt up some of the folk I had earlier recognized and reveal myself to them. That might get us out of this mess without needing the knights. Yet I had to be careful\u2014risky business. I had to appear splendidly dressed, and one can\u2019t just leap into finery. I\u2019d have to advance gradually, buying outfit after outfit from shops spaced apart, each one a bit finer than the last, until I reached silk and velvet and was ready. So I set out.\\n\\nBut the plan collapsed in a flash. At the first corner I ran smack into one of our slaves skulking with a watchman. I coughed just then, and he shot me a look that pierced to the bone; I\u2019m sure he thought he recognized the cough. I ducked into a shop at once, moved down the counter asking prices, and kept an eye sideways. The pair had stopped to talk, peering through the doorway. I resolved to slip out the back if there was one and told the shopwoman I needed to step out there to search for an escaped slave said to be hiding somewhere behind, explaining I was an officer in disguise, with my partner at the door holding one of the murderers. Would she kindly tell him not to wait, but to hurry to the far end of the back alley to catch the fellow when I flushed him out?\\n\\nFired with excitement at the chance to glimpse one of those already famous murderers, she rushed off straightaway.\"}"
