          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"52471d2897ede361f64d98bf\",\"rewritten_text\":\"From the steps where we had once embarked him, and ever afterward, I was on guard for any hint that we were suspected. I found none. We certainly had not been, and at that moment were not, watched or trailed by any boat. Had any craft hovered near us, I should have run for the shore, forcing her either to pass on or reveal her purpose. Yet we proceeded without the least sign of interference.\\n\\nHe wore his boat-cloak and seemed, as I\u2019ve remarked, naturally blended with the scene. It was striking (though the miserable life he had led might explain it) that he was the calmest of us all. He was no dullard, for he told me he wished to live to see his benefactor become one of the noblest gentlemen abroad; neither was he inclined to passivity or surrender, as I read him; but he had no intention of anticipating peril. When it arrived, he faced it, but it must arrive before he gave it thought.\\n\\n\u201cIf you knowed, dear boy,\u201d he said, \u201cwhat it is to sit alongside my dear boy with my pipe, after being day by day between four walls, you\u2019d envy me. But you don\u2019t know what it is.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI think I know the pleasure of liberty,\u201d I replied.\\n\\n\u201cAh,\u201d said he, shaking his head soberly. \u201cBut you don\u2019t know it the same as me. You\u2019d have to be under lock and key, dear boy, to know it the same as me,\u2014but I ain\u2019t a-going to be low.\u201d\\n\\nIt struck me as inconsistent that, driven by some dominant idea, he had risked his freedom and even his life. Yet I considered that perhaps freedom devoid of hazard stood too far from the habits of his existence to mean to him what it would to another man. I was near the truth, for after a short pause in his smoking he said:\u2014\\n\\n\u201cYou see, dear boy, when I was yonder, on t\u2019other side of the world, I kept always looking this way; and it grew dull to be there, though I was growing rich. Everybody knowed Magwitch, and Magwitch could come or go, and nobody\u2019s mind was put out about him. They aren\u2019t so easy concerning me here, dear boy,\u2014wouldn\u2019t be, at least, if they knew where I was.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIf all goes well,\u201d I said, \u201cyou will be entirely free and safe again within a few hours.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell,\u201d he answered, letting out a long breath, \u201cI hope so.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd think so?\u201d\"}"
        }
