          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"4e95b1fbbe4fd419008bf990\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cCertainly not,\u201d Duff replied.\\n\\n\u201cAnd just so the ladies are clear on the word \u2018yokel,\u2019 I take it you mean the culprit isn\u2019t a countryman?\u201d Mr. Losberne said with a smile.\\n\\n\u201cExactly, sir,\u201d Blathers replied. \u201cSo, this is about the robbery, then?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll of it,\u201d said the doctor.\\n\\n\u201cNow, what\u2019s this about the boy the servants keep talking about?\u201d Blathers asked.\\n\\n\u201cNothing at all,\u201d replied the doctor. \u201cOne panicked servant convinced himself the boy had something to do with the break-in, but it\u2019s nonsense\u2014pure absurdity.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cEasily dismissed, if that\u2019s the case,\u201d Duff remarked.\\n\\n\u201cHe\u2019s right,\u201d Blathers said, nodding and idly twirling the handcuffs as if they were castanets. \u201cWho is the boy? What\u2019s his story? Where did he come from? He didn\u2019t fall from the clouds, did he, sir?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOf course not,\u201d said the doctor, shooting a nervous glance at the two ladies. \u201cI know his whole history, but we can discuss that later. You\u2019d prefer to see where the thieves tried to get in first, I assume?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCertainly,\u201d said Mr. Blathers. \u201cWe should examine the scene first and question the servants afterward. That\u2019s the standard procedure.\u201d\\n\\nThey brought in lights, and Blathers and Duff, followed by the local constable, Brittles, Giles, and practically everyone else, went into the little room at the end of the hall and looked out the window. Then they went around across the lawn and looked in through the window. After that, someone handed them a candle to check the shutter, then a lantern to trace the footprints, and finally a pitchfork to prod the bushes. After all this, with everyone watching in breathless suspense, they returned inside, and Mr. Giles and Brittles reenacted their parts in the previous night\u2019s adventure with melodramatic flair\u2014some six times over\u2014contradicting each other in only one important detail at first, and in no more than a dozen by the final performance. Once that was done, Blathers and Duff cleared the room and held a lengthy conference that, for secrecy and solemnity, made the most intricate medical consultation look like child\u2019s play.\\n\\nMeanwhile, the doctor paced restlessly in the next room, and Mrs. Maylie and Rose watched with anxious faces.\\n\\n\u201cHonestly,\u201d he said, stopping after a series of brisk turns, \u201cI hardly know what to do.\u201d\"}"
