          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"4af92e207b226bcd373775b6\",\"rewritten_text\":\"This knot is one that only sailors usually know and is peculiar to the Maltese. I picked the ribbon up at the base of the lightning rod. It couldn\u2019t have belonged to either of the dead women. So, even if my deduction from this ribbon\u2014that the Frenchman was a sailor from a Maltese ship\u2014turns out wrong, there\u2019s no harm in what I wrote in the advertisement. If I\u2019m mistaken, he\u2019ll think I was misled by some detail he won\u2019t bother investigating. But if I\u2019m right, we gain a crucial advantage. Though he\u2019s innocent of the murder, the Frenchman will naturally hesitate about answering the advertisement\u2014about claiming the orangutan. He\u2019ll reason this way: \u2018I\u2019m innocent; I\u2019m poor; my orangutan is very valuable\u2014a fortune for someone in my position\u2014so why should I lose it because of unfounded fears? It\u2019s right here within my reach. It was found in the Bois de Boulogne, far from the scene of the killings. How could anyone suspect that a brute animal committed the crime? The police have no clue. Even if they track the creature, they can\u2019t prove I knew about the murder, or implicate me just because I knew something. Above all, I\u2019m identified. The advertiser names me as the owner of the animal. I can\u2019t know how much he really knows. If I fail to claim property so valuable, which people know is mine, I\u2019ll at least make the animal itself seem suspicious. It\u2019s not in my interest to draw attention to myself or the creature. I\u2019ll answer the advertisement, reclaim the orangutan, and keep it hidden until this blows over.\u2019\u201d At that moment we heard footsteps on the stairs. \u201cBe ready,\u201d Dupin said, \u201cwith your pistols, but don\u2019t show them or use them until I give the signal.\u201d We had left the front door open, and the visitor entered without ringing, coming several steps up the staircase. Now, though, he seemed to hesitate. We soon heard him going down again. Dupin moved quickly to the door just as we heard him returning. He didn\u2019t retreat a second time; instead he came up confidently and knocked on our door. \u201cCome in,\u201d Dupin said in a cheerful, hearty voice. A man entered. He was clearly a sailor\u2014a tall, broad-shouldered man with a muscular look and a certain reckless expression that wasn\u2019t entirely unappealing.\"}"
