          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"86882a14de5ed4d19ab9e90f\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Mr. Elliot looking up with so much respect.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAbsolutely delightful!\u201d cried Mrs. Clay, though she didn\u2019t dare turn her eyes toward Anne. \u201cExactly like a father and son! Dear Miss Elliot, may I call you father and son?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, I don\u2019t forbid anyone\u2019s words. If you insist on such notions! But honestly, I barely notice his attentions being any more than other men\u2019s.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Miss Elliot!\u201d exclaimed Mrs. Clay, raising her hands and eyes and letting the rest of her astonishment sink into a discreet silence.\\n\\n\u201cWell, my dear Penelope, you don\u2019t have to be so concerned about him. I did invite him, you know. I sent him away smiling. When I found he was really going to spend the whole day tomorrow with his friends at Thornberry Park, I took pity on him.\u201d\\n\\nAnne admired her friend\u2019s skill in showing such pleasure at the expectation and actual arrival of the very person whose presence must truly interfere with her primary goal. It was impossible that Mrs. Clay didn\u2019t hate the sight of Mr. Elliot; yet she could put on such a pleasant, calm face and seem perfectly satisfied with the shortened freedom of devoting only half as much attention to Sir Walter as she otherwise would.\\n\\nFor Anne, it was truly distressing to watch Mr. Elliot enter the room, and quite painful to have him approach and speak to her. She had already suspected he wasn\u2019t always sincere, but now she saw nothing but insincerity. His respectful attention to her father, so at odds with his earlier remarks, was revolting; and when she thought of his cruel behavior toward Mrs. Smith, she could hardly tolerate the sight of his current smiles and gentleness, or the sound of his artificial pleasantries.\\n\\nShe meant to avoid any change in manner that might provoke a protest from him. It was vitally important to her to escape any questioning or commotion; but she intended to be as decidedly cool toward him as their relationship allowed, and to quietly retrace the few steps of unnecessary intimacy she had been gradually led into. She was accordingly more guarded and more distant than she had been the night before.\\n\\nHe wanted to rekindle her curiosity about how and where he\u2019d once heard her praised; he wanted very much to enjoy more urging from her. But the spell was broken: he discovered that the heat and energy of a crowded room had been necessary to spark his modest cousin\u2019s vanity; or at least, he found it couldn\u2019t be done now, not with any of the efforts he dared make amid the stronger claims of the others.\"}"
