          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"84af30a895bc81bc574b69bb\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWell, that\u2019s how everyone does it, Huck.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTom, it doesn\u2019t matter. I ain\u2019t everyone, and I can\u2019t stand it. Being tied up like that is awful. And food comes too easy\u2014I don\u2019t care about eating when it\u2019s like that. I have to ask if I want to go fishing; I have to ask if I want to go swimming\u2014damn it if I don\u2019t have to ask to do everything. And I\u2019ve got to talk so polite it\u2019s no comfort\u2014I\u2019ve got to sneak up to the attic and swear a while every day just to get a taste in my mouth, or I\u2019d die, Tom. The widow wouldn\u2019t let me smoke; she wouldn\u2019t let me shout, she wouldn\u2019t let me yawn, or stretch, or scratch in front of folks\u2014\u201d He flared with a fresh burst of irritation and hurt. \u201cAnd blast it all, she prayed all the time! I never saw such a woman! I had to run, Tom\u2014I just had to. Besides, school\u2019s about to start, and I\u2019d have had to go\u2014well, I wouldn\u2019t stand that, Tom. Look here, Tom, being rich isn\u2019t what it\u2019s cracked up to be. It\u2019s nothing but worry and sweat and wishing you were dead all the time. These clothes suit me, and this barrel suits me, and I ain\u2019t ever giving them up. Tom, I wouldn\u2019t have landed in all this trouble if it hadn\u2019t been for that money; now you take my share along with yours, and give me a ten-cent piece once in a while\u2014not too often, because I don\u2019t care a lick for anything unless it\u2019s hard to get\u2014and go beg off with the widow for me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, Huck, you know I can\u2019t do that. It wouldn\u2019t be right; and besides, if you\u2019d try this a little longer, you\u2019d come to like it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLike it! Yeah\u2014the way I\u2019d like a hot stove if I sat on it long enough. No, Tom, I won\u2019t be rich, and I won\u2019t live in those cursed stuffy houses. I like the woods, and the river, and hogsheads, and I\u2019ll stick to them. Blame it! Just when we got guns, and a cave, and everything ready for robbing, this foolishness has to come up and ruin it!\u201d\\n\\nTom saw his chance.\\n\\n\u201cLook, Huck, being rich isn\u2019t going to stop me from turning robber.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo! Oh, good grief; are you dead serious, Tom?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cJust as serious as I\u2019m sitting here. But Huck, we can\u2019t let you join the gang if you ain\u2019t respectable, you know.\u201d\\n\\nHuck\u2019s joy was doused.\\n\\n\u201cCan\u2019t let me in, Tom?\u201d\"}"
