          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"753e657a8f62df1f072141f1\",\"rewritten_text\":\"One day while I was working on my studies with Mr. Pocket, a letter arrived by post, and just seeing the envelope set my heart racing; though I\u2019d never seen the handwriting addressing it, I knew whose hand it was. It had no formal opening like Dear Mr. Pip, Dear Pip, Dear Sir, or anything of the kind, but simply read:\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019m coming to London the day after tomorrow on the midday coach. I believe it was agreed you\u2019d meet me? In any case Miss Havisham believes so, and I\u2019m writing because she told me to. She sends her regards.\\n\\n\u201cYours, ESTELLA.\u201d\\n\\nIf I\u2019d had time, I probably would have ordered several new suits for the occasion; but since I didn\u2019t, I had to make do with what I already owned. My appetite vanished on the spot, and I couldn\u2019t find a moment\u2019s peace until the day came. That didn\u2019t make things any better; in fact, I was worse than ever, and I started haunting the coach office in Wood Street, Cheapside, long before the coach had even left the Blue Boar back home. Even though I knew this perfectly well, I still felt it would be unsafe to let the coach office out of my sight for more than five minutes at a time; and in this irrational state I had completed the first half-hour of a four or five-hour vigil when Wemmick bumped into me.\\n\\n\u201cHello, Mr. Pip,\u201d he said. \u201cHow are you? I wouldn\u2019t have thought this was your usual territory.\u201d\\n\\nI explained that I was waiting to meet someone arriving by coach, and I asked after the Castle and the Aged.\\n\\n\u201cBoth doing well, thank you,\u201d said Wemmick, \u201cespecially the Aged. He\u2019s in splendid spirits. He\u2019ll be eighty-two next birthday. I\u2019m thinking of firing eighty-two rounds, if the neighbors don\u2019t complain and that cannon of mine can handle the strain. Still, that\u2019s not London talk. Where do you think I\u2019m headed?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTo the office?\u201d I suggested, since he was headed that way.\\n\\n\u201cClose enough,\u201d Wemmick replied. \u201cI\u2019m going to Newgate. We have a banker\u2019s parcel case on right now, and I\u2019ve been down the road having a look at the scene of the crime, and now I need a word or two with our client.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDid your client commit the robbery?\u201d I asked.\\n\\n\u201cGood heavens, no,\u201d Wemmick replied very dryly. \u201cBut he\u2019s accused of it. So might you or I be. Either of us could be accused, you know.\u201d\"}"
        }
