          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"27d4fa2a84548bf8e1226a7d\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cNever!\u201d the girl answered.\\n\\n\u201cTell me why?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFor one reason,\u201d the girl said firmly, \u201cbecause the lady knows everything and will support me. I have her promise. And another reason is that, bad as his life has been, mine has been bad too. Many of us have followed the same path together, and I won\u2019t betray them. They could have betrayed me, but they didn\u2019t, even though they\u2019re bad.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen,\u201d said the gentleman quickly, as if this was what he had aimed for, \u201cturn Monks over to me and let me handle him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat if he betrays the others?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI promise you, if he is forced to tell the truth, that will be the end of it. There must be things in Oliver\u2019s small history that would be painful to make public, and once the truth is out, they will go free.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd if it isn\u2019t?\u201d the girl asked.\\n\\n\u201cThen,\u201d the gentleman continued, \u201cFagin will not be brought to justice without your consent. If that happens, I could show you reasons that would convince you.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDo I have the lady\u2019s promise on that?\u201d asked the girl.\\n\\n\u201cYou do,\u201d Rose replied. \u201cMy sincere and faithful pledge.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMonks would never learn how you found out what you know?\u201d the girl asked after a brief pause.\\n\\n\u201cNever,\u201d said the gentleman. \u201cThe information will be used against him in such a way that he could never guess.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have been a liar among liars since I was a child,\u201d the girl said after another pause. \u201cBut I\u2019ll trust your words.\u201d\\n\\nAfter both assured her it was safe, she described, in a voice so low the listener often struggled to catch the meaning, the public house where she had been followed that night, including its name and location. From her pauses, it seemed the gentleman was making quick notes. Once she had explained the layout, the best place to watch without being noticed, and the night and hour when Monks most often visited, she paused a moment, trying to picture his face more clearly.\\n\\n\u201cHe is tall,\u201d the girl said, \u201ca strong man but not heavy. He moves with a wary gait, always looking over his shoulder first to one side, then the other.\u201d\"}"
        }
