          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"730ae2abc8e1ffab6d24c597\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Besides sailors, almost no one can tie this knot, and it seems to be unique to the Maltese. I picked the ribbon up at the base of the lightning rod. It couldn\u2019t have belonged to either victim. Even if I am wrong in deducing from this ribbon that the Frenchman was a sailor serving on a Maltese ship, I did no harm by mentioning it in the advertisement. If I am mistaken, he\u2019ll just think I was misled by some detail and won\u2019t bother to look into it. But if I\u2019m right, we gain a great advantage. The Frenchman, although aware of the crime yet innocent of it, will naturally hesitate before replying to the advertisement or demanding the orangutan. He will think, \u201cI\u2019m innocent; I\u2019m poor; my orangutan is extremely valuable\u2014practically a fortune for me. Why should I lose it because of needless fears? It\u2019s here, within reach. It was found in the Bois de Boulogne, far from the scene of the slaughter. Who would ever suspect a mere animal of such a deed? The police are baffled\u2014they haven\u2019t found a single clue. Even if they track the animal, they can\u2019t prove I knew about the murder or involve me because of that knowledge. Above all, I am known. The advertiser identifies me as the beast\u2019s owner. I don\u2019t know how much he really knows. If I avoid claiming my valuable property, which people know I possess, I\u2019ll make the animal itself seem suspicious. It\u2019s not wise to draw attention to myself or to the creature. I\u2019ll answer the advertisement, recover the orangutan, and hide it until the fuss dies down.\u201d\\n\\nAt that moment we heard a step on the stairs.\\n\\n\u201cBe ready,\u201d said Dupin. \u201cHave your pistols, but don\u2019t use or show them until I give the signal.\u201d\\n\\nWe had left the front door open, and the visitor entered without ringing and came several steps up the staircase. He seemed to hesitate, and soon we heard him going down again. Dupin was heading quickly to the door when we heard the man climbing back up. This time he didn\u2019t retreat; he came up confidently and knocked on our chamber door.\\n\\n\u201cCome in,\u201d said Dupin, cheerful and hearty.\\n\\nA man entered. He was clearly a sailor\u2014a tall, strong, muscular fellow with a daredevil look that was not entirely unattractive.\"}"
