          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"1cb3b0ba17384a50cd746361\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Ever since we had taken him abroad at the stairs, I had watched carefully for any sign that we were suspected. I saw none. We certainly had not been suspected, and at that time we were certainly not being shadowed or followed by any boat. If a boat had waited on us, I would have steered toward shore and forced her to move on or reveal her intention. But we kept on without any sign of interference.\\n\\nHe wore his boat-cloak and looked, as I have said, like a natural part of the setting. It was striking\u2014though perhaps the miserable life he had led explained it\u2014that he was the least anxious of all of us. He was not indifferent, for he told me he hoped to live long enough to see his gentleman become one of the finest men in a foreign land. He was not inclined to be passive or resigned, as I understood it, but he had no idea of meeting danger halfway. When it reached him, he faced it, yet he would not trouble himself until it did.\\n\\n\u201cIf you knew, dear boy,\u201d he said to me, \u201cwhat it is to sit here with my dear boy and have my smoke after being day after day between four walls, you\u2019d envy me. But you don\u2019t know what it is.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI think I understand the joys of freedom,\u201d I replied.\\n\\n\u201cAh,\u201d he said, shaking his head gravely. \u201cBut you don\u2019t know it like I do. You\u2019d have to be under lock and key, dear boy, to know it like I do\u2014but I\u2019m not going to be low.\u201d\\n\\nIt struck me as inconsistent that for any overriding idea he would endanger his freedom and even his life. But I considered that perhaps freedom without danger was too far removed from all the habits of his existence to mean to him what it would to another man. I was not far wrong, for he said, after smoking a little:\\n\\n\u201cYou see, dear boy, when I was over yonder, on the other side of the world, I was always looking over here, and it turned dull being there, even though I was growing rich. Everybody knew Magwitch, and Magwitch could come and go, and nobody\u2019s mind would be troubled about him. They aren\u2019t so easy about me here, dear boy\u2014wouldn\u2019t be, at least, if they knew where I was.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIf all goes well,\u201d I said, \u201cyou will be perfectly free and safe again within a few hours.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell,\u201d he answered with a long breath, \u201cI hope so.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd do you believe so?\u201d\"}"
        }
      ],
