          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"03d361e63a972f5fe95fa144\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Suddenly Mr. Podgers let go of Lord Arthur\u2019s right hand and grabbed his left, bending so low to study it that the gold rims of his spectacles nearly touched the palm. For an instant his face turned mask-white with horror, but he quickly regained his composure, and, looking up at Lady Windermere with a forced smile, said, \u201cIt is the hand of a charming young man.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOf course it is!\u201d said Lady Windermere. \u201cBut will he be a charming husband? That is what I want to know.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll charming young men are,\u201d said Mr. Podgers.\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t think a husband should be too fascinating,\u201d Lady Jedburgh murmured pensively. \u201cIt is so dangerous.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear, they never are too fascinating,\u201d cried Lady Windermere. \u201cBut I want details. Details are the only things that interest me. What is going to happen to Lord Arthur?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, within the next few months Lord Arthur will take a voyage\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh yes, his honeymoon, of course!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd he will lose a relative.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot his sister, I hope?\u201d Lady Jedburgh said in a plaintive tone.\\n\\n\u201cCertainly not his sister,\u201d replied Mr. Podgers with a placating wave of his hand, \u201cjust a distant relative.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, I\u2019m horribly disappointed,\u201d said Lady Windermere. \u201cI have absolutely nothing to tell Sybil tomorrow. No one cares about distant relatives anymore. They went out of fashion years ago. Still, I suppose she had better keep a black silk dress handy; it always does for church, you know. And now let\u2019s go have supper. They have probably eaten everything by now, but we might find some hot soup. Fran\u00e7ois used to make excellent soup, but he is so upset about politics at the moment that I never feel quite sure of him. I do wish General Boulanger would calm down. Duchess, you must be tired?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot at all, dear Gladys,\u201d said the Duchess, waddling toward the door. \u201cI have enjoyed myself enormously, and the chiropodist\u2014I mean the palm reader\u2014is most interesting. Flora, where is my tortoiseshell fan? Oh, thank you, Sir Thomas, so much. And my lace shawl, Flora? Oh, thank you, Sir Thomas, very kind of you, I\u2019m sure.\u201d And the good creature finally managed to get downstairs without dropping her scent bottle more than twice.\\n\\nAll this time Lord Arthur Savile had been standing by the fireplace, feeling the same dreadful foreboding, the same sickening sense of coming disaster. He smiled sadly at his sister as she swept past on Lord Plymdale\u2019s arm, lovely in her pink brocade and pearls, and he barely heard Lady Windermere when she called for him to follow her. He thought of Sybil Merton, and the idea that anything could come between them brought tears to his eyes.\"}"
