          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"e464506121388c0496543a03\",\"rewritten_text\":\"He never tried again. The boys lay there counting the dragging minutes until it seemed time must be finished and eternity turning gray; then they were thankful to see the sun finally setting. \\n\\nOne snore stopped. Injun Joe sat up, looked around, gave a grim smile at his comrade whose head drooped on his knees, nudged him with his foot, and said: \\n\\n\\\"Hey! You\u2019re supposed to be on watch, aren\u2019t you! It\u2019s fine, though\u2014nothing happened.\\\" \\n\\n\\\"My! Was I asleep?\\\" \\n\\n\\\"Oh, partly. It\u2019s almost time for us to get going, pard. What\u2019ll we do with the little bit of loot we\u2019ve got left?\\\" \\n\\n\\\"I don\u2019t know\u2014leave it here like always, I guess. No point in hauling it off till we head south. Six hundred and fifty in silver is quite a load.\\\" \\n\\n\\\"Well, fine\u2014we can swing by here one more time.\\\" \\n\\n\\\"Sure\u2014but I\u2019d say come at night like we used to\u2014it\u2019s better.\\\" \\n\\n\\\"Yes, but listen; it might be a long time before I get the right shot at that job; things could go wrong; it\u2019s not in a very safe place. Let\u2019s just bury it for real\u2014and bury it deep.\\\" \\n\\n\\\"Good plan,\\\" said the comrade. He walked across the room, knelt, pried up a hearthstone near the back, and took out a bag that jingled sweetly. He pulled twenty or thirty dollars for himself, the same for Injun Joe, then handed the bag over. Joe was in the corner now, kneeling and digging with his bowie knife. \\n\\nThe boys forgot every fear and misery in a flash. With hungry eyes they watched each move. Luck!\u2014the glory of it was beyond imagination! Six hundred dollars could make half a dozen boys rich! This was treasure-hunting under the best possible stars\u2014no annoying guesswork about where to dig. They jabbed each other every moment\u2014meaningful nudges easy to read: \u201cOh, aren\u2019t you glad now that we\u2019re here!\u201d \\n\\nJoe\u2019s knife hit something. \\n\\n\\\"Hey!\\\" he said. \\n\\n\\\"What is it?\\\" asked his comrade. \\n\\n\\\"Half-rotten plank\u2014no, I think it\u2019s a box. Come give me a hand and we\u2019ll find out why it\u2019s here. Never mind, I\u2019ve busted a hole.\\\" \\n\\nHe reached in and pulled his hand back out\u2014 \\n\\n\\\"Man, it\u2019s money!\\\" \\n\\nThe two men studied the handful of coins. They were gold. The boys above were as excited and as thrilled as the men. \\n\\nJoe\u2019s comrade said, \\n\\n\\\"We\u2019ll finish fast. There\u2019s an old rusty pick over in the weeds on the other side of the fireplace\u2014I spotted it a minute ago.\\\"\"}"
