          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"871536fe366c1ac883e5cda1\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cDo you come back often?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI haven\u2019t been here since.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNor have I.\u201d\\n\\nThe moon started to rise, and I thought of that calm gaze at the white ceiling which was gone forever. The moon rose higher, and I remembered the pressure of his hand when I spoke the last words he ever heard.\\n\\nEstella was the next to break the silence between us.\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019ve often hoped and planned to come back, but I was kept away by so many circumstances. Poor, poor old place!\u201d\\n\\nThe first rays of moonlight touched the silvery mist, and they shone on the tears falling from her eyes. Not realizing I saw them, and trying to control herself, she said quietly,\\n\\n\u201cWere you wondering, as you walked along, how it came to be left like this?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, Estella.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThe land belongs to me. It\u2019s the only thing I haven\u2019t given up. Everything else has slipped away from me, little by little, but I kept this. It was the only thing I fought to keep through all those miserable years.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIs something going to be built here?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFinally, yes. I came to say goodbye before the change. And you,\u201d she said with a touching interest in a wanderer, \u201cyou still live abroad?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI do.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd you\u2019re doing well, I\u2019m sure?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI work hard enough for a modest living, and so\u2014yes, I\u2019m doing well.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019ve often thought of you,\u201d Estella said.\\n\\n\u201cHave you?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLately, very often. There was a long, painful time when I pushed away the memory of what I threw aside when I didn\u2019t know its worth. But once my duty no longer conflicted with remembering, I made room for it in my heart.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou\u2019ve always had your place in my heart,\u201d I replied.\\n\\nWe were silent again until she spoke.\\n\\n\u201cIt never occurred to me,\u201d Estella said, \u201cthat I\u2019d say goodbye to you while saying goodbye to this place. I\u2019m very glad to do both.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGlad to part again, Estella? Parting is painful for me. The memory of our last parting has always been sorrowful and painful.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut you said to me,\u201d Estella returned earnestly, \u201c\u2018God bless you, God forgive you!\u2019 If you could say that then, you won\u2019t hesitate to say it now\u2014now, when suffering has taught me more than anything else, and taught me to understand what your heart used to be. I\u2019ve been bent and broken, but\u2014I hope\u2014into a better shape.\u201d\"}"
