{"request_id":"37774153c06d10efcca02545","rewritten_text":"I had no fear on her account. She was what people call a capable woman, and could handle her own affairs without me. To tell the truth, she probably always saw me as an idle boy, a useless extra, fit only for daydreams, and was rather relieved to see me go. It was a dark night when I said goodbye to her, and, taking along the three creditors who had plagued me, we carried the balloon, with its car and gear, by a roundabout route to the station where the rest of my equipment was stored. There we found everything untouched, and I set to work at once.

“It was the first of April. The night, as I said, was dark; no stars were visible; and a drizzling rain, falling now and then, made us miserable. My main worry was the balloon, which, despite the varnish meant to protect it, was getting heavy with moisture; the powder was at risk too. I therefore kept my three duns hard at work, pounding down ice around the central cask and stirring the acid in the others. They never stopped pestering me with questions about what I meant to do with all this gear, and complained bitterly about the exhausting labor I forced on them. They said they could not see what good would come from being soaked to the skin just to take part in such awful rites. I grew uneasy and worked with all my strength, for I truly believe the fools thought I had made a pact with the devil, that what I was doing was no better than outright wickedness. I feared they would abandon me. I managed, however, to calm them with promises that I would settle every debt in full as soon as I finished the business at hand. They took these promises in their own way, no doubt thinking I would soon get plenty of ready cash, and that as long as I paid what I owed, plus a little extra for their help, they cared very little about what happened to my soul or my body.

“In about four and a half hours I found the balloon full enough. I fastened the car, loaded all my instruments into it, and did not forget the condensing apparatus, a generous supply of water, and plenty of provisions, including pemmican, which packs a lot of nutrition into little space."}"}

