          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"6ec7244d6ff5880277c03738\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cIt\u2019s just a tick.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhere\u2019d you pick him up?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOut in the woods.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019ll you take for him?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t know. I\u2019m not looking to sell.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFine. It\u2019s a pretty puny tick anyway.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, anybody can put down a tick that isn\u2019t theirs. I\u2019m happy with it. It\u2019s a good enough tick for me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSure, ticks are everywhere. I could have a thousand if I wanted.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen why don\u2019t you? Because you know you can\u2019t. This one\u2019s pretty early, I figure. It\u2019s the first I\u2019ve seen this year.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHey, Huck\u2014I\u2019ll trade you my tooth for it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLet\u2019s see it.\u201d\\n\\nTom pulled out a slip of paper and carefully unrolled it. Huckleberry eyed it wistfully. The urge was strong. Finally he said:\\n\\n\u201cIs it real?\u201d\\n\\nTom lifted his lip and showed the gap.\\n\\n\u201cAll right,\u201d said Huckleberry. \u201cIt\u2019s a deal.\u201d\\n\\nTom tucked the tick into the percussion-cap box that had recently been the pinchbug\u2019s cell, and the boys went their separate ways, each feeling richer.\\n\\nWhen Tom reached the little isolated frame schoolhouse, he walked in briskly, as if he had hurried there as fast as he could. He hung his hat on a peg and dropped into his seat with businesslike speed. The master, perched high in his big splint-bottom armchair, was dozing, lulled by the sleepy hum of study. The disturbance woke him.\\n\\n\u201cThomas Sawyer!\u201d\\n\\nTom knew his full name always meant trouble.\\n\\n\u201cSir!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCome up here. Now, sir, why are you late again, as usual?\u201d\\n\\nTom was about to take shelter in a lie when he saw two long braids of yellow hair hanging down a back he recognized through the electric spark of love. Beside that figure was the only empty seat on the girls\u2019 side of the room. Instantly he said:\\n\\n\u201cI stopped to talk with Huckleberry Finn!\u201d\\n\\nThe master\u2019s pulse stopped; he stared helplessly. The hum of study ceased. The pupils wondered if this reckless boy had lost his senses. The master said:\\n\\n\u201cYou\u2014you did what?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cStopped to talk with Huckleberry Finn.\u201d\\n\\nThere was no mistaking it.\\n\\n\u201cThomas Sawyer, this is the most astonishing admission I\u2019ve ever heard. A simple ruler won\u2019t do for this offense. Take off your jacket.\u201d\\n\\nThe master\u2019s arm swung until it was worn out and the supply of switches noticeably shrank. Then came the order:\\n\\n\u201cNow, sir, go sit with the girls! And let this be a lesson to you.\u201d\\n\\nThe ripple of giggles around the room seemed to embarrass the boy, but really it was caused more by his reverent awe of his unknown idol and the fearful pleasure in the good fortune that awaited him.\"}"
