          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"ca7c10e732e5dc1ae13d9f33\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cIf I can\u2019t live on that, I won\u2019t ask anyone to help me. Is that acceptable?\u201d\\n\\nA mighty roar of applause broke out, and through it rose the king\u2019s voice: \u201cLoose his bonds and set him free! Show him honor, high and low, rich and poor, for he has become the king\u2019s right hand, invested with power and authority, and his seat is on the highest step of the throne! Now drive away this creeping night and bring back light and cheer, that the whole world may bless you.\u201d\\n\\nBut I said, \u201cIt is nothing for a common man to be shamed before the world, but it would disgrace the king if anyone saw his minister naked without also seeing him freed from that shame. If I might ask for my clothes again\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThey are not suitable,\u201d the king interrupted. \u201cFetch garments of another kind; dress him like a prince!\u201d\\n\\nMy plan was working. I needed things to stay as they were until the eclipse became total. Otherwise they would keep begging me to end the darkness, and of course I couldn\u2019t do that. Sending for clothes bought me some time, but not enough. I had to find another excuse. I said it was natural for the king to rethink, to regret a little what he had done in excitement. So I would let the darkness deepen awhile, and if after a reasonable time the king still held the same decision, the darkness would be lifted. The king and everyone else disliked the idea, but I had to stand firm.\\n\\nIt grew darker and darker, blacker and blacker, while I wrestled with those clumsy sixth-century clothes. Soon it was pitch-dark, and the crowd groaned in dread as cold uncanny night breezes moved through the place and stars flickered into view. When the eclipse finally became total I was relieved, but everyone else was miserable, which made sense. I said, \u201cBy his silence the king still accepts the terms.\u201d Then I raised my hands, held them a moment, and said with the deepest solemnity, \u201cLet the enchantment dissolve and pass harmless away!\u201d\\n\\nFor a moment there was no answer in that thick dark and that graveyard hush. Then a silver edge of sun showed itself, and a moment later the assembly burst into a vast shout and surged toward me like a flood to overwhelm me with blessings and thanks; and Clarence was certainly among the last waves of that flood.\"}"
        }
