          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"dab4b59352614ec2b164ae55\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cIf you want one for home use, I can supply an excellent model, and I guarantee you\u2019ll be satisfied with the result. May I ask who it\u2019s meant for? If it\u2019s for the police, or anyone connected with Scotland Yard, I\u2019m afraid I can\u2019t help you. The English detectives are really our best allies, and I\u2019ve always found that by counting on their stupidity, we can do whatever we please. I couldn\u2019t part with a single one of them.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI assure you,\u201d said Lord Arthur, \u201cit has nothing to do with the police. In fact, the clock is meant for the Dean of Chichester.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy word! I had no idea you felt so strongly about religion, Lord Arthur. Few young men do nowadays.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019m afraid you give me too much credit, Herr Winckelkopf,\u201d said Lord Arthur, blushing. \u201cThe truth is, I really know nothing about theology.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSo it\u2019s purely a private matter?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cPurely private.\u201d\\n\\nHerr Winckelkopf shrugged and left the room, returning a few minutes later with a round cake of dynamite about the size of a penny, along with a charming little French clock topped by an ormolu figure of Liberty trampling the hydra of Despotism.\\n\\nLord Arthur\u2019s face lit up when he saw it. \u201cThat\u2019s exactly what I want,\u201d he exclaimed, \u201cand now tell me how it\u2019s triggered.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAh, that\u2019s my secret,\u201d replied Herr Winckelkopf, regarding his invention with understandable pride. \u201cLet me know when you want it to explode, and I\u2019ll set the mechanism to the exact moment.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, today is Tuesday, and if you could send it out at once\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s impossible; I have a great deal of important work underway for friends of mine in Moscow. Still, I might ship it tomorrow.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, that will be quite soon enough,\u201d said Lord Arthur politely. \u201cIf it\u2019s delivered tomorrow night or Thursday morning, that\u2019s fine. Time the explosion for Friday at noon exactly. The Dean is always at home then.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFriday, at noon,\u201d repeated Herr Winckelkopf, making a note of it in a large ledger lying on a bureau near the fireplace.\\n\\n\u201cAnd now,\u201d said Lord Arthur, rising, \u201cplease let me know how much I owe you.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s such a small matter, Lord Arthur, that I\u2019d rather not charge. The dynamite costs seven shillings and sixpence, the clock will be three pounds ten, and the shipping about five shillings. I\u2019m only too happy to oblige a friend of Count Rouvaloff\u2019s.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut what about your trouble, Herr Winckelkopf?\u201d\"}"
