          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"d88af1dd81262fe83858f511\",\"rewritten_text\":\"It was well past noon when he woke. His valet had tiptoed in several times to see if he was moving and wondered why his young master slept so late. At last the bell rang, and Victor glided in with a cup of tea and a stack of letters on a small tray of old S\u00e8vres china, then pulled back the olive satin curtains with their shimmering blue lining that covered the three tall windows.\\n\\n\u201cMonsieur has slept well this morning,\u201d he said with a smile.\\n\\n\u201cWhat time is it, Victor?\u201d asked Dorian Gray drowsily.\\n\\n\u201cOne fifteen, Monsieur.\u201d\\n\\nHow late it was! He sat up, sipped some tea, and sorted through his letters. One had come by hand that morning from Lord Henry. He hesitated, then set it aside. The others he opened without interest. They held the usual mix of cards, dinner invitations, tickets for private views, programmes of charity concerts, and similar things that fashionable young men receive every morning during the season. There was a heavy bill for a chased silver Louis Quinze toilet set he still hadn\u2019t dared send to his guardians, who were very old-fashioned and did not see that we live in an age where unnecessary things are our only needs; and there were several politely worded offers from Jermyn Street moneylenders willing to lend any amount at a moment\u2019s notice at very reasonable interest.\\n\\nAfter about ten minutes he rose, threw on an elaborate dressing gown of silk-embroidered cashmere, and went into the onyx-paved bathroom. The cool water revived him after his long sleep. He seemed to have forgotten everything he had gone through. Now and then a faint sense of taking part in some odd tragedy returned, but it felt as unreal as a dream.\\n\\nOnce dressed, he went to the library and sat down to a light French breakfast set out for him on a small round table beside the open window. The day was exquisite. The warm air felt heavy with spice. A bee flew in and circled the blue-dragon bowl filled with sulphur-yellow roses in front of him. He felt completely happy.\\n\\nSuddenly his eyes fell on the screen he had placed in front of the portrait, and he started.\\n\\n\u201cToo cold for Monsieur?\u201d asked his valet, setting an omelette on the table. \u201cShall I close the window?\u201d\\n\\nDorian shook his head. \u201cI\u2019m not cold,\u201d he murmured.\"}"
