          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"70bf128b684edbd6f000fc24\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cSo now I\u2019m the owner of a few knights,\u201d I said as we rode off. \u201cWho would ever have thought I\u2019d end up listing assets like that? I won\u2019t know what to do with them unless I raffle them off. How many are there, Sandy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSeven, if it please you, sir, and their squires.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s a good haul. Who are they? Where do they hang out?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhere do they hang out?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, where do they live?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAh, I didn\u2019t understand you. I\u2019ll tell you soon.\u201d Then she mused softly, turning the words over her tongue with care: \u201cHang they out\u2014hang they out\u2014where hang\u2014where do they hang out; yes, just so; where do they hang out. Truly the phrase has a fine and charming grace, and is prettily worded besides. I\u2019ll repeat it again and again in my idle hours, so I may perhaps learn it. Where do they hang out. Indeed! Already it falls lightly from my tongue, and since\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t forget the cowboys, Sandy.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCowboys?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, the knights, you know. You were going to tell me about them. A while back, remember? Figuratively speaking, the game\u2019s started.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGame\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, yes, yes! Step up to the plate. I mean get to work on your statistics, and don\u2019t waste so much tinder getting your fire going. Tell me about the knights.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI will gladly, and I\u2019ll begin without delay. So the two of them departed and rode into a great forest. And\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGood grief!\u201d\\n\\nYou see, I realized my mistake right away. I\u2019d set her machinery in motion; it was my fault; she\u2019d take thirty days to get down to the actual facts. She usually began without an introduction and finished without a point. If you interrupted she either kept going as if nothing had happened or answered with a couple of words, then went back and repeated the sentence. So interruptions only made things worse; yet I had to interrupt, and pretty often, to save my own life\u2014a person would die if he let her monotony drip on him all day.\\n\\n\u201cGood grief!\u201d I cried in my distress. She went right back and started over:\\n\\n\u201cSo the two of them departed and rode into a great forest. And\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhich two?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSir Gawaine and Sir Uwaine. And so they came to an abbey of monks, where they were well lodged. In the morning they heard mass in the abbey, and then they rode on until they came to a great forest; then Sir Gawaine saw in a valley near a turret twelve lovely damsels and two knights in armor on great horses, and the damsels went back and forth by a tree.\u201d\"}"
