          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"50db7b444dc8a1c4c11fdb6f\",\"rewritten_text\":\"He never tried again. The boys lay there, counting the dragging seconds until it felt as if time itself had ended and eternity was turning gray; then, at last, they felt relief to see the sun begin to sink. One snore stopped. Injun Joe sat upright, looked around, gave a grim smile at his comrade, whose head sagged onto his knees, prodded him with his foot, and said: \u201cHey! You\u2019re the watchman, aren\u2019t you! All right, though\u2014nothing\u2019s happened.\u201d \u201cMy! Have I been sleeping?\u201d \u201cOnly partly. Near time for us to be moving, pard. What\u2019ll we do with what little plunder we\u2019ve still got?\u201d \u201cI don\u2019t know\u2014leave it here as usual, I suppose. No reason to haul it off until we head south. Six hundred and fifty in silver\u2019s heavy to lug.\u201d \u201cWell\u2014all right\u2014it ain\u2019t any trouble to come once more.\u201d \u201cNo\u2014but I\u2019d rather come at night the way we used to\u2014it\u2019s safer.\u201d \u201cYes; but listen, it might be a while before I get the right chance for that job; accidents could happen; it\u2019s not in such a safe spot; we\u2019ll just bury it properly\u2014and bury it deep.\u201d \u201cGood notion,\u201d said the comrade. He crossed the room, knelt, lifted one of the back hearth-stones, and fetched out a bag that clinked pleasantly. He took off twenty or thirty dollars for himself and the same for Injun Joe, and handed the bag over. Joe was kneeling in the corner, digging with his bowie-knife. Instantly, the boys forgot every fear and misery. With greedy eyes they tracked every motion. Fortune!\u2014its splendor was beyond imagining! Six hundred dollars could make half a dozen boys rich! Here was treasure-hunting under the best auspices\u2014there\u2019d be no vexing uncertainty about where to dig. They nudged each other at every turn\u2014eloquent prods easily read, saying simply\u2014\u201cOh, aren\u2019t you glad now that we\u2019re here!\u201d Joe\u2019s knife struck something. \u201cHey!\u201d he said. \u201cWhat is it?\u201d asked his comrade. \u201cHalf-rotten plank\u2014no, I think it\u2019s a box. Here\u2014lend a hand and we\u2019ll find out what it\u2019s doing here. No need, I\u2019ve broken a hole.\u201d He reached in and pulled his hand back out\u2014 \u201cMan, it\u2019s money!\u201d The two examined the handful of coins. They were gold. The boys above were as thrilled and delighted as the men. Joe\u2019s comrade said: \u201cWe\u2019ll make short work of this. There\u2019s a rusty old pick among the weeds in the corner on the far side of the fireplace\u2014I spotted it a minute ago.\u201d\"}"
