          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"da9e48b5d56db2ebf218a36e\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Even so, the boy kept growing paler, more downcast, and more depressed. She tried hot baths, sitz baths, showers, and plunges. He stayed as solemn as a hearse. She added a thin oatmeal diet and blister plasters to back up the water treatment. She gauged his capacity like a jug and filled him every day with patent remedies.\\n\\nBy now Tom hardly noticed persecution. This stage terrified the old lady. That indifference had to be shattered no matter what. Then she heard about Pain-killer for the first time. She ordered a large supply right away. She tasted it and felt profound gratitude. It was pure fire in liquid form. She gave up the water cures and everything else and put her faith entirely in Pain-killer. She gave Tom a teaspoonful and waited anxiously. Her worries vanished instantly; her heart was calm again, because the \u201cindifference\u201d was gone. The boy couldn\u2019t have shown more wild, eager interest if she\u2019d lit a fire under him.\\n\\nTom decided it was time to snap out of it; this lifestyle might suit his tragic mood, but it was losing romance and gaining too much chaotic variety. He weighed several escape plans and settled on pretending to adore Pain-killer. He asked for it so often he became a pest, and his aunt finally told him to help himself and stop bothering her. If it had been Sid, she would have enjoyed it without a second thought; but since it was Tom, she kept secret watch on the bottle. She noticed the medicine really was disappearing, yet it never occurred to her that Tom was treating a crack in the sitting-room floor with it.\\n\\nOne day, as Tom was dosing the crack, his aunt\u2019s yellow cat wandered up, purring, eyeing the teaspoon greedily, begging for a taste. Tom said:\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t ask for it unless you mean it, Peter.\u201d\\n\\nBut Peter insisted he wanted it.\\n\\n\u201cYou\u2019d better be sure.\u201d\\n\\nPeter was sure.\\n\\n\u201cYou\u2019ve asked for it, so I\u2019ll give it to you, because I\u2019m not mean; but if you dislike it, you can\u2019t blame anyone but yourself.\u201d\\n\\nPeter agreed. Tom pried the cat\u2019s mouth open and poured in the Pain-killer. Peter shot two yards into the air, then let out a war whoop and tore around the room, slamming into furniture, toppling flowerpots, and creating general havoc.\"}"
