          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"0041859c7570ed4d03ab834a\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cI suppose I may ask you two questions?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou can ask,\u201d said Monks, with a hint of surprise. \u201cWhether I answer is another matter.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat makes three questions,\u201d remarked Mr. Bumble, trying to be witty.\\n\\n\u201cIs that what you expected to get from me?\u201d the matron demanded.\\n\\n\u201cIt is,\u201d said Monks. \u201cAnd the other question?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you plan to do with it? Could it be used against me?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNever,\u201d Monks responded, \u201cnor against me either. Look at this\u2014but don\u2019t step closer, or your life won\u2019t be worth a rush.\u201d\\n\\nHe suddenly shoved the table aside and, pulling an iron ring in the floorboards, threw back a large trapdoor right by Mr. Bumble\u2019s feet. The shock sent Bumble stumbling several steps back.\\n\\n\u201cLook down,\u201d said Monks, lowering the lantern into the darkness. \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid of me. I could have dropped you quietly enough while you sat over it, if that had been my plan.\u201d\\n\\nEncouraged, the matron moved to the edge; even Mr. Bumble, driven by curiosity, crept closer. The muddy water, swollen by heavy rain, rushed below. The roar of its splashing and swirling against the slimy green piles drowned every other sound. There had once been a mill underneath; the tide, foaming and chafing around the few rotting posts and scraps of machinery still left, seemed to leap forward with new force once free of the useless obstacles that had tried to block it.\\n\\n\u201cIf you threw a man\u2019s body down there, where would it be by morning?\u201d asked Monks, swinging the lantern over the dark shaft.\\n\\n\u201cTwelve miles downriver, and chopped to bits as well,\u201d Bumble answered, recoiling.\\n\\nMonks pulled the small packet from his breast, where he had hastily hidden it. He tied it to a lead weight from an old pulley lying on the floor, then dropped it into the stream. It fell straight and true, slipping into the water with barely a splash, and vanished.\\n\\nThe three of them looked at one another and seemed to breathe easier.\\n\\n\u201cThere,\u201d Monks said, closing the trapdoor, which thudded back into place. \u201cIf the sea ever gives up the dead, like the books say, it will keep its gold and silver and that rubbish with it. We\u2019re finished talking and can end this pleasant gathering.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBy all means,\u201d Mr. Bumble replied eagerly.\\n\\n\u201cYou\u2019ll keep your mouth shut, won\u2019t you?\u201d Monks said, with a threatening glare.\"}"
