          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"e9b2df15ea1f328a137a522b\",\"rewritten_text\":\"But no, there was something flashier than even that. He would be a pirate! That was it! Now his future stretched before him, blazing with unimaginable splendor. His name would echo around the world and make people shudder. He pictured himself tearing across the dancing seas in his sleek, low, black-hulled racer, the Spirit of the Storm, with his grisly flag flying at the fore. At the height of his fame, he would stride into the old village church, sunburned and weather-beaten, dressed in a black velvet doublet and trunks, great jackboots, a crimson sash, a belt bristling with horse pistols, a crime-stained cutlass at his side, a slouch hat with trailing plumes, his black flag unfurled, skull and crossbones displayed, while the whispers rose in awed delight: \u201cIt\u2019s Tom Sawyer the Pirate\u2014The Black Avenger of the Spanish Main!\u201d\\n\\nYes, it was settled; his path was chosen. He would run away from home and set out. He would leave the very next morning. So he had to start preparing. He gathered his resources. He went to a rotting log nearby and began digging under one end with his Barlow knife. Soon he hit wood that sounded hollow. He slid his hand in and recited this incantation with solemn emphasis:\\n\\n\u201cWhat hasn\u2019t come here, come! What\u2019s here, stay here!\u201d\\n\\nThen he scraped away the dirt and uncovered a pine shingle. Lifting it revealed a neat little cache with sides and bottom of shingles. Inside lay a marble. Tom\u2019s astonishment was boundless. He scratched his head in perplexity and said, \u201cWell, that beats anything!\u201d Then he flung the marble away in irritation and stood thinking. The truth was, a superstition he and all his friends considered infallible had failed. If you buried a marble with the required spell, left it alone for two weeks, and then reopened the spot with the incantation he had just used, every marble you had ever lost would have gathered there, no matter how widely scattered. But this time, it had clearly failed. Tom\u2019s whole structure of faith was shaken. He had heard of it succeeding many times and never of it failing. It never occurred to him that he himself had tried it several times but could never relocate the hiding places afterward. He pondered the mystery for a while and finally concluded that some witch had interfered and broken the charm.\"}"
