          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"503dbb232b55c544d6fc6f5d\",\"rewritten_text\":\"After I sent in the petitions, I could not keep away from the places where they were. I felt they were more hopeful and less desperate when I was near. In that restless, aching state of mind, I walked the streets every evening, passing the offices and houses where I had left the petitions. To this day, the tired western streets of London on a cold, dusty spring night\u2014with their rows of stern, shut-up mansions and their endless lamps\u2014remain bleak to me because of it.\\n\\nI could not visit him as often now, and he was kept under tighter watch. Thinking they suspected me of trying to carry poison to him, I asked to be searched before sitting down at his bedside. I told the officer there that I would do anything to prove my intentions were pure. No one was cruel to him or to me. There was duty to do, and it was done without roughness. The officer always told me he was worse, and other sick prisoners in the room, along with prisoners acting as nurses\u2014criminals, yet capable of kindness, thank God\u2014always said the same.\\n\\nAs the days passed, I saw more often that he lay quietly looking at the white ceiling, his face empty of light until one of my words flashed across it for a moment before fading again. Sometimes he could hardly speak or not at all. Then he answered with slight pressures of his hand, and I learned to understand him.\\n\\nOn the tenth day, I saw a greater change than before. His eyes turned toward the door, brightening as I entered.\\n\\n\u201cDear boy,\u201d he said when I sat by his bed, \u201cI thought you were late. But I knew you couldn\u2019t be.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s exactly the time,\u201d I said. \u201cI waited for it at the gate.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou always wait at the gate, don\u2019t you, dear boy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes. I don\u2019t want to lose a moment.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThank you, dear boy, thank you. God bless you! You\u2019ve never deserted me, dear boy.\u201d\\n\\nI pressed his hand in silence, remembering how I had once meant to desert him.\\n\\n\u201cAnd best of all,\u201d he said, \u201cyou\u2019ve been more comfortable with me since I fell under a dark cloud than when the sun shone.\u201d\"}"
        }
      ],
