          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"b8e428fa4fcc23c4b7e31f0b\",\"rewritten_text\":\"There was something so unusual in the way Mr. Wopsle\u2019s eyes kept widening, as if he were turning over a hundred thoughts and getting more confused by the minute, that I could not make sense of it. Even after he\u2019d floated up to the rafters in a giant watch case, I sat there thinking about it and still couldn\u2019t figure it out. An hour later, when I left the theatre, I was still puzzling over it when I found him waiting for me near the door.\\n\\n\u201cHow are you?\u201d I said, shaking his hand as we walked down the street together. \u201cI saw you had seen me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSaw you, Mr. Pip!\u201d he replied. \u201cOf course I saw you. But who else was there?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWho else?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s the strangest thing,\u201d Mr. Wopsle said, drifting back into that faraway stare, \u201cand yet I could swear to him.\u201d\\n\\nAlarmed, I begged him to explain.\\n\\n\u201cWhether I would have noticed him at first if you hadn\u2019t been there,\u201d Mr. Wopsle went on in that same absent way, \u201cI can\u2019t say for sure; still, I think I would have.\u201d\\n\\nWithout meaning to, I glanced around, like I had gotten used to doing when heading home, because his mysterious words sent a shiver through me.\\n\\n\u201cOh! He can\u2019t be in sight,\u201d said Mr. Wopsle. \u201cHe left before I came off the stage. I saw him go.\u201d\\n\\nBecause I had reason to be suspicious, I even suspected this poor actor. I distrusted it as some plan to trap me into admitting something. So I studied him as we walked, but kept quiet.\\n\\n\u201cI had this ridiculous notion that he must be with you, Mr. Pip, until I saw you had no idea he was there, sitting behind you like a ghost.\u201d\\n\\nThe chill returned, but I was determined not to speak yet, because everything he said could be part of an attempt to make me link his hints to Provis. Of course I was absolutely sure Provis hadn\u2019t been there.\\n\\n\u201cI suppose you think I\u2019m acting strangely, Mr. Pip; I can see you do. But it\u2019s so very strange! You\u2019ll hardly believe what I\u2019m about to tell you. I could barely believe it myself if you were the one telling me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cReally?\u201d I said.\\n\\n\u201cIndeed. Mr. Pip, do you remember the Christmas Day when you were a little child, and I dined at the Gargerys\u2019, and some soldiers came to the door to get a pair of handcuffs fixed?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI remember it perfectly.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd you remember there was a chase after two convicts, and we took part, and Gargery carried you on his back, while I led the way and you kept up as best you could?\u201d\"}"
