          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"b848201b4770a4fa91fc4e59\",\"rewritten_text\":\"These reflections soothed me enough that by afternoon I fell into a deep slumber, though the fever burning in my veins denied me tranquil dreams. The ghastly scene of the preceding day continued to play relentlessly before my eyes; the women fleeing, and Felix, raging, wrenching me from his father\u2019s feet. I woke drained, and realizing night had already fallen, I slipped out of my hiding-place to search for food.\\n\\nWhen my need was satisfied, I turned onto the familiar path that led to the cottage. Everything there seemed peaceful. I crawled into my hovel and waited silently for the hour when the household typically arose. That time came and went, the sun climbed higher, yet the cottagers did not appear. A tremor seized me, fearing some terrible calamity. The cottage interior remained dark, and no sound met my ear; I cannot convey the torment of that suspense.\\n\\nSoon two peasants went by, and stopping near the cottage, began discussing something with emphatic gestures; however, I could not comprehend their words, for they spoke the village dialect unlike that of my protectors. Shortly afterward Felix came with another man; I was astonished, as I knew he had not left the cottage that morning, and I waited anxiously to learn from their speech the cause of these strange proceedings.\\n\\n\u201c\u2018Have you considered,\u2019 said his companion, \u2018that you will have to pay three months\u2019 rent and forfeit the produce of your garden? I wish to take no undue advantage, so I beg you to take a few days to settle your decision.\u2019\\n\\n\u201c\u2018It avails nothing,\u2019 Felix answered; \u2018we can never again dwell in your cottage. My father\u2019s life is in extreme peril because of the dreadful event I have described. My wife and sister will never shake off their terror. I implore you, do not argue further. Reclaim your dwelling and let me escape this place.\u2019\\n\\nFelix shook violently while speaking. He and the man went into the cottage, stayed only a few minutes, then departed. I beheld no member of the De Lacey family again.\\n\\nFor the rest of the day I lingered in my hovel, sunk in absolute, senseless despair. My protectors had gone, severing the single thread that tied me to the world. For the first time my heart filled with vengeance and hatred. I made no attempt to repress them; instead, letting myself be carried away by their current, I turned my thoughts toward harm and death.\"}"
