          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"de52c3cb66a33efbf47ad96c\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The oaks around us housed a tribe of nightingales\u2014there I am now; Idris, in the prime of her youth, stands beside me\u2014remember, I am just twenty-two, and the beloved of my heart has barely seen seventeen summers. The river, swollen by autumn rains, flooded the lowlands, and Adrian, in his favorite boat, was occupied with the dangerous sport of snapping off the highest branch of a submerged oak. Are you so tired of life, Adrian, that you toy with danger like this?\\n\\nHe had taken his prize and was steering his boat through the torrent; we stared at him anxiously, but the current carried him away from us. He was forced to land far downstream and take a long detour before he could rejoin us. \u201cHe is safe!\u201d said Idris when he sprang ashore and waved the bough over his head in triumph. \u201cWe will wait here for him.\u201d\\n\\nWe were alone together; the sun had set; the nightingales began their song; the evening star shone clear in the lingering light of the west. My angelic girl\u2019s blue eyes were fixed on this lovely emblem of herself: \u201cHow the light pulses,\u201d she said, \u201cwhich is the life of that star. Its wavering brilliance seems to tell that its state, like ours on earth, is unsteady and uncertain; it fears, I think, and it loves.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDo not gaze at the star, dear, generous friend,\u201d I cried. \u201cDo not read love in its trembling rays; do not study distant worlds; do not speak of the fancied image of a sentiment. I have been silent so long; so long, even to illness, I have yearned to speak to you and surrender my soul, my life, my whole being to you. Do not look at the star, dear love\u2014or do, and let that eternal spark plead for me; let it be my witness and advocate, shining silently\u2014love is to me what light is to the star; as long as it remains untouched by annihilation, so long will I love you.\u201d\\n\\nThe ecstasy of that moment must remain forever hidden from the world\u2019s callous gaze. I still feel her graceful form pressed against my overflowing heart\u2014still do sight, pulse, and breath falter at the memory of that first kiss. Slowly and quietly we went to meet Adrian, whose approach we heard.\\n\\nI begged Adrian to return to me after he had taken his sister home. And that same evening, walking along the moonlit forest paths, I poured out my whole heart\u2014its delight and its hope\u2014to my friend. For a moment he looked troubled. \u201cI might have foreseen this,\u201d he said. \u201cWhat conflict will now unfold!\u201d\"}"
