          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"044f4a61afebe78862c25ee2\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cNothing but a tick.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhere\u2019d you find him?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOut in the woods.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019ll you take for him?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t know. I\u2019m not aiming to sell him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll right. It\u2019s a mighty small tick, anyhow.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, anybody can run down a tick that isn\u2019t theirs. I\u2019m pleased with this one. It suits me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSho, ticks are thick as fleas. I could have a thousand if I wanted.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, why don\u2019t you? Because you know you can\u2019t. This must be an early tick. It\u2019s the first I\u2019ve seen this year.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSay, Huck\u2014I\u2019ll swap you my tooth for him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLet\u2019s see it.\u201d\\n\\nTom pulled out a slip of paper and carefully unwrapped it. Huckleberry gazed with longing. The urge was mighty. At last he murmured:\\n\\n\u201cIs it genuine?\u201d\\n\\nTom lifted his lip to show the gap.\\n\\n\u201cWell, all right,\u201d Huckleberry said, \u201cyou\u2019ve got a bargain.\u201d\\n\\nTom tucked the tick into the percussion-cap box that lately held the pinchbug, and the boys parted, each feeling richer than before.\\n\\nWhen Tom arrived at the little solitary frame schoolhouse, he strode in briskly, as though he had made all haste. He hung up his hat and dropped into his seat with businesslike dispatch. The master, enthroned in his grand splint-bottomed arm-chair, was napping, soothed by the sleepy drone of lessons. The interruption roused him.\\n\\n\u201cThomas Sawyer!\u201d\\n\\nTom knew his full name meant mischief.\\n\\n\u201cSir!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCome here. Now, sir, why are you late again, same as always?\u201d\\n\\nTom was about to retreat into a falsehood when he spotted two long tails of yellow hair down the back he knew by love\u2019s electrical sympathy; and beside that form lay the only empty seat among the girls. He instantly declared:\\n\\n\u201cI stopped to talk with Huckleberry Finn!\u201d\\n\\nThe master\u2019s pulse seemed to halt, and he stared in helpless astonishment. The study-drone ceased. The scholars wondered if this reckless boy had gone mad. The master demanded:\\n\\n\u201cYou\u2014you did what?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cStopped to talk with Huckleberry Finn.\u201d\\n\\nNo mistaking it.\\n\\n\u201cThomas Sawyer, that is the most amazing admission I ever heard. No simple ferule suits such an offense. Take off your jacket.\u201d\\n\\nThe master\u2019s arm worked until it was weary and the pile of switches notably reduced. Then came the command:\\n\\n\u201cNow, sir, go sit with the girls! And let this teach you.\u201d\\n\\nThe titter running round the room seemed to shame the boy, yet his blush sprang more from reverent awe of his unknown idol and the fearful delight in such grand good luck.\"}"
