{"request_id":"0d6754a46d28b42cea803e0e","rewritten_text":"The next day he stayed inside and spent most of it in his room, sick with a fierce terror of dying yet feeling no care for life. The sense of being hunted and trapped ruled him. If the tapestry stirred in the wind, he trembled. The dead leaves blowing against the leaded windows felt like his own wasted promises and frantic regrets. When he closed his eyes, he saw the sailor’s face again through the stained glass, and horror clutched his heart once more.

Still, perhaps it was only his mind that had summoned vengeance from the night and set those dreadful shapes of punishment before him. Life was chaotic, yet the imagination held a terrible logic. It was the imagination that made remorse chase sin. It was the imagination that forced each crime to bear its misshapen offspring. In the real world, the wicked went free and the good went unrewarded. The strong won success, and failure was pushed on the weak. That was all. Besides, if a stranger had been sneaking around the house, the servants or keepers would have noticed. If footprints had marked the flower beds, the gardeners would have reported it. Yes, it had been only an illusion. Sibyl Vane’s brother had not returned to kill him. He had sailed away to drown in some winter sea. At least from him he was safe. The man did not know who he was and could never know. The mask of youth had protected him.

Yet if it was only a hallucination, how dreadful it was that conscience could summon such frightful ghosts, give them form, and set them moving before someone! What life would he have if day and night shadows of his crime stared at him from silent corners, mocked him from hidden places, whispered in his ear at feasts, and woke him with icy fingers in his sleep? As the thought seeped through his mind, he turned pale with fear, and the air felt suddenly colder. In what wild moment of madness had he killed his friend! How ghastly even the memory of it! He saw it once more. Each awful detail returned with new terror. From the black cave of time, terrible and draped in scarlet, rose the image of his sin."}

