          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"e18dc8557b51220cadf63b3b\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cThis must have been that very period of Mr Elliot\u2019s life,\u201d observed Anne, \u201cwhich has always stirred my particular curiosity. It must coincide with when he first became acquainted with my father and sister. I never met him myself; I only heard of him. Yet there was something in his behavior then, regarding my father and sister, and later in the circumstances of his marriage, that I never could reconcile with the man we see now. It hinted at a different character.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI know the whole history, I know the whole history,\u201d exclaimed Mrs Smith. \u201cHe had been introduced to Sir Walter and your sister before I knew him, yet he talked of them endlessly. I know he received invitations and encouragement, and I know he refused to go. I can probably satisfy you on matters you would hardly expect; and as for his marriage, I was in full possession of the facts at the time. I knew all the pros and cons; I was the confidante to whom he revealed his hopes and schemes; and though I had not previously known his wife\u2014her inferior rank, indeed, made that impossible\u2014I knew her through all the rest of her life, or at least up to two years before her death, and can answer whatever you wish to ask.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo,\u201d replied Anne, \u201cI have no particular question about her. I have always understood they were not a happy couple. But I should like to learn why, at that stage of his life, he would slight my father\u2019s acquaintance as he did. My father was certainly inclined to treat him with great and proper attention. Why did Mr Elliot withdraw?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMr Elliot,\u201d said Mrs Smith, \u201cat that period of his life, had a single aim: to make his fortune, and by a somewhat quicker route than the law would allow. He resolved to secure it through marriage. He was determined, at least, not to ruin it through an unwise marriage; and I know he believed (whether rightly or wrongly I cannot say) that your father and sister, in their politeness and invitations, were plotting a match between the heir and the young lady, and such a match could never have fulfilled his notions of wealth and independence. That was the motive behind his withdrawal, I assure you. He told me everything. He never hid anything from me. It was odd, that having left you behind in Bath, the first and closest acquaintance I formed after marrying should be your cousin; and that, through him, I should be constantly hearing of your father and sister.\u201d\"}"
        }
      ],
