          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"2c2b71a4605721abcf138657\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cOne word more, Rose. Beloved Rose! just one more!\u201d Harry burst out, placing himself before her. \u201cHad I been less\u2014less fortunate, as the world phrases it\u2014had some quiet, hidden life been my lot\u2014had I been poor, ailing, helpless\u2014would you have turned away then? Or has this hesitation sprung up only because I seem destined for wealth and distinction?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDo not force me to answer,\u201d Rose replied. \u201cThat situation never has existed and never will. It is unfair\u2014almost unkind\u2014to insist upon it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIf your reply is what I scarcely dare to hope,\u201d Harry went on, \u201cit will throw a ray of joy across my solitary path, and guide me onward. It is no small thing to do this by uttering a few short words to one who loves you beyond all else. Oh, Rose: in the name of my fervent, unfaltering devotion; in remembrance of all I have suffered for you, and all you condemn me yet to suffer; answer me this single question!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen, had your fate been otherwise shaped,\u201d Rose returned; \u201chad you been even slightly, yet not so widely, above me; if I could have aided and cheered you in some modest, peaceful retreat, and not been a stain and hindrance amid ambitious, distinguished circles; I should have been spared this ordeal. I have every reason to be happy, very happy, now; but then, Harry, I admit I should have been happier.\u201d\\n\\nWhile she confessed it, busy memories of childhood\u2019s hopes, treasured long ago, thronged Rose\u2019s mind; but they came with tears, as old hopes do when they return blighted, and those tears brought relief.\\n\\n\u201cThis weakness is beyond my control, yet it strengthens my resolve,\u201d said Rose, reaching out her hand. \u201cI must leave you now, indeed.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI ask but one pledge,\u201d Harry said. \u201cOnce, only once again\u2014say within a year, perhaps much sooner\u2014let me speak of this once more, for the last time.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot to urge me to forsake my just determination,\u201d answered Rose, a sorrowful smile hovering on her lips; \u201cit would be useless.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo,\u201d said Harry; \u201cmerely to hear you repeat it, if you will\u2014finally repeat it. I will lay before you whatever rank or fortune may be mine; and if you still hold to your present decision, I will not endeavor, by speech or deed, to alter it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen let it be so,\u201d Rose replied; \u201cit is but one more pang, and perhaps by then I shall bear it better.\u201d\\n\\nShe offered her hand again.\"}"
