. He tore the letter into shreds. He had decided he would try no more experiments. Then he wandered down to the Thames Embankment and sat for hours by the river. The moon peered through a mane of tawny clouds like a lion\u2019s eye, and countless stars dotted the hollow sky like gold dust scattered on a purple dome. Now and then a barge drifted into the murky current and floated away with the tide, and the railway signals shifted from green to scarlet as the trains shrieked across the bridge.\"}"
