          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"ec9ec6ffb1bf53415fe9953a\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cI am very ignorant, and it troubles me\u2014only a little.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTell me what is on your mind.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have a cousin, my sole relative and an orphan like myself, whom I love dearly. She is five years younger than I, living in a farmer\u2019s house in the south. Poverty separated us, and she knows nothing of what has become of me\u2014for I cannot write\u2014and if I could, how should I explain it? It is better left so.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, yes: better as it stands.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat I was thinking as we came along, and still think now as I look into your kind, strong face that gives me so much courage, is this:\u2014If the Republic truly benefits the poor, if they grow less hungry and suffer less in every way, she might live many years; she might even grow old.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat then, my gentle sister?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDo you suppose\u201d\u2014the patient eyes, so full of endurance, brim with tears, the lips part more and tremble\u2014\u201cthat it will feel long to me, waiting for her in that better land where I trust both you and I will be mercifully sheltered?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt cannot, my child; there is no Time there, no hardship there.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou comfort me so deeply! I am so ignorant. Should I kiss you now? Has the moment arrived?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes.\u201d\\n\\nShe touches his lips; he touches hers; they bless each other solemnly. The slender hand is steady as he lets it go; nothing but a sweet, bright constancy shows in the patient face. She steps forward ahead of him\u2014then she is gone; the knitting women count Twenty-Two.\\n\\n\u201cI am the Resurrection and the Life, saith the Lord: he that believeth in me, though he were dead, yet shall he live: and whosoever liveth and believeth in me shall never die.\u201d\\n\\nThe murmur of countless voices, countless faces turning upward, the surge of many footsteps along the crowd\u2019s edge, until it swells forward in one mass, like a single great heave of water, all vanish in a flash. Twenty-Three.\\n\\n*****\\n\\nThey said of him, across the city that night, that no one had ever seen a face more peaceful there. Many added that he appeared sublime and prophetic"
