          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"8855edd8ce992e7fab075964\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cI wrapped him up in the paper and stuffed part of it in his mouth\u2014that was how I did it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd you think your master was actually bitten by the beetle, and that the bite made him sick?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t think anything about it\u2014I know it. Why would he keep dreaming about the gold so much if it isn\u2019t because he was bitten by the gold-bug? I\u2019ve heard about those gold-bugs before now.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut how do you know he dreams about gold?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHow do I know? Because he talks about it in his sleep\u2014that\u2019s how I know.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, Jup, maybe you\u2019re right; but to what good fortune do I owe the honor of a visit from you today?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s the matter, master?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDid you bring any message from Mr. Legrand?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, master, I brought this pistol;\u201d and here Jupiter handed me a note which read as follows:\\n\\n\u201cMY DEAR \u2014\u2014 Why haven\u2019t I seen you for so long? I hope you haven\u2019t been foolish enough to take offense at any small brusqueness of mine; but no, that seems unlikely. Since I saw you I\u2019ve had great cause for anxiety. I have something to tell you, yet hardly know how to tell it, or whether I should tell it at all.\\n\\n\u201cI haven\u2019t been quite well for some days, and poor old Jup annoys me almost beyond bearing with his well-meant attentions. Would you believe it? The other day he prepared a huge stick to chastise me for slipping away and spending the day alone among the hills on the mainland. I truly believe my sickly appearance was the only thing that spared me a whipping.\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019ve made no additions to my collection since we met.\\n\\n\u201cIf you can make it convenient, come over with Jupiter. Do come. I want to see you tonight, on business of importance. I assure you it is of the highest importance.\\n\\n\u201cEver yours,\\n\u201cWILLIAM LEGRAND.\u201d\\n\\nSomething in the tone of this note filled me with unease. The whole style was markedly different from Legrand\u2019s usual manner. What was he imagining now? What new notion had seized his excitable brain? What \u201cbusiness of the highest importance\u201d could he possibly have? Jupiter\u2019s account of him promised nothing good. I feared that the ongoing weight of misfortune had finally unsettled my friend\u2019s mind. Without hesitation, therefore, I made ready to go with the man.\\n\\nWhen we reached the wharf, I noticed a scythe and three spades, all apparently new, lying in the bottom of the boat we were to take.\\n\\n\u201cWhat does all this mean, Jup?\u201d\"}"
