          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"b78d33d1d643da6c1daa8576\",\"rewritten_text\":\"I now examined the death\u2019s-head attentively. The outermost edges\u2014the parts of the drawing nearest the margin of the vellum\u2014stood out far more clearly than the rest. It was evident the heat had acted imperfectly or unevenly. I immediately lit a fire and exposed every inch of the parchment to a glowing warmth. At first, the sole result was the sharpening of the faint skull-lines; but by persisting, I saw appear, at the corner of the slip opposite the death\u2019s-head, the figure I initially took for a goat. A closer look convinced me it was meant for a kid.\\n\\n\u201cHa! ha!\u201d I cried. \u201cTruly, I\u2019ve no right to laugh\u2014a million and a half is no laughing matter\u2014but you surely cannot forge a third link for your chain; you will find no special tie between your pirates and a goat. Pirates, you know, are no cattle-dealers.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have already told you, the figure was not a goat.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell then, a kid\u2014much the same.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNearly, yet not quite,\u201d Legrand said. \u201cYou may have heard of Captain Kidd. I instantly regarded the creature as a punning or hieroglyphic signature. I use \u2018signature\u2019 because its place on the vellum implied as much. The death\u2019s-head in the opposite corner wore the appearance of a stamp or seal. Still, I was vexed by the lack of all else\u2014no body to my supposed instrument\u2014no text to accompany my context.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI suppose you expected a letter between stamp and signature.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSomething of that nature. The truth is, I felt an irresistible presentiment of great fortune at hand. I hardly know why. Perhaps it was more yearning than belief; yet Jupiter\u2019s foolish talk about the bug being pure gold strangely fired my imagination. And then all those accidents and coincidences\u2014so singular! Notice how purely accidental it was that every event happened on the only day in the year cool enough for a fire; and without the fire\u2014or the dog\u2019s timely intrusion\u2014I should never have discovered the death\u2019s-head, and thus never become master of the treasure.\u201d\"}"
