          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"88b29f82aad1efdd261d5a14\",\"rewritten_text\":\"There was something so remarkable in the growing shine of Mr. Wopsle\u2019s eye, and he seemed to be turning so many thoughts over and getting so confused, that I could not understand it. I kept thinking about it long after he had risen into the clouds in a large watch-case, and still I could not understand. I was still thinking about it when I left the theatre an hour later and found him waiting for me near the door.\\n\\n\u201cHow are you?\u201d I said, shaking hands with him as we headed down the street together. \u201cI saw that you saw me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSaw you, Mr. Pip!\u201d he answered. \u201cYes, of course I saw you. But who else was there?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWho else?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s the strangest thing,\u201d said Mr. Wopsle, slipping back into that dazed look. \u201cAnd yet I could swear to him.\u201d\\n\\nGrowing alarmed, I begged Mr. Wopsle to explain his meaning.\\n\\n\u201cWhether I would have noticed him at first if you hadn\u2019t been there,\u201d he said, still in that far-off way, \u201cI can\u2019t say for sure; but I think I would have.\u201d\\n\\nWithout meaning to, I looked around me, as I often did when returning home; his mysterious words gave me a chill.\\n\\n\u201cOh! He can\u2019t be in sight,\u201d said Mr. Wopsle. \u201cHe left before I went off. I saw him go.\u201d\\n\\nBecause I had my reasons for being wary, I even suspected this poor actor. I feared he meant to trick me into admitting something. So I glanced at him as we walked, but kept silent.\\n\\n\u201cI had a foolish notion he must be with you, Mr. Pip, until I saw you were entirely unaware of him, sitting behind you like a ghost.\u201d\\n\\nThe chill crept over me again, yet I was set on staying quiet, for his words could easily be a plan to make me link these hints to Provis. Of course, I knew for certain Provis had not been there.\\n\\n\u201cI dare say you find me strange, Mr. 