true distance from Earth was the first point to address. The average space between the centers of the two bodies is 59.9643 Earth equatorial radii, or only about 237,000 miles. I say average, but remember that the moon\u2019s orbit, being an ellipse of eccentricity equal to 0.05484 of its major semi-axis, with Earth\u2019s center at its focus, would let me greatly reduce the distance if I could contrive to meet the moon, so to speak, at its perigee.\u201d\"}"
