          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"8b59c5f23fb5c552b0142d84\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cStarve you to death? Oh, Mr. Ghost\u2014I mean Sir Simon\u2014are you hungry? I have a sandwich in my case. Would you like it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, thank you, I never eat anything now; but it is very kind of you, all the same, and you are far nicer than the rest of your dreadful, rude, vulgar, dishonest family.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cStop!\u201d cried Virginia, stamping her foot. \u201cIt is you who are rude and vulgar and dreadful, and as for dishonesty, you know you stole the paints from my box to touch up that ridiculous bloodstain in the library. First you took all my reds, including the vermilion, so I couldn\u2019t finish any sunsets. Then you took the emerald-green and the chrome-yellow, and finally I had nothing left but indigo and Chinese white, so I could only paint moonlight scenes, which are always depressing to look at and very hard to paint. I never told on you, though I was extremely annoyed, and the whole thing was absurd; who ever heard of emerald-green blood?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, really,\u201d said the Ghost rather meekly, \u201cwhat else could I do? It is very difficult to get real blood nowadays, and since your brother started it all with his Paragon Detergent, I certainly saw no reason why I shouldn\u2019t take your paints. As for color, that is always a matter of taste: the Cantervilles have blue blood, for example, the very bluest in England; but I know you Americans don\u2019t care about such details.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou know nothing about it, and the best thing you can do is emigrate and improve your mind. My father will be delighted to give you a free passage, and though there is a heavy duty on spirits of every kind, there will be no trouble at the Custom House, as the officers are all Democrats. Once in New York, you are sure to be a great success. I know lots of people there who would give a hundred thousand dollars to have a grandfather, and much more to have a family ghost.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t think I should like America.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI suppose because we have no ruins and no curiosities,\u201d said Virginia sarcastically.\\n\\n\u201cNo ruins! No curiosities!\u201d answered the Ghost. \u201cYou have your navy and your manners.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGood evening; I\u2019ll go ask Papa to get the twins an extra week\u2019s holiday.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cPlease don\u2019t go, Miss Virginia,\u201d he cried. \u201cI am so lonely and unhappy, and I truly don\u2019t know what to do. I want to go to sleep and I cannot.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s quite absurd! You only have to go to bed and blow out the candle.\u201d\"}"
        }
