 the northern mimic, landed in a tree over his head and poured out imitations of her neighbors in pure delight; then a sharp-voiced jay dropped down like a streak of blue flame, perched on a twig within arm\u2019s reach, cocked its head, and stared at the strangers with burning curiosity. A gray squirrel and a bigger \u201cfox\u201d squirrel dashed past, sitting up now and then to study and chatter at the boys, for these wild creatures had probably never seen human beings before and didn\u2019t quite know whether to be afraid.\"}"
