          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"30945653735f6d2a1740e283\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The elegant gentlemen of the finest breeding wore dangling trinkets that chimed as they moved; those golden chains rang like tiny bells. Along with that chiming, and the rustle of silk, brocade, and fine linen, there was a flutter in the air that kept Saint Antoine and its ravenous hunger far away.\\n\\nClothing was the unfailing spell used to keep everything in its place. Everyone was dressed for a Fancy Ball that would never end. From the Palace of the Tuileries, through Monseigneur and the entire Court, through the Chambers, the Tribunals of Justice, and all society (except the scarecrows), the Fancy Ball even reached the Common Executioner, who had to perform \u201cfrizzled, powdered, in a gold-laced coat, pumps, and white silk stockings.\u201d At the gallows and the wheel\u2014the axe was rare\u2014Monsieur Paris, as his fellow professors in the provinces, Monsieur Orleans, and the rest called him in the churchly style, presided in this dainty outfit. And who among the guests at Monseigneur\u2019s reception in that seventeen hundred and eightieth year of our Lord could doubt that a system rooted in a frizzled, powdered, gold-laced, pump-wearing, white-silk-stockinged hangman would outlast the stars!\\n\\nAfter Monseigneur relieved his four men of their burdens and drank his chocolate, he ordered the doors of the Holiest of Holies opened and came out. Then came submission, cringing, fawning, servility, and utter humiliation. There was no bowing left for Heaven\u2014which might be one reason why Monseigneur\u2019s worshippers never bothered with it.\\n\\nDropping a promise here and a smile there, a whisper for one lucky servant and a wave of the hand for another, Monseigneur graciously passed through his rooms to the distant region of the Circumference of Truth. There, Monseigneur turned and came back again, and in due time was shut up in his sanctuary by the chocolate sprites, and was seen no more.\\n\\nWhen the show ended, the flutter in the air became a little storm, and the precious little bells rang down the stairs. Soon only one person remained, and he, with his hat under his arm and his snuffbox in his hand, slowly passed the mirrors on his way out.\\n\\n\u201cI devote you,\u201d said this person, stopping at the last door and turning toward the sanctuary, \u201cto the Devil!\u201d\\n\\nWith that, he shook the snuff from his fingers as if shaking dust from his feet, and quietly walked downstairs.\"}"
