he wall was a huge iron ring, and chained to it lay a gaunt skeleton stretched full length on the stone floor, its long fleshless fingers straining toward an old-fashioned trencher and ewer placed just beyond reach. The jug had clearly once held water, as green mold coated its interior. The trencher held nothing but a pile of dust. Virginia knelt beside the skeleton, folded her little hands, and began to pray in silence, while the rest of the group watched in awe at the terrible tragedy now revealed to them.\"}"
