          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"ad6061d15fb91916651de743\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Accordingly, I determined to jump down the instant we reached the town and remove myself from his hearing. I carried out this plan without difficulty. My small portmanteau lay in the boot beneath my feet; a twist of the hinge freed it; I dropped it in front of me, followed it out, and found myself under the first lamp upon the initial stones of the town pavement. The convicts proceeded with the coach, and I knew precisely where they would be spirited away to the river. In imagination, I saw their boat with its crew of prisoners waiting at the slime-coated steps, heard once more the gruff \u201cGive way, you!\u201d as if to hounds, and again beheld the sinister Noah\u2019s Ark riding on the black water.\\n\\nI could not have declared what alarmed me, for my dread was utterly shapeless and obscure, yet it weighed heavily upon me. While I walked toward the hotel, I felt a terror far beyond the apprehension of an unpleasant or awkward recognition, and it set me quivering. I am sure it took no distinct outline, but was the momentary revival of the fright of childhood.\\n\\nThe Blue Boar\u2019s coffee-room stood empty, and I had ordered and even begun my dinner there before the waiter recognized me. When he had apologized for his forgetfulness, he asked if he should send Boots for Mr. Pumblechook.\\n\\n\u201cNo,\u201d I answered, \u201cdecidedly not.\u201d\\n\\nThe waiter\u2014he who had carried up the Great Remonstrance from the Commercials the day I was bound\u2014looked astonished, and soon contrived to place a grimy old local newspaper directly before me so that I picked it up and read the following paragraph:\\n\\nOur readers will learn, not without a degree of interest, concerning the late romantic rise in fortune of a young iron artificer from this neighbourhood (and what a topic, indeed, for the wand of our not yet universally celebrated fellow citizen TOOBY, the poet of our columns!) that the youth\u2019s earliest patron, companion, and confidant was a most respectable personage not entirely disconnected from the corn and seed business, whose most convenient and spacious premises stand within a hundred miles of the High Street. It is not quite apart from our own personal feeling that we chronicle HIM as the Mentor of our young Telemachus, for it is satisfying to know that our town produced the originator of the latter\u2019s fortune.\"}"
