          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"06b10f04749075dbfcb6af34\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cCertainly not,\u201d Duff answered. \\n\\n\u201cAnd to interpret \u2018yokel\u2019 for the ladies, you mean the attempt wasn\u2019t made by a countryman?\u201d Mr. Losberne asked with a smile.\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s right, sir,\u201d Blathers replied. \u201cThis is all about the robbery, then?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll,\u201d said the doctor.\\n\\n\u201cAnd what\u2019s this about the boy the servants keep talking about?\u201d Blathers asked.\\n\\n\u201cNothing at all,\u201d the doctor answered. \u201cOne of the scared servants decided he had something to do with the break-in, but it\u2019s nonsense.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cVery easily settled, if so,\u201d Duff remarked.\\n\\n\u201cHe\u2019s quite right,\u201d Blathers said, nodding and idly clicking the handcuffs as if they were castanets. \u201cWho is the boy? What does he say about himself? Where did he come from? He didn\u2019t fall out of the clouds, did he, sir?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOf course not,\u201d the doctor replied, glancing nervously at the two ladies. \u201cI know his whole history, but we can talk about that later. You\u2019d like to see where the thieves tried to get in first, I suppose?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCertainly,\u201d Mr. Blathers said. \u201cWe should inspect the place first and question the servants afterward. That\u2019s the usual procedure.\u201d\\n\\nThey got lights, and Blathers and Duff, followed by the town constable, Brittles, Giles, and everyone else, went into the small room at the end of the hall to look out the window. Then they went across the lawn to look in through the window; then someone handed out a candle so they could examine the shutter; then a lantern so they could trace footprints; then a pitchfork to probe the bushes. All this was done with everyone looking on in breathless suspense. They came back in, and Mr. Giles and Brittles acted out their part in the previous night\u2019s adventure, performing it about six times over: disagreeing the first time in only one important point, and by the last time in perhaps a dozen. Once they finished, Blathers and Duff cleared the room and held a long meeting together which, for secrecy and gravity, would make the most serious medical consultation seem like child\u2019s play.\\n\\nMeanwhile the doctor paced the next room in great anxiety, while Mrs. Maylie and Rose watched with worried faces.\\n\\n\u201cHonestly,\u201d he said, stopping after many quick turns, \u201cI hardly know what to do.\u201d\"}"
