          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"5ce7b37d09590c6c6f65c53c\",\"rewritten_text\":\"It is strange, but everyone who vanishes is said to have been seen in San Francisco. It must be a charming city, with all the appeal of the next world.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you think happened to Basil?\u201d asked Dorian, holding his Burgundy up to the light and wondering how he could talk about it so calmly.\\n\\n\u201cI have no idea. If Basil wants to hide, that\u2019s his affair. If he\u2019s dead, I\u2019d rather not think about him. Death is the only thing that frightens me. I hate it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy?\u201d asked the younger man tiredly.\\n\\n\u201cBecause,\u201d said Lord Henry, touching his nose with the gilt grille of an open vinaigrette, \u201cnowadays you can survive everything but that. Death and vulgarity are the only facts in the nineteenth century you can\u2019t explain away. Let\u2019s have our coffee in the music room, Dorian. You must play Chopin for me. The man my wife ran off with played Chopin beautifully. Poor Victoria! I was very fond of her. The house is rather lonely without her. Of course marriage is just a habit, a bad habit. But one still misses even one\u2019s worst habits. Perhaps those are the ones we miss most. They are such an essential part of one\u2019s personality.\u201d\\n\\nDorian said nothing, but rose from the table, went into the next room, sat at the piano, and let his fingers wander over the ivory keys. After the coffee arrived, he stopped and looked over at Lord Henry. \u201cHarry, did it ever occur to you that Basil was murdered?\u201d\\n\\nLord Henry yawned. \u201cBasil was very popular and always wore a Waterbury watch. Why would anyone murder him? He wasn\u2019t clever enough to have enemies. He had a wonderful talent for painting, of course. But a man can paint like Vel\u00e1zquez and still be dull. Basil was really rather dull. He only interested me once, when he told me years ago that he adored you and that you were the driving force of his art.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI was very fond of Basil,\u201d said Dorian, his voice sad. \u201cBut don\u2019t people say he was murdered?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, some papers do. It doesn\u2019t seem likely. I know there are horrible places in Paris, but Basil wasn\u2019t the sort to go to them. He had no curiosity. That was his main failing.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat would you say, Harry, if I told you I murdered Basil?\u201d asked the younger man.\"}"
