 intend to say these deductions are the only proper ones, and that the suspicion arises inevitably from them as the sole outcome. What that suspicion is, however, I won\u2019t say yet. I only ask you to remember that, for me, it was forceful enough to shape and direct my inquiries in the chamber. \u201cNow let us imagine ourselves inside that room. What should we look for first? The escape route the murderers used. It\u2019s no exaggeration to say that neither of us believes in supernatural events.\u201d\"}"
