          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"46a55f2f6f28c35e5e4ba6bf\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Dear me, she was a consummate talker. It would not have suited me to hint that it was quite late, that I was worn out, drowsy, and eager for sleep. I wished I had taken myself off to bed when I had the opportunity. Now I had to see it through; nothing else to be done. So she tinkled on and on, while the castle slumbered in profound, eerie stillness, until after a time there rose, as though from far beneath, a faint sound like a muffled scream\u2014with such pain in it that my skin prickled. The queen paused, eyes gleaming with delight; she cocked her slender head the way a bird does when it listens. The sound tunneled up through the quiet once more.\\n\\n\u201cWhat is it?\u201d I asked.\\n\\n\u201cIt is indeed a stubborn spirit that suffereth long. Many hours hath it been now.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSuffereth what?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThe rack. Come\u2014ye shall behold a merry sight. If he will not yield his secret even now, ye shall watch him rent in twain.\u201d\\n\\nWhat an exquisitely smooth she-devil she was; so calm and self-possessed, while every nerve down my legs twinged in sympathy with that man\u2019s torment. Escorted by armored guards carrying blazing torches, we clattered through echoing hallways, descended stone staircases clammy and dripping, smelling of damp and centuries of captive darkness\u2014a chilly, uncanny trek, a long one, not the more pleasant or shorter for the sorceress\u2019s chatter, which dwelt on the victim and his offense. He had been accused by an unknown informer of slaying a stag in the royal preserve. I said:\\n\\n\u201cAnonymous testimony is hardly the right thing, your Highness. It were fairer to bring the accused face to face with the accuser.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI had not bethought me of that, it being but a small matter. Yet even an I would, I could not, for that the accuser came masked by night, told the forester, and straightway departed, so the forester knoweth him not.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen this Unknown is the only witness who saw the stag killed?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMarry, _no_ man _saw_ the slaying; this Unknown observed the bold varlet near the spot where the stag lay, and came with right loyal fervor to betray him to the forester.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSo the Unknown, too, was near the dead stag? Might it not be he himself who did the killing? His loyal zeal\u2014behind a mask\u2014seems a trifle suspicious. But what does your Highness expect to gain by racking the prisoner? Where lies the advantage?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHe will not confess otherwise; without confession his soul were lost. For his crime the law forfeits his life\u2014and of a surety will I see that he pay it!\u2014yet it were peril to my own soul to let him perish unconfessed and unabsolved.\u201d\"}"
        }
