          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"4bd6bb859cb5cb9357ba1d1d\",\"rewritten_text\":\"She wasn\u2019t mistaken about the rats. Every so often one would poke its snout out of a hole in the corner. She kept things close at hand to fling at them whenever she was by herself, or else they\u2019d torment her without cease. She showed me a bar of lead twisted into a knot and said she usually could hit with it, but she\u2019d strained her arm a day or two before and wasn\u2019t sure she could throw straight now. Still, she watched for her chance and soon let fly at a rat; she missed badly and cried \u201cOuch!\u201d because it hurt her arm. Then she told me to try for the next one. I wanted to get away before the old man returned, but naturally I didn\u2019t let that show. I took the lead, and the first rat that poked out, I let go; if he\u2019d stayed put he\u2019d have been a mighty sick rat. She called it fine work and figured I\u2019d bag the next. She retrieved the lead and brought a hank of yarn she wanted me to help with. I held up my hands while she draped the hank over them, talking about her own affairs and her husband\u2019s. But she broke off to say:\\n\\n\u201cKeep watch for the rats. You better keep the lead in your lap, ready.\u201d\\n\\nSo she dropped the lump into my lap then and there, and I squeezed my knees together on it while she kept on. But only for a minute. Then she took the hank away, looked me straight in the eye, friendly-like, and said:\\n\\n\u201cCome now, what\u2019s your real name?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWh\u2014what, ma\u2019am?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s your real name? Is it Bill, or Tom, or Bob?\u2014or which?\u201d\\n\\nI reckon I trembled like a leaf, not knowing what to do. But I said:\\n\\n\u201cPlease don\u2019t make sport of a poor girl like me, ma\u2019am. If I\u2019m a bother here, I\u2019ll\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, you won\u2019t. Sit right where you are. I won\u2019t hurt you, and I won\u2019t inform on you, neither. Just tell me your secret and trust me. I\u2019ll keep it; and more than that, I\u2019ll help you. My old man will too if you want him. See, you\u2019re just a runaway apprentice, that\u2019s all. It\u2019s nothing. There\u2019s no harm in it. You\u2019ve been mistreated, and you decided to light out. Bless you, child, I\u2019d never tell on you.\u201d\"}"
