          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"557c43c177659ed80cf53728\",\"rewritten_text\":\"They know how sharp the lad is; he\u2019ll get sent down for life. They won\u2019t settle for anything less than making the Artful a lifer.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat d\u2019ye mean by lagging and a lifer?\u201d Mr. Bolter demanded. \u201cWhat\u2019s the sense of talking to me like that? Why don\u2019t yer speak so\u2019s I can understand?\u201d\\n\\nFagin was about to translate these mysterious phrases into plain talk; had he done so, Mr. Bolter would have learned they meant \u201ctransportation for life.\u201d But the conversation was interrupted by Master Bates, hands buried in his breeches-pockets and his face twisted into a half-comic distress.\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s all over, Fagin,\u201d Charley declared, after he and the newcomer were introduced.\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s that supposed to mean?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThey\u2019ve tracked down the gent the box belongs to; two or three others are coming to \u2019dentify him; and the Artful\u2019s booked for the long voyage,\u201d said Master Bates. \u201cI\u2019ll need a full suit of mourning, Fagin, and a hatband, to visit him before he starts his travels. To think Jack Dawkins\u2014flash Jack\u2014the Dodger\u2014the Artful Dodger\u2014should be deported over a cheap twopenny-halfpenny snuff-box! Never thought he\u2019d be nabbed for less than a gold watch with chain and seals, at the very least. Oh, why didn\u2019t he clean out some wealthy old gent of all his valubles, and sail off like a gentleman, instead of like any common prig, with no honour nor glory!\u201d\\n\\nHaving voiced his sympathy for his unlucky friend, Master Bates dropped onto the nearest chair, wearing an air of gloom and disappointment.\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you mean by saying he\u2019s no honour nor glory?\u201d Fagin cried, turning a furious look on his pupil. \u201cWasn\u2019t he always the top-sawyer among you? Any of you ever match him or get near him on any scent, eh?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot one,\u201d Master Bates answered, his voice thick with remorse. \u201cNot a soul.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen what\u2019s this talk? What are you bawling about?\u201d Fagin snapped.\\n\\n\u201c\u2019Cause it isn\u2019t entered on the record, is it?\u201d Charley shot back, stung into full defiance by his grief. \u201c\u2019Cause it won\u2019t show in the indictment; \u2019cause nobody\u2019ll ever know half of what he could do. How\u2019ll he be listed in the Newgate Calendar? Maybe not there at all. Oh, my eye, my eye, what a blow!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHa! ha!\u201d Fagin crowed, stretching out his right hand and turning to Mr. Bolter in a fit of mirth that shook him as though he had the palsy. \u201cSee the pride they take in their trade, my dear.\u201d\"}"
