          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"2e9c7ab899260f81c276cf12\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cNever!\u201d the girl retorted. \u201cTell me why?\u201d \u201cFor one reason,\u201d she answered with steady resolve, \u201cfor one reason alone: the lady is aware and will stand beside me; I know she will, for she has pledged as much. Besides, for this other reason\u2014though he has lived wickedly, I have lived wickedly too. Many of us have trod the same paths together, and I will not betray them, when any one of them\u2014bad as they are\u2014might have betrayed me, yet didn\u2019t.\u201d \u201cThen,\u201d said the gentleman swiftly, as if this were the point he had strained to reach, \u201cplace Monks in my hands and leave him for me to manage.\u201d \u201cWhat if he betrays the others?\u201d \u201cIn that event,\u201d he replied, \u201cif the truth must be forced from him, there the matter will end. There must be passages in Oliver\u2019s little story which it would be painful to drag into public view; and once the truth is laid bare, the others shall go unscathed.\u201d \u201cAnd if it is not?\u201d the girl suggested. \u201cThen,\u201d continued the gentleman, \u201cFagin shall not be surrendered to justice without your consent. In such a situation I believe I could show you reasons that would prevail upon you to grant it.\u201d \u201cDo I have the lady\u2019s promise to that effect?\u201d the girl asked. \u201cYou do,\u201d Rose answered. \u201cMy faithful pledge.\u201d \u201cMonks would never discover how you learned what you know?\u201d the girl said after a brief pause. \u201cNever,\u201d declared the gentleman. \u201cThe information would be applied in such a manner that he could not even conjecture.\u201d \u201cI have been a liar, and among liars since my earliest days,\u201d she said after another silence, \u201cbut I will accept your word.\u201d Receiving reassurance from both that she could safely do so, she continued\u2014in such a low tone that the listener 