          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"d51baba3c987832104568ea9\",\"rewritten_text\":\"She studied me intently for a brief interval before quietly asking, \u201cWhat do you require for them?\u201d \u201cOnly,\u201d I replied, \u201cthat you will not confuse them with the rest. They may share the same bloodline, but, believe me, their nature is different.\u201d Keeping her scrutinizing gaze upon me, Miss Havisham reiterated, \u201cWhat do you require for them?\u201d \u201cI am not so artful,\u201d I answered, aware that I flushed slightly, \u201cas to conceal from you, even if I wished, that I do desire something. Miss Havisham, if you would spare the money to render my friend Herbert a lasting service, which by necessity must be done without his knowledge, I can show you the means.\u201d \u201cWhy must it be kept from him?\u201d she asked, settling her hands upon her cane so she might examine me more carefully. \u201cBecause,\u201d I said, \u201cI began the service myself, more than two years ago, without his knowledge, and I am unwilling to be betrayed. Why I cannot finish it I cannot explain. That part of the secret belongs to someone else, not to me.\u201d Her eyes drifted from me to the fire. She watched it for what, in the silence and by the wan light of the slowly burning candles, seemed a considerable time, until some coals fell in and roused her. She stared back at me\u2014first blankly, then with her attention slowly sharpening. Estella knitted steadily all the while. Once Miss Havisham fixed her thoughts on me, she spoke as if our conversation had never paused, \u201cWhat more?\u201d \u201cEstella,\u201d I said, turning to her and trying to steady my shaking voice, \u201cyou know I love you. You know I have loved you long and dearly.\u201d At my words she lifted her eyes to my face without arresting her fingers, and regarded me without a change of expression. I noticed Miss Havisham\u2019s glances shift between us. \u201cI should have spoken sooner, but for my long delusion. It led me to believe Miss Havisham destined us for each other. While I supposed you powerless, I held back. But I must say it now.\u201d Estella maintained her impassive look, fingers working still, and she shook her head. \u201cI know,\u201d I replied to that gesture. \u201cI know. I have no hope of ever calling you mine, Estella.\u201d\"}"
