          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"8e29c415d7ef788a87c3b2c8\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Hearing Jim say that made me sorry for him, it felt like such a come-down. My conscience began riling me up worse than ever till finally I told it, \u201cQuit riding me\u2014it ain\u2019t too late yet\u2014I\u2019ll paddle ashore at first light and confess.\u201d Right away I felt relieved, pleased, light as a feather. Every bit of worry dropped off. I kept sharp watch for a light, half humming to myself. After a bit, one showed, and Jim hollers:\\n\\n\u201cWe\u2019s safe, Huck, we\u2019s safe! Jump up en crack yo\u2019 heels! Dat\u2019s good ole Cairo at las\u2019, I jis knows it!\u201d\\n\\nI says:\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019ll take the canoe over and see, Jim. Might not be, you know.\u201d\\n\\nHe sprang up, readied the canoe, spread his old coat in the bottom for me to sit, handed me the paddle; and as I shoved off, he says:\\n\\n\u201cPooty soon I\u2019ll be shout\u2019n for joy, en I\u2019ll say it\u2019s all cause o\u2019 Huck; I\u2019s a free man, en couldn\u2019 never ben free if it hadn\u2019 ben for Huck; Huck done it. Jim ain\u2019t ever gwine forgit you, Huck; you\u2019s de best fren\u2019 Jim ever had; en you\u2019s de only fren\u2019 ole Jim\u2019s got now.\u201d\\n\\nI was paddling away, sweating to betray him; but when he said that, it just knocked the stuffing out of me. I drifted slower then and couldn\u2019t say for sure if I was glad I\u2019d started or not. When I was thirty yards off, Jim says:\\n\\n\u201cDah you goes, de ole true Huck; de on\u2019y white genlman dat ever kep\u2019 his promise to ole Jim.\u201d\\n\\nThat made me feel downright sick. Still, I told myself I had to go through with it\u2014no backing out. Just then along comes a skiff with two men carrying guns; they drew up and so did I. One asks:\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s that out there?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cPiece of a raft,\u201d says I.\\n\\n\u201cYou belong on it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAny men aboard?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cJust one, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, five niggers lit out tonight from up yonder above the head of the bend. Is your man white or black?\u201d\\n\\nI didn\u2019t answer quick. I tried, but couldn\u2019t get the words past my throat. I spent a second or two mustering up the grit, but I warn\u2019t man enough\u2014didn\u2019t have the nerve of a rabbit. I felt myself giving way; so I let it go and blurted:\\n\\n\u201cHe\u2019s white.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI reckon we\u2019ll go see for ourselves.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019d be obliged if you would,\u201d says I, \u201ccause it\u2019s pap out there, and maybe you\u2019ll help me tow the raft in to where that light is.\u201d\"}"
