          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"a48f493c957779d7ac435b18\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cDo you often return?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have not set foot here since then.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNor have I.\u201d\\n\\nAs the moon rose, I remembered the calm gaze fixed on the white ceiling that was gone. As the moon rose, I recalled the pressure of his hand when I spoke the final words he heard in life.\\n\\nEstella next broke the quiet stretching between us.\\n\\n\u201cI have often wished and meant to come back, but many things have held me away. Poor, poor old place!\u201d\\n\\nThe silvery mist caught the first glint of moonlight, and the same light rested on the tears slipping from her eyes. Unaware that I noticed, and trying to master them, she quietly asked,\\n\\n\u201cWere you wondering, as you walked, how it came to be left like this?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, Estella.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThe land is mine. It is the one possession I have not given up. Everything else has fallen from me bit by bit, but I held this. It was the only firm resistance I made through all those miserable years.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIs it to be built on?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAt last it is. I came to bid it farewell before it changes. And you,\u201d she added with a tone that touched a wanderer, \u201cyou still live abroad?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cStill.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd you prosper, I know?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI labor hard for a decent living, and so\u2014yes, I do well.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have often thought of you,\u201d Estella said.\\n\\n\u201cIndeed?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLately, very often. There was a long harsh season when I kept far from me the memory of what I discarded when I knew nothing of its value. But since my duty has not clashed with admitting that remembrance, I have given it a place in my heart.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou have never lost your place in mine,\u201d I replied.\\n\\nWe fell silent again until she spoke.\\n\\n\u201cI never imagined,\u201d said Estella, \u201cthat in taking leave of this place I should also take leave of you. I am very glad of it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGlad to part again, Estella? To me, parting is sorrowful. The memory of our last parting has always been sad and painful to me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut you said to me,\u201d Estella returned with great earnestness, \u201c\u2018God bless you, God forgive you!\u2019 And if you could say that then, you will not hesitate to say it now\u2014now, when suffering has outweighed all other lessons and taught me what your heart used to be. I have been bent and broken, but\u2014I hope\u2014into something better.\u201d\"}"
