          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"3d13cab6e31c64c5d2fd7e4e\",\"rewritten_text\":\"His face, deeply sunburned, was more than half hidden by whiskers and a thick mustache. He carried a massive oak cudgel, but seemed otherwise unarmed. He bowed awkwardly and greeted us with a \u201cgood evening\u201d in French, the accent somewhat Neuch\u00e2tel, yet still clearly indicating Parisian roots.\\n\\n\u201cSit down, my friend,\u201d said Dupin. \u201cI assume you\u2019re here about the orangutan. Honestly, I almost envy you owning him; a remarkably fine and undoubtedly valuable animal. How old do you think he is?\u201d\\n\\nThe sailor drew a long breath, like a man relieved of an unbearable weight, and then replied in a confident tone:\\n\\n\u201cI can\u2019t say for sure\u2014but he can\u2019t be more than four or five years old. Do you have him here?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh no, we had nowhere to keep him here. He\u2019s at a livery stable on Rue Dubourg, just nearby. You can fetch him in the morning. Naturally you\u2019re prepared to prove ownership?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOf course I am, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019ll be sorry to give him up,\u201d Dupin said.\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t expect you to go to all this trouble for nothing, sir,\u201d the man said. \u201cWouldn\u2019t expect it. I\u2019m quite willing to pay a reward for finding the animal\u2014that is, anything reasonable.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell,\u201d my friend replied, \u201cthat\u2019s entirely fair, certainly. Let me think! What should I take? Oh! I\u2019ll tell you. My reward will be this: you\u2019ll give me every bit of information you can about the murders in the Rue Morgue.\u201d\\n\\nDupin spoke those last words very softly, very calmly. Just as calmly, he walked to the door, locked it, and put the key in his pocket. Then he drew a pistol from his coat and laid it on the table without the slightest fuss.\\n\\nThe sailor\u2019s face flared up as if he were suffocating. He jumped up and clutched his cudgel, but the next moment he fell back into his seat, shaking violently, pale as death. He said nothing. I pitied him from the bottom of my heart.\\n\\n\u201cMy friend,\u201d said Dupin gently, \u201cyou\u2019re frightening yourself needlessly\u2014you truly are. We mean you no harm at all. I give you the honor of a gentleman, and of a Frenchman, that we intend you no injury. I know perfectly well that you\u2019re innocent of the atrocities in the Rue Morgue. However, it won\u2019t do to deny that you\u2019re somewhat involved in them.\u201d\"}"
