          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"7d8e27bd044365065834821f\",\"rewritten_text\":\"To be fair to the young lady, she never flatly said she wouldn\u2019t do it; she only strongly wished to be damned if she would. It was a polite, delicate way of refusing and showed she had the kind of natural good manners that hates causing anyone the pain of a blunt rejection.\\n\\nThe Jew\u2019s face fell. He turned from this young lady\u2014who was dressed cheerfully, even flamboyantly, in a red gown, green boots, and yellow curlers\u2014to the other woman.\\n\\n\u201cNancy, my dear,\u201d the Jew said gently, \u201cwhat do you say?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat it\u2019s no good, so don\u2019t bother trying, Fagin,\u201d Nancy replied.\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you mean by that?\u201d Mr. Sikes demanded with a nasty look.\\n\\n\u201cWhat I said, Bill,\u201d the woman answered calmly.\\n\\n\u201cWhy, you\u2019re the perfect person for it,\u201d Sikes argued. \u201cNo one around here knows you.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd I\u2019d like to keep it that way,\u201d Nancy answered in the same calm tone. \u201cSo it\u2019s more no than yes for me, Bill.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cShe\u2019ll go, Fagin,\u201d said Sikes.\\n\\n\u201cNo, she won\u2019t, Fagin,\u201d said Nancy.\\n\\n\u201cYes, she will, Fagin,\u201d said Sikes.\\n\\nAnd Sikes was right. With a mix of threats, promises, and bribes, they finally got the lady to take the job. Unlike her smartly dressed friend, she had recently moved from the distant but respectable suburb of Ratcliffe to Field Lane, so she wasn\u2019t worried about being recognized by any of her many acquaintances.\\n\\nWith a clean white apron tied over her dress and her curlers tucked under a straw bonnet\u2014both supplied from the Jew\u2019s endless stock\u2014Miss Nancy prepared to set out on her errand.\\n\\n\u201cWait a moment, my dear,\u201d said the Jew, pulling out a small covered basket. \u201cCarry this in one hand. It looks more respectable, my dear.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGive her a door key for the other hand, Fagin,\u201d Sikes suggested. \u201cMakes it look proper and genuine.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, yes, my dear, so it does,\u201d said the Jew, hanging a big front-door key on the forefinger of her right hand. \u201cThere; very good! Very good indeed, my dear!\u201d he said, rubbing his hands.\\n\\n\u201cOh, my brother! My poor, dear, sweet, innocent little brother!\u201d Nancy cried, bursting into tears and clutching the basket and key in agony. \u201cWhat\u2019s become of him? Where have they taken him? Please pity me and tell me what\u2019s happened to the dear boy, gentlemen; please, gentlemen, if you please, gentlemen!\u201d\"}"
