          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"d041902c22976f83da88d538\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Dawn had come when I set the manuscript aside. The rain had mostly stopped, leaving the world gray and sad, and the worn-out storm was sighing itself to rest. I went to the stranger\u2019s room and listened at his door, which was slightly open. I heard his voice, so I knocked. There was no answer, though he kept speaking. I peered in. He lay on his back in bed, talking in broken but lively bursts, his arms thrashing restlessly the way delirious patients do. I slipped in quietly and leaned over him. He kept muttering exclamations. I spoke a single word to get his attention. His glassy eyes and ashen face lit at once with pleasure, gratitude, joy, and welcome.\\n\\n\u201cOh, Sandy, you\u2019re here at last\u2014how I\u2019ve longed for you! Sit by me\u2014don\u2019t go\u2014never leave me again, Sandy, never again. Where\u2019s your hand?\u2014give it to me, dear, let me hold it\u2014there\u2014now everything is right, all is peaceful, and I\u2019m happy again\u2014we\u2019re happy again, aren\u2019t we, Sandy? You\u2019re so dim, so vague, like a mist, a cloud, but you\u2019re here, and that\u2019s blessing enough; and I have your hand; don\u2019t take it away\u2014it\u2019s only for a little while, I won\u2019t need it long\u2026. Was that the child?\u2026 Hello\u2014Central!\u2026 she doesn\u2019t answer. Asleep, maybe? Bring her when she wakes, and let me touch her hands, her face, her hair, and say goodbye\u2026. Sandy! Yes, you\u2019re there. I drifted for a moment, and thought you were gone\u2026. Have I been sick long? It must be so; it feels like months. And such dreams! such strange, terrible dreams, Sandy! Dreams as real as waking\u2014delirium, of course, yet so real! I thought the king had died, I thought you were in Gaul and couldn\u2019t get home, I thought there was a revolution; in the wild frenzy of those dreams I thought Clarence and I and a handful of my cadets fought and wiped out the whole chivalry of England! But even that wasn\u2019t the strangest. I seemed to be a creature from a far future age, centuries away, and even that felt real! Yes, I seemed to have flown back from that age into this one, then forward again, and was dropped, a stranger and alone in that strange England, with thirteen centuries yawning between me and you! between me and my home and my friends! between me and everything dear to me, everything that could make life worth living!\u201d\"}"
