          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"989926f6c471ce365c6bf263\",\"rewritten_text\":\"There was something so extraordinary in the growing brightness of Mr. Wopsle\u2019s eye, and he appeared to be balancing so many notions and becoming so muddled, that I could not interpret it. I sat pondering over it long after he had risen to the clouds in a large watch-case, and still I could make nothing of it. I was yet reflecting on it when I stepped out of the theatre an hour later and discovered him lingering near the entrance for me.\\n\\n\u201cHow are you?\u201d I said, shaking his hand as we turned down the street together. \u201cI noticed that you saw me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSaw you, Mr. Pip!\u201d he replied. \u201cCertainly I saw you. But who else was there?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWho besides?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt is the oddest thing,\u201d Mr. Wopsle said, drifting back into that absent expression, \u201cand yet I could swear to him.\u201d\\n\\nGrowing uneasy, I implored Mr. Wopsle to make his meaning clear.\\n\\n\u201cWhether I should have observed him at first without your being there,\u201d Mr. Wopsle went on in the same absent manner, \u201cI can\u2019t say for sure; but I think I should.\u201d\\n\\nUnconsciously I glanced about, as was my habit when going home; for these enigmatic words sent a cold shiver through me.\\n\\n\u201cOh! He can\u2019t be within sight,\u201d Mr. Wopsle said. \u201cHe left before I went off. I watched him go.\u201d\\n\\nBecause of my reason for suspicion, I even doubted this poor player. I feared some scheme to lure me into an admission. So I watched him as we walked together, but kept silent.\\n\\n\u201cI had an absurd idea that he must be with you, Mr. Pip, until I saw you were wholly unaware of him, sitting behind you there like a spirit.\u201d\\n\\nThe earlier chill crawled over me once more, but I was determined not to speak yet, for his words easily allowed that he might be trying to prompt me to link these allusions with Provis. Naturally, I was entirely certain and secure that Provis had not been present.\\n\\n\u201cI dare say you are astonished at me, Mr. Pip; in fact, I can see you are. But it is so very surprising! You\u2019ll scarcely credit what I am about to tell you. I could scarcely credit it myself, if you said it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIndeed?\u201d I said.\\n\\n\u201cNo, indeed. Mr. Pip, you recall, in bygone days, a particular Christmas Day when you were a mere child, and I dined at Gargery\u2019s, and some soldiers came to the door to have a pair of handcuffs repaired?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI remember it perfectly.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd you recollect that there was a pursuit of two convicts, and that we joined it, and Gargery carried you on his back, and I took the lead, and you stayed with me as best you could?\u201d\"}"
