          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"64de09cf5414364e20f0b1ad\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWell, Jup,\u201d I said, \u201cwhat\u2019s the matter now? How is your master?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTo tell the truth, sir, he\u2019s not as well as he should be.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot well! I\u2019m truly sorry to hear it. What does he complain of?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s just it! He never complains about anything, but he\u2019s very sick all the same.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cVery sick, Jupiter! Why didn\u2019t you just say so? Is he confined to bed?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, he\u2019s not! He isn\u2019t shut up anywhere\u2014that\u2019s exactly what bothers me. My mind feels very heavy about poor Master Will.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cJupiter, I\u2019d like to understand what you\u2019re talking about. You say your master is sick. Hasn\u2019t he told you what\u2019s wrong?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, sir, it\u2019s not worth getting angry over. Master Will keeps saying nothing\u2019s the matter with him\u2014but then why does he go around like this, with his head down and his shoulders up, and as pale as a goose? And he keeps a siphon all the time\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cKeeps a what, Jupiter?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cKeeps a siphon with the figures on the slate\u2014the strangest figures I ever saw. I\u2019m starting to get scared, I tell you. I\u2019ve got to keep a very close eye on his moves. The other day he slipped away before sunrise and was gone the whole blessed day. I had a big stick cut and ready to give him a good beating when he came back\u2014but I\u2019m such a fool I couldn\u2019t go through with it after all\u2014he looked so very poor.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cEh? What? Ah yes\u2014on the whole, I think you\u2019d better not be too harsh with the poor fellow. Don\u2019t flog him, Jupiter\u2014he really couldn\u2019t stand it. But can\u2019t you imagine what has caused this illness, or rather this change in his behavior? Has anything unpleasant happened since I saw you?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, sir, nothing unpleasant has happened since then\u2014it was before that, I\u2019m afraid\u2014it was the very day you were there.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHow? What do you mean?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, sir, I mean the bug\u2014there it is.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThe what?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThe bug\u2014I\u2019m certain Master Will was bitten somewhere around the head by that gold bug.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd what makes you think that, Jupiter?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cPlenty of reason, sir, and a mouth too. I never saw such a devilish bug\u2014it kicks and bites everything that comes near it. Master Will caught it first, but had to let it go again very quickly, I\u2019ll tell you\u2014then must have been when he got the bite. I didn\u2019t like the look of the bug\u2019s mouth myself, not at all, so I wouldn\u2019t hold it with my fingers. I picked it up with a piece of paper I found.\u201d\"}"
