          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"7c9efedfe3111b2975fa7652\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Tom managed to scratch up the cupboard with it and was getting ready to start on the bureau when he was summoned to get dressed for Sunday school.\\n\\nMary handed him a tin basin of water and a bar of soap, and he stepped outside, setting the basin on a little bench. He dipped the soap in the water and set it aside, rolled up his sleeves, poured the water out gently onto the ground, and then slipped back into the kitchen to scrub his face vigorously on the towel behind the door. But Mary snatched the towel away and said:\\n\\n\u201cNow aren\u2019t you ashamed, Tom? You can\u2019t be that bad. Water won\u2019t hurt you.\u201d\\n\\nTom was slightly unsettled. She refilled the basin, and this time he hovered over it for a moment, summoning courage; he took a deep breath and began. When he came back into the kitchen with both eyes squeezed shut, feeling for the towel with his hands, a respectable mix of suds and water was streaming off his face. Yet after he finished with the towel, he still wasn\u2019t acceptable; the clean patch ended abruptly at his chin and jaw like a mask, and below that stretched a dark field of untouched dirt spreading across his chest and circling his neck. Mary took over, and when she finished he looked like a man and a brother without any distinction of color, his soaked hair neatly brushed and its short curls arranged into a tidy, symmetrical pattern. [He secretly flattened the curls with a lot of effort, plastering his hair down, because he considered curls effeminate and his own tormented him endlessly.] Then Mary produced a suit he had worn only on Sundays for two years\u2014they were simply referred to as his \u201cother clothes\u201d\u2014and that tells us the size of his wardrobe. After he dressed, she put him in order; she buttoned his snug roundabout up to his chin, flipped his enormous shirt collar down over his shoulders, brushed him off, and set his speckled straw hat on his head. He now looked greatly improved and decidedly miserable. He felt exactly as miserable as he looked, because whole clothes and cleanliness chafed him. He hoped Mary would forget his shoes, but that wish died quickly; she coated them thoroughly with tallow, as was customary, and brought them out. He lost his temper and complained that he was always forced to do everything he didn\u2019t want to do.\"}"
