          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"d32fef5aa99eccfda4ee5e00\",\"rewritten_text\":\"She studied me closely for a moment, then said quietly, \u201cWhat do you want for them?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOnly,\u201d I answered, \u201cthat you won\u2019t mix them up with the others. They may share the same blood, but believe me, they are not of the same nature.\u201d\\n\\nStill watching me, Miss Havisham repeated, \u201cWhat do you want for them?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019m not so sly,\u201d I admitted, feeling myself blush, \u201cthat I could hide from you\u2014even if I wanted to\u2014that I do want something. Miss Havisham, if you would give the money to do my friend Herbert a lasting service in life, a service that must be done without him knowing, I could show you how.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy must it be done without his knowledge?\u201d she asked, settling her hands on her stick so she could study me more closely.\\n\\n\u201cBecause,\u201d I said, \u201cI began helping him over two years ago without his knowing, and I don\u2019t want that secret betrayed. Why I can\u2019t finish it myself, I can\u2019t explain. That part of the secret belongs to someone else, not me.\u201d\\n\\nShe slowly turned her eyes from me to the fire. After watching it in silence for what seemed a long time by the light of the slowly burning candles, she was roused when some of the red coals collapsed. She looked back at me\u2014first blankly, then with growing focus. All the while Estella kept knitting. Once Miss Havisham had fixed her attention on me again, she spoke as if our talk had never paused: \u201cWhat else?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cEstella,\u201d I said, turning to her and trying to steady my shaking voice, \u201cyou know I love you. You know I have loved you for a long time, and dearly.\u201d\\n\\nShe raised her eyes to my face when I spoke, her fingers kept working, and she looked at me without expression. I saw Miss Havisham glance from me to her and back again.\\n\\n\u201cI would have said this sooner, except for the mistake I made so long. It led me to hope that Miss Havisham meant us for each other. While I believed you could not help yourself, in a way, I kept silent. But I have to say it now.\u201d\\n\\nStill expressionless, and with her fingers moving, Estella shook her head.\\n\\n\u201cI know,\u201d I said to that gesture. \u201cI know. I have no hope of ever being able to call you mine, Estella.\u201d\"}"
