          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"075b25118598e48a4ce5e08f\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWe have been to your residence,\u201d said the first man. \u201cNot finding you there, and being told you were likely walking this way, we followed in hopes of overtaking you. Will you please get into the carriage?\u201d\\n\\nBoth men were commanding. As they spoke, they shifted to place me between them and the carriage door. They were armed. I was not.\\n\\n\u201cGentlemen,\u201d I said, \u201cforgive me, but I usually ask who seeks my help and what sort of case I am being called to.\u201d\\n\\nThe second man answered. \u201cDoctor, your clients are people of rank. As for the case itself, our faith in your skill assures us you will figure it out better than we can explain it. Enough. Will you please enter the carriage?\u201d\\n\\nI had no choice but to obey, and I stepped inside without another word. They both followed\u2014one leaping in after raising the steps. The carriage turned around and resumed its former speed.\\n\\nI repeat this conversation exactly as it happened. I am sure every word is the same. I describe everything as it took place, forcing my mind not to stray from the job. Whenever I mark the breaks that follow, I stop for the moment and hide these pages.\\n\\n*****\\n\\nThe carriage left the city streets, passed the North Barrier, and entered the country road. Two-thirds of a league from the Barrier\u2014it was only afterward, when I retraced the route, that I measured the distance\u2014it left the main avenue and soon stopped at a solitary house. All three of us got out and walked along a damp, soft path in a garden where a neglected fountain had overflowed, until we reached the door. It did not open at once after the bell rang, and one of my escorts struck the man who finally opened it across the face with his heavy riding glove.\\n\\nThis did not especially strike me; I had seen common folk beaten more often than dogs. But the other man, also angry, hit him in the same way. Their appearance and manner were now so identical that I realized for the first time they were twin brothers.\\n\\nFrom the moment we stepped through the outer gate\u2014which we found locked and which one brother opened for us and relocked\u2014I had heard cries coming from an upper room.\"}"
