          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"162037f8bec0a856b12b13b1\",\"rewritten_text\":\"There was plenty of cold water to end the meal with. After a while Becky suggested they move on again. Tom stayed quiet a moment before he said, \u201cBecky, can you handle it if I tell you something?\u201d Becky\u2019s face went pale, but she thought she could. \u201cWell then, Becky, we have to stay here where there\u2019s water to drink. That little piece is our last candle!\u201d Becky burst into tears and cried uncontrollably. Tom did his best to comfort her, but not much came of it. Finally Becky said, \u201cTom!\u201d \u201cWell, Becky?\u201d \u201cThey\u2019ll miss us and look for us!\u201d \u201cYes, they will! Of course they will!\u201d \u201cMaybe they\u2019re already looking for us, Tom.\u201d \u201cWell, I guess they might be. I hope they are.\u201d \u201cWhen would they notice we\u2019re gone, Tom?\u201d \u201cWhen they get back to the boat, I suppose.\u201d \u201cTom, it could be dark by then\u2014would they notice we hadn\u2019t come back?\u201d \u201cI don\u2019t know. But anyway, your mother would notice as soon as they got home.\u201d The frightened look on Becky\u2019s face made Tom realize he\u2019d made a mistake. Becky wasn\u2019t even supposed to go home that night! The children fell silent and thoughtful. In a moment Becky broke into fresh sobs, which showed Tom that she had the same thought he did\u2014that Sunday morning might be half over before Mrs. Thatcher realized Becky wasn\u2019t at Mrs. Harper\u2019s. The children fixed their eyes on the tiny candle and watched it melt away, slow and merciless; they watched the half inch of wick stand alone at last; watched the weak flame rise and fall, climb the thin column of smoke, linger at the top a moment, and then\u2014utter darkness took over! Neither of them knew how much time passed before Becky slowly realized she was crying in Tom\u2019s arms. All they knew was that after what felt like a vast stretch of time, both woke from a deathlike stupor of sleep and sank back into their misery. Tom said it might be Sunday now\u2014maybe even Monday. He tried to get Becky to talk, but her grief was too heavy, all her hope gone. Tom said they must have been missed long ago and the search was surely underway. He\u2019d shout, maybe someone would hear. He tried, but in the darkness the distant echoes sounded so terrifying that he wouldn\u2019t try again. The hours dragged by, and hunger returned to torment them. Part of Tom\u2019s half of the cake was left; they divided it and ate, but they only felt hungrier afterward.\"}"
