          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"f2bd506228f166e8bc332d2c\",\"rewritten_text\":\"His features, much scorched by the sun, were more than half concealed beneath whiskers and mustachios. He carried a massive oaken cudgel, yet seemed otherwise without weapons. He gave an awkward bow and greeted us with a \u201cgood evening\u201d in French accents which, though a bit Neufch\u00e2tel in flavor, still betrayed unmistakable Parisian roots.\\n\\n\u201cTake a seat, my friend,\u201d said Dupin. \u201cI assume you\u2019ve come about the Ourang-Outang. Truly, I almost grudge you his possession; he\u2019s a remarkably fine creature, and doubtless of great value. How old would you judge him to be?\u201d\\n\\nThe sailor drew a deep breath, like a man unburdened of a grievous weight, and answered with confidence:\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019ve no means of knowing\u2014but he cannot be more than four or five years old. Have you got him here?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh no, we\u2019re unfitted to keep him here. He\u2019s lodged at a livery stable in the Rue Dubourg, close by. You may take him in the morning. You are, of course, ready to prove your ownership?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCertainly I am, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI shall regret parting with him,\u201d Dupin added.\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t expect you to take all this trouble for nothing, sir,\u201d the fellow replied. \u201cWouldn\u2019t be reasonable. I\u2019m quite willing to pay a reward for recovering the animal\u2014in reason, of course.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell,\u201d returned my companion, \u201cthat is quite fair. Let me see!\u2014what should the reward be? Ah! I have it. You shall give me every scrap of information you possess about the murders in the Rue Morgue.\u201d\\n\\nDupin uttered these last words in a very subdued voice, very calmly. Just as calmly he strolled to the door, locked it, and slipped the key into his pocket. He then drew a pistol from his breast and laid it on the table without the slightest perturbation.\\n\\nThe sailor\u2019s visage flushed as though he were on the verge of suffocation. He sprang up and clutched his cudgel, but the next instant sank back into his chair, shaking uncontrollably and looking like death itself. He did not utter a syllable. I pitied him with all my heart.\\n\\n\u201cMy good fellow,\u201d said Dupin gently, \u201cyou are frightening yourself needlessly\u2014you truly are. We intend you no harm whatever. I give you the pledge of my honor as a gentleman and a Frenchman that we mean you no injury. I am perfectly aware that you are innocent of the butchery in the Rue Morgue. Still, it will not do to deny that you are, in some degree, involved.\u201d\"}"
