          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"50332f0a227aa593bf5ff06d\",\"rewritten_text\":\"I went from shop to shop, buying whatever was needed to change his appearance. When that business was done, I headed to Little Britain on my own errand. Mr. Jaggers sat at his desk, but as soon as he saw me enter, he rose and stood before his fire.\\n\\n\u201cNow, Pip,\u201d he said, \u201cbe careful.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI will, sir,\u201d I answered, for I had planned what I meant to say on my way there.\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t condemn yourself,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, \u201cand don\u2019t condemn anyone else. You understand\u2014anyone. Don\u2019t tell me anything: I don\u2019t want to know anything; I\u2019m not curious.\u201d\\n\\nOf course I realized he knew the man had come.\\n\\n\u201cI only want, Mr. Jaggers,\u201d I said, \u201cto assure myself that what I have been told is true. I don\u2019t hope it is false, but at least I can confirm it.\u201d\\n\\nMr. Jaggers nodded. \u201cBut did you say \u2018told\u2019 or \u2018informed\u2019?\u201d he asked, tilting his head and looking not at me but thoughtfully at the floor. \u201c\u2018Told\u2019 would suggest spoken communication. You can\u2019t have spoken communication with a man in New South Wales, you know.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI will say informed, Mr. Jaggers.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGood.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have been informed by a person named Abel Magwitch that he is the long-unknown benefactor to me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat is the man,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, \u201cin New South Wales.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd only he?\u201d I said.\\n\\n\u201cAnd only he,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers.\\n\\n\u201cI am not so unreasonable, sir, as to hold you in any way responsible for my mistakes and wrong conclusions, but I always believed it was Miss Havisham.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAs you say, Pip,\u201d returned Mr. Jaggers, turning his eyes on me coolly and biting his forefinger, \u201cI am not responsible for that at all.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd yet it seemed so likely, sir,\u201d I pleaded, downcast.\\n\\n\u201cNot a speck of evidence, Pip,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, shaking his head and gathering up his skirts. \u201cTake nothing on appearances; take everything on evidence. There\u2019s no better rule.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have nothing more to say,\u201d I answered with a sigh after a short silence. \u201cI have confirmed my information, and that is the end of it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd with Magwitch\u2014in New South Wales\u2014having finally revealed himself,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, \u201cyou will understand, Pip, how strictly, throughout my dealings with you, I have kept to the exact line of fact. There has never been the least deviation from the exact line of fact. You know that?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cQuite, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI informed Magwitch\u2014in New South Wales\u2014when he first wrote to me\u2014from New South Wales\u2014that he must never expect me to deviate from the exact line of fact.\u201d\"}"
