          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"eae5aec142e522711717db72\",\"rewritten_text\":\"With everything thus harmoniously settled, the agreement was sealed by another teacup of peppermint cordial, the more needful because of the lady\u2019s fluttered nerves. While she sipped, she informed Mr. Bumble of the old woman\u2019s passing.\\n\\n\u201cVery good,\u201d said he, tasting his peppermint. \u201cI\u2019ll stop by Sowerberry\u2019s on my way home and tell him to send in the morning. Was that what startled you, love?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt was nothing particular, dear,\u201d she replied evasively.\\n\\n\u201cIt must have been something, love,\u201d Mr. Bumble insisted. \u201cWon\u2019t you tell your own B.?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot now,\u201d the lady answered. \u201cOne day. After we\u2019re married, dear.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAfter we\u2019re married!\u201d cried Mr. Bumble. \u201cIt wasn\u2019t any impertinence from those male paupers as\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, no, love!\u201d the lady cried quickly.\\n\\n\u201cIf I thought it was,\u201d Mr. Bumble went on, \u201cif I believed any of them had dared to lift their wulgar eyes to that lovely face\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThey wouldn\u2019t have dared, love,\u201d she returned.\\n\\n\u201cThey had better not!\u201d he declared, clenching his fist. \u201cLet me see any man, parochial or extra-parochial, who would presume it, and I\u2019ll tell him he wouldn\u2019t do so twice!\u201d\\n\\nLacking any energetic gestures, the speech might not have flattered the lady\u2019s beauty; but, as Mr. Bumble accompanied it with many martial motions, she was deeply affected, and fervently declared he was indeed a dove.\\n\\nThe dove then flipped up his coat-collar, donned his cocked hat, and, after a lingering and affectionate embrace with his future partner, once more faced the night wind: pausing briefly in the male paupers\u2019 ward to scold them, just to assure himself he possessed the necessary sharpness to be master of the workhouse. Satisfied of his fitness, Mr. Bumble departed with a buoyant heart and bright dreams of advancement that occupied him until he reached the undertaker\u2019s shop.\\n\\nAs Mr. and Mrs. Sowerberry were out to tea and supper, and Noah Claypole was never inclined to exert himself beyond what was necessary for eating and drinking, the shop remained open, though it was past closing time. Mr. Bumble rapped his cane on the counter several times; receiving no answer, and seeing a light shining through the glass of the little parlour window behind the shop, he ventured to peep in\u2014and was considerably astonished by what met his eyes.\"}"
