          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"27691e9b09344c159b097774\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The exquisite gentlemen of the highest breeding wore small dangling trinkets that chimed as they moved with languid grace; these golden chains rang like delicate little bells, and with that tinkling, along with the rustle of silk, brocade, and fine linen, there was a flutter in the air that swept Saint Antoine and his ravenous hunger far away.\\n\\nClothing was the unfailing talisman, the charm that kept everything in its place. Everyone was dressed for a Fancy Ball that would never end. From the Tuileries Palace, through Monseigneur and all the Court, through the Chambers, the courts of justice, and the whole of society (save for the scarecrows), the Fancy Ball extended all the way to the common executioner, who, under the spell, was required to perform his duties \u201ccurled, powdered, in a gold-laced coat, pumps, and white silk stockings.\u201d At the gallows and the wheel\u2014the axe was a rarity\u2014Monsieur Paris, for so his brother professors in the provinces, Monsieur Orleans, and the rest called him in keeping with episcopal custom, presided in this dainty attire. And who among the guests at Monseigneur\u2019s reception in that seventeen-hundred-and-eightieth year of our Lord could possibly doubt that a system rooted in a frizzled hangman, powdered, gold-laced, in pumps and white silk stockings, would outlast the stars themselves?\\n\\nAfter Monseigneur relieved his four bearers of their burdens and took his chocolate, he ordered the doors of the Holiest of Holies thrown open and emerged. Then came such submission, such fawning and groveling, such servility, such abject humiliation! When it came to bowing in body and spirit, nothing was left for Heaven\u2014which may have been one among other reasons why Monseigneur\u2019s worshippers never concerned themselves with it.\\n\\nHanding out a promise here and a smile there, a whisper to one fortunate slave and a wave of the hand to another, Monseigneur graciously moved through his rooms to the distant region of the Circumference of Truth. There, he turned around and came back again, and so, in due time, he had himself shut up in his sanctuary by the chocolate sprites and was seen no more.\\n\\nOnce the spectacle was done, the flutter in the air grew into quite a little storm, and the tiny precious bells went ringing down the stairs. Soon, only one person remained from all the crowd, and he, with his hat under his arm and his snuffbox in hand, slowly passed the mirrors on his way out.\\n\\n\u201cI dedicate you,\u201d he said, stopping at the last door on his way and turning toward the sanctuary, \u201cto the Devil!\u201d\\n\\nWith that, he flicked the snuff from his fingers as though shaking the dust from his feet, and calmly walked downstairs.\"}"
