          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"9842007917f038a1981f7de2\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Well, I said, I needed the watermelon. But he said I didn\u2019t need it to break out of prison with; that was the difference. He said if I\u2019d wanted it to hide a knife and sneak it to Jim to kill the seneskal, that would\u2019ve been fine. So I let it go at that, though I couldn\u2019t see any point in acting like a lawyer if I had to sit around and chew over gold-leaf distinctions every time I saw a chance to grab a watermelon.\\n\\nAnyway, we waited that morning until everybody was busy and no one was around the yard; then Tom carried the sack into the lean-to while I stood off a ways to keep watch. After a while he came out, and we sat on the woodpile to talk. He says:\\n\\n\u201cEverything\u2019s all set now except tools; that\u2019s easy fixed.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTools?\u201d I said.\\n\\n\u201cYeah.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTools for what?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTo dig with. We ain\u2019t going to gnaw him out, are we?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAin\u2019t those old busted picks in there good enough to dig a nigger out with?\u201d I said.\\n\\nHe turned on me, looking so pitying it could make you cry, and says:\\n\\n\u201cHuck Finn, did you ever hear of a prisoner having picks and shovels and all the modern conveniences in his closet to dig himself out with? Now I ask you\u2014if you\u2019ve got any sense at all\u2014what chance would that give him to be a hero? They might as well lend him the key. Picks and shovels\u2014they wouldn\u2019t give them to a king.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell then,\u201d I said, \u201cif we don\u2019t want the picks and shovels, what do we want?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cA couple of case-knives.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTo dig the foundations out from under that cabin with?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cConfound it, it\u2019s foolish, Tom.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt don\u2019t matter how foolish it is, it\u2019s the right way\u2014and the regular way. And there isn\u2019t any other way that I ever heard of, and I\u2019ve read all the books that tell about these things. They always dig out with a case-knife\u2014and not through dirt, either; usually it\u2019s solid rock. And it takes them weeks and weeks and weeks, forever. Why, look at one of those prisoners in the bottom dungeon of the Castle Deef, in the harbor of Marseilles, that dug himself out that way; how long was he at it, do you think?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t know.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, guess.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t know. A month and a half.\u201d\"}"
