          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"4adafc527971266edab5ae33\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Hearing Jim talk like that really hurt me; it dragged him down in my eyes. My conscience started nagging me harder than ever, until finally I said to it, \u201cBack off\u2014it\u2019s not too late yet. I\u2019ll paddle to shore at first light and confess.\u201d Right away I felt calm and happy and light as air. All my worries vanished. I began watching hard for a light and humming to myself. After a while one appeared. Jim called out:\\n\\n\u201cWe\u2019re safe, Huck, we\u2019re safe! Jump up and click your heels! That\u2019s good old Cairo at last, I just know it!\u201d\\n\\nI said:\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019ll take the canoe and go check, Jim. It might not be, you know.\u201d\\n\\nHe jumped up, got the canoe ready, laid his old coat in the bottom for me to sit on, and handed me the paddle; and as I shoved off, he said:\\n\\n\u201cPretty soon I\u2019ll be shouting for joy, and I\u2019ll say it\u2019s all thanks to Huck. I\u2019m a free man, and I never could\u2019ve been free if it hadn\u2019t been for Huck; Huck made it happen. Jim won\u2019t ever forget you, Huck; you\u2019re the best friend Jim\u2019s ever had, and you\u2019re the only friend old Jim\u2019s got now.\u201d\\n\\nI was paddling away, sweating to turn him in; but when he said that, it knocked all the wind out of me. I went slower after that, and I wasn\u2019t sure anymore whether I was glad I\u2019d started or not. When I was fifty yards out, Jim said:\\n\\n\u201cThere you go, the true Huck\u2014the only white gentleman who ever kept his word to old Jim.\u201d\\n\\nI felt downright sick. But I said to myself, I have to do it\u2014I can\u2019t back out. Right then a skiff came along with two men holding guns. They stopped, and I stopped. One of them said:\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s that over there?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cA piece of a raft,\u201d I said.\\n\\n\u201cYou belong on it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAny men on it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOnly one, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, five slaves ran off tonight up the river, above the head of the bend. Is your man white or Black?\u201d\\n\\nI didn\u2019t answer right away. I tried, but the words wouldn\u2019t come. I tried for a couple of seconds to brace myself and say it, but I wasn\u2019t man enough\u2014didn\u2019t have the nerve of a rabbit. I felt myself giving in; so I quit trying, and finally said:\\n\\n\u201cHe\u2019s white.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI guess we\u2019ll go see for ourselves.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI wish you would,\u201d I said, \u201cbecause my pap is the one there, and maybe you could help me tow the raft ashore where the light is.\u201d\"}"
