          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"b2a7575d24057d5d96ba9ba3\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cAll right, I\u2019m agreed. It\u2019s the best plan. Would you just clasp hands and swear that we\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh no, that ain\u2019t fit for this. That\u2019ll do for small, trifling matters\u2014\u2019specially with girls, cuz they\u2019ll double-cross you anyway and chatter if they take offense\u2014but a big business like this needs writing. And blood.\u201d\\n\\nTom\u2019s whole spirit exulted in the notion. It was grim, shadowy, and ominous; the hour, the situation, the setting all matched. He stooped for a clean pine shingle lying in the moonlight, fished a bit of \u201cred keel\u201d from his pocket, set his work so the moon shone on it, and painfully scratched the words, pressing down each slow stroke with his tongue clamped between his teeth and easing up on the way back.\\n\\n\u201cHuck Finn and Tom Sawyer swears they will keep mum about This and They wish They may Drop down dead in Their Tracks if They ever Tell and Rot.\u201d\\n\\nHuckleberry admired Tom\u2019s easy penmanship and the grandeur of his speech. He immediately plucked a pin from his lapel to prick himself, but Tom interrupted:\\n\\n\u201cHold up! Don\u2019t. A pin\u2019s brass\u2014it might have verdigrease on it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s verdigrease?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s poison, that\u2019s what. Just swallow a little once\u2014you\u2019ll find out.\u201d\\n\\nSo Tom unwound the thread off one of his needles, and each boy pricked the pad of his thumb, squeezing out a bead of blood. After much squeezing, Tom managed to write his initials, using his littlest finger\u2019s ball as a pen. Then he showed Huckleberry how to shape an H and an F, and the vow was done. They buried the shingle near the wall with gloomy rites and mutterings, and the chains on their tongues were held to be locked and the key flung away.\\n\\nA shape crept quietly through a gap at the opposite end of the wrecked building just then, but they didn\u2019t notice.\\n\\n\u201cTom,\u201d whispered Huckleberry, \u201cdoes this stop us from ever telling\u2014always?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOf course. No matter what happens, we have to keep quiet. We\u2019d fall dead\u2014don\u2019t you know that?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, I reckon that\u2019s true.\u201d\\n\\nThey kept whispering for quite a while. Soon a dog lifted a long, deathly howl just outside\u2014within ten feet. The boys grabbed each other, stricken with terror.\\n\\n\u201cWhich of us is he after?\u201d panted Huckleberry.\\n\\n\u201cI dunno\u2014look out the crack. Hurry!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, you, Tom!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI can\u2019t\u2014I can\u2019t do it, Huck!\u201d\"}"
