          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"94b5b766aa9a943469567f08\",\"rewritten_text\":\"After dinner the whole gang headed out to the sandbar to hunt for turtle eggs. They jabbed sticks into the sand, and when they hit a soft spot they knelt and dug with their hands. Sometimes they pulled fifty or sixty eggs from a single hole. They looked like perfectly round white balls, just a bit smaller than an English walnut. That night they gorged on fried eggs, and they did it again Friday morning.\\n\\nAfter breakfast they raced out onto the bar, shouting and skipping around, tossing clothes aside until they were naked, then kept up the chase far along the shallow water, pushing against the strong current that kept knocking their legs out from under them and made things even more fun. Every so often they crouched together and slapped water into one another\u2019s faces with their palms, edging closer with their heads turned so the splash wouldn\u2019t choke them, and finally locking arms in a wrestling match until the winner dunked his opponent, then everybody sank into a jumble of pale legs and arms and surfaced all at once, blowing, sputtering, laughing, and gasping.\\n\\nOnce they were worn out, they ran ashore, sprawled on the hot dry sand, and covered themselves with it, only to dash back into the water and repeat the whole show. Eventually it struck them that their bare skin looked a lot like flesh-colored tights, so they drew a ring in the sand and staged a circus\u2014with three clowns, because none of them would surrender the top job.\\n\\nThen they grabbed their marbles and played knucks and ringtaw and keeps until it got boring. Joe and Huck went for another swim, but Tom stayed put; when he kicked off his pants he had also kicked the string of rattlesnake rattles off his ankle, and he couldn\u2019t believe he\u2019d gone so long without cramping up when the charm wasn\u2019t protecting him. He refused to swim again until he found it, and by then the other boys were tired and ready to lounge. Gradually they drifted apart, sank into gloomy moods, and stared longingly across the wide river toward the village dozing in the sun. Tom caught himself tracing \u201cBECKY\u201d in the sand with his big toe; he scraped it away, furious with himself for being soft. Yet he wrote it again; he couldn\u2019t stop. He wiped it out once more, then escaped the temptation by herding the other boys together and joining them.\"}"
