          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"916a2b6245ceef780667c1d2\",\"rewritten_text\":\"His face, burned dark by the sun, was more than half hidden by whiskers and a mustache. He carried a huge oak cudgel, but seemed otherwise unarmed. He bowed awkwardly and gave us a \u201cgood evening\u201d in French accents that, though a bit Neufch\u00e2tel-like, still showed he came from Paris. \\n\\n\u201cSit down, my friend,\u201d said Dupin. \u201cI suppose you\u2019ve come about the Ourang-Outang. Honestly, I almost envy you owning him; he\u2019s a remarkably fine and surely valuable animal. How old do you think he is?\u201d\\n\\nThe sailor drew a long breath, like a man freed from a terrible weight, then answered steadily:\\n\\n\u201cI can\u2019t say exactly\u2014but he can\u2019t be more than four or five years old. Do you have him here?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh no, we had no way to keep him at the house. He\u2019s at a livery stable on the Rue Dubourg, just nearby. You can collect him in the morning. You\u2019re ready, of course, to prove he\u2019s yours?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCertainly I am, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019ll be sorry to let him go,\u201d said Dupin.\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t expect you to go to all this trouble for nothing, sir,\u201d the man replied. \u201cWouldn\u2019t be right. I\u2019m very willing to pay a reward for finding the animal\u2014that is, any reasonable sum.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell,\u201d my friend replied, \u201cthat\u2019s fair enough. Let me think!\u2014what should I want? Oh! I know. My reward will be this. You will give me all the information you can about the murders in the Rue Morgue.\u201d\\n\\nDupin spoke the last words in a very low, calm voice. Just as calmly, he walked to the door, locked it, and put the key in his pocket. Then he drew a pistol from his coat and set it on the table without the slightest fuss.\\n\\nThe sailor\u2019s face went red, as if he were choking. He sprang to his feet and grabbed his cudgel, but the next moment he dropped back into his seat, shaking violently, his face pale as death. He said nothing. I felt deep pity for him.\\n\\n\u201cMy friend,\u201d said Dupin gently, \u201cyou\u2019re frightening yourself for no reason\u2014you truly are. We mean you no harm. I give you my honor as a gentleman and as a Frenchman that we intend you no injury. I know perfectly well that you are innocent of the crimes in the Rue Morgue. Still, you can\u2019t deny that you\u2019re involved to some degree.\u201d\"}"
