          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"dc1f92aa3cb2781e89fdc3b1\",\"rewritten_text\":\"A shade past noon the boys borrowed a small skiff from a townsman who happened to be away, and pushed off right then. Once they were several miles below Cave Hollow, Tom remarked:\\n\\n\u201cNow you notice how this bluff looks the same the whole stretch from the cave hollow\u2014no houses, no wood-yards, bushes all alike. But do you spy that white patch up ahead where a landslide happened? That\u2019s one of my signs. We\u2019ll land there.\u201d\\n\\nThey pulled ashore.\\n\\n\u201cNow, Huck, from where we stand you could touch that hole I escaped by with a fishing pole. Try to find it.\u201d\\n\\nHuck poked around everywhere but saw nothing. Tom strutted into a thick clutch of sumach and announced:\\n\\n\u201cHere she is! Look at it, Huck; it\u2019s the coziest hideout in this country. You just keep still about it. I\u2019ve always wanted to be a robber, but I knew I needed a place like this, and finding it was the tough part. Now we\u2019ve got it, and we\u2019ll keep it secret, except we\u2019ll let Joe Harper and Ben Rogers know\u2014because of course there\u2019s got to be a gang, or there\u2019s no style in it. Tom Sawyer\u2019s Gang\u2014it sounds grand, doesn\u2019t it, Huck?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt sure does, Tom. Who are we going to rob?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, near anybody. Waylay folks\u2014that\u2019s the chief way.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd kill them?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, not every time. Pen them in the cave till they fetch a ransom.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s a ransom?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMoney. You make them wring all they can out of their friends; and after you\u2019ve held them a year, if it ain\u2019t paid, then you kill them. That\u2019s the usual rule. Only you don\u2019t kill the women. You lock up the women, but you don\u2019t kill them. They\u2019re always beautiful and rich and scared half to death. You take their watches and things, but you always lift your hat and talk proper. Nobody\u2019s as polite as robbers\u2014you\u2019ll find that in any book. Well, the women fall in love with you, and after they\u2019ve been in the cave a week or two they quit crying, and then you couldn\u2019t chase them away. If you drove them off they\u2019d whirl around and come back. That\u2019s how it goes in all the books.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, that\u2019s real bully, Tom. I reckon it beats being a pirate.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, it\u2019s better in some fashions, because it keeps you near home and circuses and such.\u201d\\n\\nBy then everything was set and the boys slipped into the hole, Tom leading. They worked their way to the tunnel\u2019s far end, made their spliced kite-string fast, and continued on.\"}"
