          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"f86d1d4fc16f0c9e3bec8b36\",\"rewritten_text\":\"It seemed a maze of back alleys, drains, and tiny gardens, having the look of a somewhat dreary retreat. Wemmick\u2019s dwelling was a small wooden cottage amid garden plots, its roof trimmed and painted like a gun battery.\\n\\n\u201cAll my own work,\u201d said Wemmick. \u201cPretty, isn\u2019t it?\u201d\\n\\nI praised it heartily; it must have been the tiniest house I\u2019d ever seen, with the oddest Gothic windows (most of them mere make-believe) and a Gothic door hardly large enough to squeeze through.\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s a genuine flagstaff, you observe,\u201d Wemmick continued, \u201cand on Sundays I send up an actual flag. Now look. Once I cross this bridge, I haul it up\u2014so\u2014and break the connection.\u201d\\n\\nThe bridge was just a plank over a trench about four feet wide and two deep. But it was delightful to watch him raising it and securing it in place, smiling with relish, not just as a rote performance.\\n\\n\u201cAt nine each evening, Greenwich time,\u201d said Wemmick, \u201cthe gun fires. There he stands, you know! And when you hear him go, I believe you\u2019ll admit he\u2019s a real Stinger.\u201d\\n\\nThe artillery in question was set up in a separate little fort of lattice-work, shielded from the weather by an ingenious tarpaulin gadget resembling an umbrella.\\n\\n\u201cThen, behind,\u201d Wemmick went on, \u201cout of sight, so the notion of fortifications isn\u2019t spoiled\u2014because my rule is, if you have a notion, carry it through and maintain it\u2014I\u2019m not sure if you agree\u2014\u201d\\n\\nI assured him I did.\\n\\n\u201c\u2014Behind, there\u2019s a pig, and there are chickens and rabbits; then I knock together a small frame, you see, and raise cucumbers; and at supper you\u2019ll decide what manner of salad I can provide. So, sir,\u201d said Wemmick, smiling yet grave as he shook his head, \u201cif you can imagine the little place under siege, it would hold out an extraordinary while for provisions.\u201d\\n\\nHe then led me to a bower about twelve yards away, though the path was so cleverly wound that it took quite a while to reach; there our glasses stood ready. Our punch cooled in an ornamental pool beside which the bower was built. This circular piece of water\u2014with an island in the midst that might have supplied the evening salad\u2014held a fountain he had devised, which, when you set a small mill spinning and pulled a cork from a pipe, spouted so vigorously it dampened the back of one\u2019s hand.\"}"
