          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"a444bd4718ed5f8252d2852e\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Raymond paced angrily up and down the room. I stood ready to receive and answer his accusations. Adrian leaned against the wall. \u201cThis is utterly ridiculous,\u201d he said. \u201cYou couldn\u2019t behave more unreasonably if you were schoolboys.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou don\u2019t understand,\u201d said Raymond. \u201cThis is just one part of a whole system\u2014a plan of tyranny I\u2019ll never submit to. Because I\u2019m Protector of England, am I supposed to be the only slave in the empire? My privacy invaded, my actions criticized, my friends insulted? No, I\u2019ll rid myself of all of it. Bear witness.\u201d He removed the star, the badge of his office, from his chest and threw it on the table. \u201cI renounce my office. I give up my power\u2014let anyone else take it!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLet him take it,\u201d Adrian cried, \u201cif he can claim\u2014and if the world will acknowledge\u2014that he\u2019s your superior. There isn\u2019t a man in England presumptuous enough. Know yourself, Raymond, and your anger will end; your calm will return. A few months ago, whenever we prayed for the prosperity of our country or ourselves, we simultaneously prayed for the life and well-being of the Protector, inseparably tied to us. Your hours were dedicated to our benefit, your ambition was to win our approval. You adorned our towns with public buildings, bestowed useful institutions, and gave the land abundant fertility. The powerful and unjust shrank from judgment at your tribunal, and the poor and oppressed rose like morning flowers in the sunlight of your protection.\\n\\n\u201cCan you wonder that we\u2019re all shocked and sorrowful when this seems changed? But come, this splenetic mood has already passed; resume your duties. Your supporters will cheer you, your enemies will be silenced, and our love, honour, and loyalty will be shown to you again. Master yourself, Raymond, and the world will be yours.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll this would make perfect sense if you were talking to someone else,\u201d Raymond replied sullenly. \u201cLearn the lesson yourself, and you, the first noble in the land, might become its ruler. You, the good, wise, and just, could command every heart. But I see too soon for my own happiness, and too late for England\u2019s good, that I took on a task beyond me. I can\u2019t control myself. My passions are my masters; even my smallest impulse tyrannises over me. Do you think I renounced the Protectorate\u2014and I have renounced it\u2014in a fit of bad temper? By the living God, I swear never to take up that bauble again, never again to burden myself with the weight of care and misery represented by that symbol.\u201d\"}"
