          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"66ec2d4561ab23aed01c6c72\",\"rewritten_text\":\"With everything settled so pleasantly, they sealed the agreement with another teacup of peppermint drink; the lady needed it, as her nerves were fluttering. While they sipped, she told Mr. Bumble that the old woman had died.\\n\\n\u201cVery good,\u201d said Mr. Bumble, tasting the peppermint. \u201cI\u2019ll stop at Sowerberry\u2019s on my way home, and tell him to send first thing tomorrow. Was that the thing that frightened you, my love?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt wasn\u2019t anything specific, dear,\u201d the lady answered, dodging the question.\\n\\n\u201cIt must have been something, love,\u201d Mr. Bumble insisted. \u201cWon\u2019t you tell your own B.?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot now,\u201d she replied. \u201cOne day. After we\u2019re married, dear.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAfter we\u2019re married!\u201d cried Mr. Bumble. \u201cIt wasn\u2019t any rudeness from any of the male paupers\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, no, love!\u201d she cut in quickly.\\n\\n\u201cIf I thought it was,\u201d Mr. Bumble went on, \u201cif I thought any of them dared to raise their coarse eyes to that lovely face\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThey wouldn\u2019t have dared, love,\u201d the lady answered.\\n\\n\u201cThey\u2019d better not!\u201d said Mr. Bumble, clenching his fist. \u201cLet me see any man, parish or not, who would dare, and I promise he wouldn\u2019t try twice!\u201d\\n\\nWithout his energetic gestures, this might not have sounded like much of a compliment, but as Mr. Bumble acted out his threat with a bold display, she was deeply moved by this proof of his devotion and declared, admiringly, that he was a dove.\\n\\nThe dove then flipped up his coat collar and set his cocked hat on his head. After he and his future wife shared a long and loving embrace, he faced the cold night again, pausing only a few minutes in the male paupers\u2019 ward to scold them, satisfying himself that he had the right sharpness to be workhouse-master. Confident in his fitness, Mr. Bumble left the building lighthearted, filled with bright dreams of his future rise, and these thoughts carried him along until he reached the undertaker\u2019s shop.\\n\\nMr. and Mrs. Sowerberry had gone out for tea and supper, and Noah Claypole was never eager to exert himself beyond what was needed for eating and drinking, so the shop remained open even though it was past closing time. Mr. Bumble rapped his cane on the counter several times; getting no response, and seeing a light glowing through the glass window of the little parlor behind the shop, he boldly peeked in to see what was happening, and what he saw surprised him greatly.\"}"
