          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"de72aaa7f09b1ca14320dd69\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cNever,\u201d the girl replied. \u201cWhy not?\u201d \u201cFor one reason,\u201d she answered firmly, \u201cbecause that lady knows and will stand by me\u2014I know she will, because she promised me she would. And also, because although he\u2019s lived a wicked life, I\u2019ve led a wicked life too. There are plenty of us who\u2019ve walked the same paths together, and I won\u2019t betray them. Any one of them could have turned on me but didn\u2019t, bad as they may be.\u201d \u201cThen,\u201d said the gentleman quickly, as if this was what he\u2019d been hoping for, \u201chand Monks over to me and let me deal with him.\u201d \u201cWhat if he turns on the others?\u201d \u201cI promise you, if the truth is forced out of him, that\u2019s where it ends. There must be parts of Oliver\u2019s story that would be painful to expose publicly, and if the truth comes out, the rest will go free.\u201d \u201cAnd if it doesn\u2019t?\u201d the girl asked. \u201cThen,\u201d the gentleman continued, \u201cFagin won\u2019t be brought to justice without your consent. In that case I could give you reasons that I believe would persuade you.\u201d \u201cDo I have the lady\u2019s promise on that?\u201d the girl asked. \u201cYou do,\u201d Rose replied. \u201cMy true and faithful pledge.\u201d \u201cMonks would never find out how you learned what you know?\u201d the girl asked after a brief pause. \u201cNever,\u201d said the gentleman. \u201cThe information would be used so that he could never even suspect.\u201d \u201cI\u2019ve been a liar, and among liars since I was a child,\u201d said the girl after another quiet moment, \u201cbut I\u2019ll take you at your word.\u201d After both assured her she could, she spoke in a voice so low it was often hard for the listener to catch the meaning, describing by name and location the tavern she\u2019d been followed from that night. From her occasional pauses, it seemed the gentleman was making quick notes of what she was sharing. When she had explained the layout, the best place to watch without being noticed, and the night and hour Monks usually went there, she stopped to think, trying to bring his features and manner more clearly to mind. \u201cHe\u2019s tall,\u201d said the girl, \u201cstrongly built but not heavy. He has a stealthy way of walking, and as he walks, he keeps looking over his shoulder, first one way, then the other.\u201d\"}"
