          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"b9a50d0fd6e708789e80cf09\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cSo now I own some knights,\u201d I said as we rode off. \u201cWho would have thought I\u2019d live to count assets like that? I\u2019ve no idea what to do with them unless I raffle them off. How many are there, Sandy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSeven, please you, sir, and their squires.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cA good haul. Who are they? Where do they hang out?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhere do they hang out?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, where do they live?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAh, I understood thee not. I will tell thee soon.\u201d Then she murmured softly, tasting the words like they were sweets. \u201cHang they out\u2014hang they out\u2014where hang\u2014where do they hang out; yes, just so; where do they hang out. Truly the phrase has a pleasing grace and is prettily turned. I will repeat it again and again in my idleness, and perhaps I shall learn it. Where do they hang out. Indeed! it already slips lightly from my tongue, and since\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t forget the cowboys, Sandy.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCowboys?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, the knights, remember? You were going to tell me about them a moment ago. Figuratively speaking, play ball.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGame\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, yes, yes! Step up to the plate. I mean get to work on the facts, and don\u2019t waste so much kindling to start the fire. Tell me about the knights.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI will, and lightly begin. So they two departed and rode into a great forest. And\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGreat Scott!\u201d\\n\\nYou see, I saw my mistake at once. I had set her machinery going; it was my fault; she would take thirty days to reach the point. She usually started without any introduction and stopped without giving the result. If you interrupted, she either kept going as if nothing happened or answered with a couple of words and then backed up and repeated the sentence. So interruptions only made it worse; yet I had to interrupt, and fairly often, to save my life; a person would die if that monotony dripped on him all day.\\n\\n\u201cGreat Scott!\u201d I said, miserable. She merely went back and began again:\\n\\n\u201cSo they two departed and rode into a great forest. And\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhich two?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSir Gawaine and Sir Uwaine. So they came to an abbey of monks and were well lodged there. In the morning they heard mass in the abbey, and then they rode on till they came to a great forest; then Sir Gawaine saw in a valley near a tower twelve fair damsels and two knights armed on great horses, and the damsels moved to and fro by a tree.\u201d\"}"
