          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"9cc0648a1bdab5e75b598da5\",\"rewritten_text\":\"And if he pressed me for the reason I wanted it, and questioned my right to it, I would tell him\u2014however little he valued such meagre visions\u2014that I had loved Estella devotedly and for a long time, and that though I had lost her and must go on in bereavement, anything touching her was still dearer and nearer to me than all else on earth. Seeing Mr. Jaggers remain motionless, mute, and seemingly implacable before this appeal, I turned to Wemmick and said, \u201cWemmick, I know you for a man of kindly heart. I have seen your cheerful house, your aged father, and all the innocent, lively, playful ways with which you lighten your business existence. I beg you to speak for me to Mr. Jaggers, and tell him that, given every circumstance, he ought to be more open with me!\u201d\\n\\nNever had I witnessed two men stare at each other more strangely than Mr. Jaggers and Wemmick did after that invocation. For an instant I feared Wemmick would be dismissed on the spot; but the fear faded as I observed Mr. Jaggers relax into the semblance of a smile, while Wemmick gained courage.\\n\\n\u201cWhat is all this?\u201d demanded Mr. Jaggers. \u201cYou with an aged father, and you with pleasant, playful ways?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell!\u201d Wemmick answered. \u201cIf I don\u2019t bring them here, where is the harm?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cPip,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, laying his hand on my arm and smiling outright, \u201cthis fellow must be the craftiest impostor in London.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot in the least,\u201d retorted Wemmick, growing more valiant. \u201cI think you\u2019re the impostor.\u201d\\n\\nAgain they traded those former odd looks, each seemingly still unsure whether the other was deceiving him.\\n\\n\u201cYou, with a pleasant home?\u201d said Mr. Jaggers.\\n\\n\u201cSo long as it doesn\u2019t meddle with business,\u201d Wemmick replied, \u201clet it remain. Now that I study you, sir, I shouldn\u2019t be surprised if you were scheming to secure a comfortable home of your own one of these days, when you\u2019ve had enough of all this toil.\u201d\\n\\nMr. Jaggers tilted his head backward two or three times, as though in review, and even drew a sigh. \u201cPip,\u201d he said, \u201clet\u2019s leave off talking of \u2018poor dreams;\u2019 you know more about such matters than I do, having much fresher dealings with them. But now, concerning this other business. I\u2019ll put a case to you. Mind! I admit nothing.\u201d\\n\\nHe paused for me to assure him that I thoroughly understood he expressly admitted nothing.\\n\\n\u201cNow, Pip,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, \u201ctake this case. Imagine that a woman, under the circumstances you have described, concealed her child, and was obliged to disclose the fact to her legal adviser, after he insisted he must know, in view of the latitude of his defence, exactly how the fact stood regarding that child.\u201d\"}"
