          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"1cc7ad0724fab9c3ff83c263\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cNo bringing up by hand then. Not a bit of it!\u201d\\n\\nJoe offered me more gravy, which I was afraid to take.\\n\\n\u201cHe was a world of trouble to you, ma\u2019am,\u201d said Mrs. Hubble, sympathizing with my sister.\\n\\n\u201cTrouble?\u201d echoed my sister; \u201ctrouble?\u201d She launched into a terrifying list of every illness I had caused, every sleepless night I had given her, every high place I had fallen from, every low place I had fallen into, every injury I had inflicted on myself, and all the times she had wished me dead while I stubbornly refused to die.\\n\\nI think the Romans must have annoyed each other terribly with their noses. Perhaps that was why they were such a restless people. In any case, Mr. Wopsle\u2019s Roman nose irritated me so much during this recital of my misconduct that I wanted to pull it until he howled. But everything I had suffered so far was nothing compared with the awful feeling that seized me when the silence following my sister\u2019s speech was broken, during which everyone had looked at me, as I felt painfully aware, with indignation and disgust.\\n\\n\u201cYet,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, gently steering the company back to the earlier topic, \u201cpork\u2014considered as boiled\u2014is rich, too, isn\u2019t it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHave a little brandy, uncle,\u201d said my sister.\\n\\nO Heavens, it had come at last! He would find it weak, he would say it was weak, and I was doomed! I clutched the leg of the table under the cloth with both hands and waited for my fate.\\n\\nMy sister went for the stone bottle, returned with it, and poured his brandy, no one else taking any. The wretched man toyed with his glass\u2014picked it up, held it to the light, set it down\u2014dragging out my torment. Meanwhile Mrs. Joe and Joe briskly cleared the table for the pie and pudding.\\n\\nI couldn\u2019t take my eyes off him. Still gripping the table leg with hands and feet, I watched the miserable man play with his glass, lift it, smile, tilt back his head, and drink the brandy. Immediately after, the company was seized with indescribable alarm as he sprang to his feet, spun around several times in a terrifying, spasmodic whooping-cough dance, and bolted out the door; then he appeared through the window, violently spluttering and spitting, making the most hideous faces, and seeming completely out of his senses.\\n\\nI held on tight while Mrs. Joe and Joe ran after him.\"}"
        }
