          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"c40ab4cece89d2611ee55551\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cOh, I misunderstood you. I thought you said \u2018anybody,\u2019 and of course I figured \u2018anybody\u2019 meant\u2014well, anybody; basically, everyone.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt does\u2014anyone of noble birth, and especially if he is royal.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat seems reasonable,\u201d said the abbot, seeing his chance to calm things down and avoid a disaster, \u201cbecause it would hardly make sense that such a marvelous gift would be granted to reveal matters concerning people less exalted than those born close to greatness. Our Arthur the king\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWould you know of him?\u201d interrupted the enchanter.\\n\\n\u201cMost gladly, yes, and gratefully.\u201d\\n\\nEveryone was awestruck and fascinated again right away, the hopeless fools. They watched the spells intently, and looked at me with a \u201cWell, what do you say to that?\u201d expression when the announcement came:\\n\\n\u201cThe king is tired from the hunt and has lain in his palace for two hours, sleeping dreamlessly.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGod bless him!\u201d said the abbot, crossing himself. \u201cMay that sleep refresh his body and soul.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd so it might, if he were sleeping,\u201d I said, \u201cbut the king is not sleeping; the king rides.\u201d\\n\\nHere was trouble again\u2014a clash of authorities. No one knew which of us to believe; I still had a bit of reputation left. The magician\u2019s scorn rose, and he said:\\n\\n\u201cLo, I have seen many marvelous seers and prophets and magicians in my life, but never one before who could sit idle and see into things without any incantation to aid him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou have lived in the woods and missed much because of it. I use incantations myself, as this good brotherhood knows\u2014but only on truly important occasions.\u201d\\n\\nWhen it comes to sarcasm, I can handle my end. That jab made him squirm. The abbot asked about the queen and the court, and got this answer:\\n\\n\u201cThey all sleep, being exhausted, like the king.\u201d\\n\\nI said:\\n\\n\u201cThat is just another lie. Half of them are busy with their entertainments, the queen and the rest are not sleeping; they ride. Now maybe you can show off a bit more and tell us where the king and queen and everyone riding with them are headed this moment?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThey sleep now, as I said; but tomorrow they will ride, for they go on a journey toward the sea.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd where will they be the day after tomorrow at vespers?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFar north of Camelot, with half their journey done.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat is another lie, out by a hundred and fifty miles.\u201d\"}"
        }
