          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"28ab978de5d751faa7f90caf\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Yet for all her efforts, the boy grew gloomier, paler, and more downcast. She tried hot baths, sitz baths, showers, and plunges. The boy stayed as mournful as a hearse. She added a thin oatmeal diet and blister plasters to help the water cures. She measured his capacity like a jug\u2019s and filled him daily with bogus remedies.\\n\\nTom had grown numb to her punishments. This stage terrified the old lady. She had to break this indifference at any cost. When she first heard of Pain-killer, she ordered a supply. She tasted it and felt grateful; it was fire in liquid form. She abandoned water treatments and everything else, and put all her faith in Pain-killer. She gave Tom a teaspoonful and waited anxiously. Her worries vanished and her soul relaxed, because the indifference was gone. The boy could not have shown more wild interest if she had lit a fire under him.\\n\\nTom realized it was time to stir things up. Life in his supposedly delicate state might seem dramatic, but it was growing drearily busy and chaotic. He considered many plans and settled on pretending to love Pain-killer. He asked for it so often that he became a pest, and his aunt finally told him to help himself and stop pestering her. If it had been Sid, she would have been joyful without doubt; but because it was Tom, she watched the bottle in secret. She noticed the medicine really was disappearing, but never guessed he was doctoring a crack in the sitting-room floor with it.\\n\\nOne day Tom was pouring a dose into the crack when his aunt\u2019s yellow cat strolled up, purring, eyeing the spoon greedily, and begging for a taste. Tom said:\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t ask if you don\u2019t want it, Peter.\u201d\\n\\nBut Peter insisted he did want it.\\n\\n\u201cYou better be sure.\u201d\\n\\nPeter was sure.\\n\\n\u201cNow you\u2019ve asked for it, and I\u2019ll give it to you, because I\u2019m not mean; but if you don\u2019t like it, don\u2019t blame anyone but yourself.\u201d\\n\\nPeter agreed. Tom pried his mouth open and poured in the Pain-killer. Peter leaped two yards into the air, let out a war whoop, and tore around the room, crashing into furniture, knocking over flowerpots, and causing general destruction.\"}"
