          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"f2f0ab4450c8670316c9645a\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWell, everybody does it that way, Huck.\u201d \u201cTom, that don\u2019t make any difference. I\u2019m not everybody, and I can\u2019t stand it. It\u2019s terrible to be tied down like that. And the food comes too easy\u2014I can\u2019t even enjoy eating when it\u2019s like that. I have to ask to go fishing; I have to ask to go swimming\u2014blast it, I have to ask to do everything. I had to speak so proper it wasn\u2019t any fun\u2014I had to go up to the attic and let loose a while every day just to get a taste of my old self, or I\u2019d have died, Tom. The widow wouldn\u2019t let me smoke; she wouldn\u2019t let me yell, or yawn, or stretch, or scratch in front of people.\u201d He flared up again. \u201cAnd darn it, she prayed all the time! I never saw such a woman! I had to bolt, Tom\u2014I just had to. Besides, that school was about to open, and I\u2019d have had to go to it\u2014well, I wouldn\u2019t stand that, Tom. Look here, Tom, being rich isn\u2019t what it\u2019s cracked up to be. It\u2019s just worry and sweat, and wishing you were dead all the time. These clothes suit me, and this barrel suits me, and I\u2019m never letting them go again. Tom, I wouldn\u2019t have got into all this trouble if it wasn\u2019t for that money; now you take my share along with yours, and give me a dime now and then\u2014not too often, because I don\u2019t care for anything unless it\u2019s kind of hard to get\u2014and you go beg off for me with the widow.\u201d \u201cOh, Huck, you know I can\u2019t do that. It isn\u2019t fair; besides, if you try this just a little longer you\u2019ll come to like it.\u201d \u201cLike it! Sure\u2014as if I\u2019d like sitting on a hot stove long enough. No, Tom, I won\u2019t be rich, and I won\u2019t live in those cursed stuffy houses. I like the woods, and the river, and hogsheads, and I\u2019ll stick to them. Confound it! Just when we had guns, and a cave, and everything ready for robbing, this foolishness had to mess it all up!\u201d Tom saw his chance. \u201cLook here, Huck, being rich isn\u2019t going to stop me from turning robber.\u201d \u201cNo! Oh, good gracious! Are you serious, Tom?\u201d \u201cJust as serious as I\u2019m sitting here. But Huck, we can\u2019t let you into the gang if you aren\u2019t respectable, you know.\u201d Huck\u2019s joy died out. \u201cYou can\u2019t let me in, Tom?\u201d\"}"
