          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"cd8e3dfc9455ae6bc8da20bc\",\"rewritten_text\":\"I examined the skull drawing closely. The outer lines, the ones nearest the edge of the vellum, were much clearer than the rest. It was obvious the heat had affected the parchment unevenly. I quickly lit a fire and held every part of the parchment over the flames. At first, only the faint lines of the skull grew darker, but after I kept at it, a figure appeared in the corner opposite the skull. At first I thought it was a goat, but on closer inspection I saw it was meant to be a kid.\\n\\n\u201cHa! ha!\u201d I said. \u201cI shouldn\u2019t laugh\u2014a million and a half is no laughing matter\u2014but you can\u2019t add a third link to your chain. You won\u2019t find any real connection between pirates and a goat. Pirates have nothing to do with goats; they\u2019re for farmers.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut I just said the figure was not a goat.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, a kid then\u2014almost the same thing.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAlmost, but not quite,\u201d said Legrand. \u201cYou may have heard of Captain Kidd. I saw the animal figure as a pun or a symbolic signature. I call it a signature because its position suggested that idea. The skull in the opposite corner had the appearance of a stamp or seal. Still, I was annoyed by the lack of everything else\u2014the body of my imagined instrument\u2014the text for my context.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI suppose you expected to find a letter between the seal and the signature.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSomething like that. The truth is, I had a strong feeling that some great fortune was coming. I can hardly explain why. Maybe it was more desire than belief. Still, do you know that Jupiter\u2019s foolish claim that the bug was solid gold had a surprising effect on my imagination? And then there were all the strange accidents and coincidences. Consider how accidental it was that everything happened on the only day cool enough for a fire, and that without the fire, or without the dog showing up exactly when he did, I never would have noticed the skull, and thus never found the treasure.\u201d\"}"
