          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"d2a50de3e67c2ef67c918857\",\"rewritten_text\":\"About ten minutes later the bell rang for tea, and, when Virginia did not come down, Mrs. Otis sent a footman to fetch her. After a little while he returned saying he could not find Miss Virginia anywhere. Since Virginia usually went into the garden every evening to gather flowers for the dinner table, Mrs. Otis was not worried at first, but when six o\u2019clock struck and Virginia still did not appear, she grew truly alarmed. She sent the boys out to search while she and Mr. Otis went through every room in the house. At half-past six the boys came back reporting they had found no trace of their sister. Everyone was now extremely agitated and unsure what to do, when Mr. Otis suddenly remembered that a few days earlier he had allowed a band of gypsies to camp in the park. He at once set off for Blackfell Hollow, where he knew they were staying, taking his eldest son and two farmhands. The little Duke of Cheshire, frantic with worry, begged to go too, but Mr. Otis refused, fearing there might be a fight. When they arrived, however, they saw the gypsies were gone, and from the burning fire and plates lying on the grass it was clear they had left in a hurry. Mr. Otis sent Washington and the two men to comb the district, then ran home and sent telegrams to every police inspector in the county, warning them to watch for a young girl who might have been kidnapped by tramps or gypsies. He ordered his horse, insisted his wife and the three boys sit down to dinner, and rode off down the Ascot Road with a groom. He had scarcely gone two miles when he heard someone galloping behind him. Looking back, he saw the little Duke riding up on his pony, face flushed and bareheaded. \u201cI\u2019m terribly sorry, Mr. Otis,\u201d the boy gasped, \u201cbut I can\u2019t eat any dinner while Virginia is missing. Please don\u2019t be angry; if you had let us be engaged last year, none of this would have happened. You won\u2019t send me back, will you? I can\u2019t go! I won\u2019t go!\u201d\\n\\nThe Minister could not help smiling at the handsome young rascal and was moved by his devotion to Virginia. Leaning down from his horse, he patted the boy kindly on the shoulders and said, \u201cWell, Cecil, if you won\u2019t go back, I suppose you must come with me, but I\u2019ll have to get you a hat at Ascot.\u201d\"}"
