          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"21722e3cc87e7aaa847f00ed\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cYes, it is\u2014and I could have had it if I\u2019d been big enough. I saw him first. Who caught him?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt was an old stranger, and he sold his claim for forty dollars because he has to go up the river and can\u2019t wait. Think of that! I\u2019d wait seven years if I had to.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s me every time,\u201d I said. \u201cBut maybe his claim isn\u2019t worth more than that if he\u2019d sell it so cheap. Maybe something isn\u2019t right.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut it is, straight as a string. I saw the handbill myself. It tells every detail\u2014describes him like a picture and names the plantation he\u2019s from below New Orleans. No trouble with that deal, you can bet. Say, give me a chew of tobacco, will you?\u201d\\n\\nI didn\u2019t have any, so he left. I went to the raft and sat down in the wigwam to think, but I couldn\u2019t figure anything out. I thought till my head hurt, yet I couldn\u2019t see a way out of the mess. After this long trip, and after all we\u2019d done for those scoundrels, everything was ruined. They had the heart to trick Jim like that and make him a slave for life among strangers, for forty dirty dollars.\\n\\nOnce I told myself it would be a thousand times better for Jim to be a slave at home with his family, if he had to be one, and I ought to write Tom Sawyer to tell Miss Watson where he was. But I dropped that notion for two reasons: she\u2019d be furious at his rascality and ungratefulness in running off, and she\u2019d sell him down the river again; and even if she didn\u2019t, everyone naturally despises an ungrateful slave, and they\u2019d make Jim feel it till he felt mean and ashamed. And then think of me! Word would spread that Huck Finn helped a slave to get his freedom, and if I ever saw anyone from that town again I\u2019d be ready to kneel and lick his boots from shame. That\u2019s how it goes: a person does a low-down thing and doesn\u2019t want the consequences. Figures if he can hide it, it isn\u2019t a disgrace. That was exactly my fix. The more I studied on it, the more my conscience ground me, and the more wicked and low and mean I felt.\"}"
        }
      ],
