          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"83d00f0a6df161207c4e9c75\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWhat\u2019s going on?\u201d Oliver demanded.\\n\\n\u201cQuiet!\u201d the Dodger whispered. \u201cDo you see that old fellow at the bookstall?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThe old gentleman across the way?\u201d said Oliver. \u201cYes, I see him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHe\u2019ll do,\u201d said the Dodger.\\n\\n\u201cA perfect setup,\u201d added Master Charley Bates.\\n\\nOliver looked from one to the other in utter astonishment, but he had no chance to ask anything; the two boys slipped silently across the street and crept up behind the old gentleman who had caught Oliver\u2019s attention. Oliver followed a few steps, uncertain whether to go forward or back, and stood there, watching in stunned silence.\\n\\nThe old gentleman looked thoroughly respectable, with powdered hair and gold spectacles. He wore a bottle-green coat with a black velvet collar, white trousers, and carried a stylish bamboo cane under his arm. He had picked up a book at the stall and stood there reading as intently as if he were in his own study chair. He might well have imagined himself there, for from his deep absorption it was obvious he noticed neither the stall, nor the street, nor the boys\u2014nothing but the book. He read straight on, turning the page when he reached the bottom, starting at the top of the next, proceeding steadily with keen interest.\\n\\nImagine Oliver\u2019s horror and panic, standing a few paces away with eyes stretched wide, when he saw the Dodger plunge his hand into the old gentleman\u2019s pocket and pull out a handkerchief! He saw him pass it to Charley Bates; then, to cap it all, watched them both tear away around the corner at full speed.\\n\\nIn a flash, the entire secret of the handkerchiefs, the watches, the jewels, and the Jew crashed into Oliver\u2019s mind.\\n\\nFor a moment he stood frozen, blood surging through his veins in terror until he felt as if he were being scorched. Then, dazed and frightened, he bolted, running as fast as his legs could carry him without any idea of what he was doing.\\n\\nIt all happened in a single minute. Just as Oliver began to run, the old gentleman, reaching for his pocket and missing his handkerchief, spun around. Seeing Oliver sprinting away at such a pace, he naturally assumed the boy was the thief; shouting \u201cStop thief!\u201d with all his strength, he sprinted after him, book still in hand.\"}"
        }
