          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"1701c8ae600ade4ca15bf174\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cDo you play?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI think,\u201d said the spy in his humblest tone as he turned to Mr. Lorry, \u201cI may appeal to a gentleman of your age and kindness to ask this other gentleman, much younger than you, how he can under any circumstances justify playing that Ace he mentioned. I admit that I am a spy, and that it is seen as a shameful job\u2014though someone must do it. But this gentleman is no spy, so why should he lower himself to become one?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI play my Ace, Mr. Barsad,\u201d said Carton, taking the answer himself and glancing at his watch, \u201cwithout hesitation, in just a few minutes.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI had hoped, gentlemen both,\u201d said the spy, still trying to pull Mr. Lorry into the talk, \u201cthat your respect for my sister\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI could show no greater respect for your sister than by finally freeing her from her brother,\u201d said Sydney Carton.\\n\\n\u201cYou don\u2019t think so, sir?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI am completely sure of it.\u201d\\n\\nThe spy\u2019s smooth manner, oddly at odds with his showy rough clothes and probably with his usual behavior, met such a barrier in Carton\u2019s unreadable face\u2014so puzzling even to wiser and more honest men than he\u2014that it faltered and failed him. While he hesitated, Carton said, returning to his earlier air of studying cards:\\n\\n\u201cAnd now that I think of it again, I strongly suspect I have another good card here, not yet mentioned. That friend and fellow-Sheep who said he was grazing in the country prisons; who was he?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFrench. You don\u2019t know him,\u201d said the spy quickly.\\n\\n\u201cFrench, eh?\u201d repeated Carton, thinking, seeming not to notice him, though he echoed the word. \u201cWell, he may be.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHe is, I assure you,\u201d said the spy; \u201cthough it doesn\u2019t matter.\u201d\\n\\n\u201c\u2018Though it doesn\u2019t matter,\u2019\u201d repeated Carton in the same mechanical tone\u2014\u201c\u2018though it doesn\u2019t matter\u2019\u2014No, it doesn\u2019t matter. No. Yet I know the face.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI think not. I\u2019m sure not. It can\u2019t be,\u201d said the spy.\\n\\n\u201cIt can\u2019t be,\u201d muttered Sydney Carton, looking back and idly turning his glass (which, fortunately, was a small one) again. \u201cCan\u2019t be. Spoke good French. Yet like a foreigner, I thought?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cProvincial,\u201d said the spy.\\n\\n\u201cNo. Foreign!\u201d cried Carton, striking his open hand on the table as a clear idea broke in his mind. \u201cCly! Disguised, but the same man. We had him before us at the Old Bailey.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNow there you are hasty, sir,\u201d said Barsad, with a smile that pushed his aquiline nose even more to one side; \u201cthere you really give me an advantage over you.\u201d\"}"
