          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"49cf4d77a1ca368882012087\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cIf I can\u2019t live on that, I won\u2019t ask anyone to help me. Is that good enough?\u201d\\n\\nThere was an enormous roar of applause, and above it the king\u2019s voice rang out:\\n\\n\u201cUnbind him and set him free! Give him homage, high and low, rich and poor, for he has become the king\u2019s right hand, clothed with power and authority, seated on the highest step of the throne! Now sweep away this creeping night and bring back light and cheer, so the whole world may bless you.\u201d\\n\\nBut I answered:\\n\\n\u201cIt is nothing for a common man to be shamed in front of the world; but it would dishonor the king if those who saw his minister stripped did not also see him restored from that shame. If I may ask for my clothes to be brought back\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThey\u2019re not fit,\u201d the king interrupted. \u201cFetch other garments; dress him like a prince!\u201d\\n\\nMy plan was working. I needed everything to remain as it was until the eclipse was total, otherwise they would press me again to chase away the darkness, and of course I couldn\u2019t. Sending for clothes bought some time, but not enough. So I had to come up with another excuse. I said it would be natural if the king regretted, even a little, what he had done in his excitement; therefore I would let the darkness deepen a while, and if, after a reasonable time, the king held to his decision, the darkness would be lifted. Neither the king nor anyone else liked that, but I had to stand my ground.\\n\\nIt grew darker and darker, blacker and blacker, while I fought with those clumsy sixth-century clothes. Finally it was pitch black, and the crowd groaned in horror as the cold, otherworldly night breeze swept through and the stars came out and flickered in the sky. At last the eclipse was total, and I was very glad, though everyone else was miserable, which made perfect sense. I said:\\n\\n\u201cThe king, by his silence, still agrees to the terms.\u201d Then I raised my hands\u2014held them that way a moment\u2014and said with the gravest solemnity, \u201cLet the enchantment dissolve and fade away without harm!\u201d\\n\\nThere was no response, at first, in that deep darkness and that graveyard hush. But when the silver rim of the sun slid out a moment later, the crowd erupted with a massive shout and surged down like a flood to bury me in blessings and gratitude\u2014and Clarence was certainly not last in that tide.\"}"
        }
      ],
