          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"e511728b24ec2238eddd6da6\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Suddenly Mr. Podgers let go of Lord Arthur\u2019s right hand and grabbed his left, bending so low to examine it that the gold rims of his spectacles almost touched the palm. For an instant his face became a pale mask of terror, but he quickly regained his composure, and looking up at Lady Windermere with a forced smile, said, \u2018It is the hand of a charming young man.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Of course it is!\u2019 replied Lady Windermere. \u2018But will he be a charming husband? That is what I want to know.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018All charming young men are,\u2019 said Mr. Podgers.\\n\\n\u2018I don\u2019t think a husband should be too fascinating,\u2019 murmured Lady Jedburgh thoughtfully. \u2018It is so dangerous.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018My dear child, they never are too fascinating,\u2019 cried Lady Windermere. \u2018But I want details. Details are the only interesting things. What will happen to Lord Arthur?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Well, within the next few months Lord Arthur will take a voyage\u2014\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Oh yes, his honeymoon, of course!\u2019\\n\\n\u2018And lose a relative.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Not his sister, I hope?\u2019 said Lady Jedburgh in a pleading voice.\\n\\n\u2018Certainly not his sister,\u2019 answered Mr. Podgers, waving his hand as if to calm her. \u2018Only a distant relative.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018I am dreadfully disappointed,\u2019 said Lady Windermere. \u2018I have nothing to tell Sybil tomorrow. No one cares about distant relatives now. They went out of fashion years ago. Still, I suppose she should have a black silk dress on hand; it always works for church, you know. And now let us go to supper. They are sure to have eaten everything, but we might find some hot soup. Fran\u00e7ois used to make excellent soup once, but he is so agitated about politics now that I never feel quite sure about him. I wish General Boulanger would be quiet. Duchess, I\u2019m sure you are tired?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Not at all, dear Gladys,\u2019 answered the Duchess, waddling toward the door. \u2018I have enjoyed myself immensely, and the chiropodist\u2014I mean the chiromantist\u2014is most interesting. Flora, where is my tortoise-shell fan? Oh, thank you so much, Sir Thomas. And my lace shawl, Flora? Oh, thank you, Sir Thomas, very kind of you.\u2019 And the good creature finally got downstairs without dropping her scent bottle more than twice.\\n\\nAll this time Lord Arthur Savile had stood by the fireplace, feeling the same dread, the same sickening sense of coming trouble. He gave his sister a sad smile as she swept past on Lord Plymdale\u2019s arm, looking lovely in her pink brocade and pearls, and he barely heard Lady Windermere call him to follow. He thought of Sybil Merton, and the idea that anything might come between them filled his eyes with tears.\"}"
