          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"1f2c22ea864cd4794a0ce7bf\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Goodness, she could talk. It wouldn\u2019t have been polite to hint that it was very late and I was worn out and ready to drop. I wished I had gone to bed when I had the chance. Now I had to see it through; there was no other option. So she kept chattering on and on, in the otherwise profound, ghostly silence of the sleeping castle, until eventually there rose, as if from deep beneath us, a distant sound like a muffled scream\u2014with such agony in it that it made my flesh crawl. The queen stopped, her eyes lighting with pleasure; she tilted her graceful head like a bird listening. The sound bored up through the stillness again.\\n\\n\u201cWhat is it?\u201d I asked.\\n\\n\u201cIt is truly a stubborn soul, and it endures long. It has been many hours now.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cEndures what?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThe rack. Come\u2014you shall see a merry sight. If he still refuses to yield his secret, you shall watch him torn apart.\u201d\\n\\nWhat a silky smooth hellion she was, so composed and serene while the muscles all down my legs were aching in sympathy with that man\u2019s suffering. Led by armored guards bearing blazing torches, we marched along echoing corridors and down dank, dripping stone stairs, smelling of mold and centuries of imprisoned night\u2014a chilly, uncanny journey, and a long one, not made shorter or cheerier by the sorceress\u2019s conversation, which centered on this victim and his crime. He had been accused by an anonymous informant of killing a stag in the royal preserves. I said:\\n\\n\u201cAnonymous testimony isn\u2019t quite right, your Highness. It would be fairer to confront the accused with the accuser.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI had not considered that, it being of little consequence. But even if I wished it, I could not, for the accuser came masked at night and told the forester, then immediately left again, so the forester knows him not.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen this Unknown is the only person who saw the stag killed?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIndeed, no man saw the killing, but this Unknown saw the daring miscreant near the spot where the stag lay, and came with loyal zeal to betray him to the forester.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSo the Unknown was also near the dead stag? Isn\u2019t it possible he did the killing himself? His loyal zeal\u2014behind a mask\u2014looks a bit suspicious. But why is your Highness racking the prisoner? What\u2019s the gain?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHe will not confess otherwise; without confession his soul would be lost. His life is forfeit by law for his crime\u2014and I will make sure he pays it\u2014but it would endanger my own soul to let him die without confession and absolution.\u201d\"}"
        }
      ],
