          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"6c639d03fc8bcd8a063fa2ab\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Their arrival ignited a spark in the heart of Saint Antoine, spreading quickly as they moved along, flaring in the faces at most doors and windows. Yet no one followed them, and not a word was spoken when they entered the wine shop, though every man\u2019s eyes were on them.\\n\\n\u201cGood day, gentlemen!\u201d said Monsieur Defarge.\\n\\nIt might have been the cue for everyone to speak. A chorus of \u201cGood day!\u201d answered him.\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s bad weather, gentlemen,\u201d Defarge said, shaking his head.\\n\\nAt that, every man looked at his neighbor, then they all lowered their eyes and sat in silence. Except for one man, who stood up and walked out.\\n\\n\u201cMy wife,\u201d Defarge said loudly to Madame Defarge, \u201cI have traveled several leagues with this good mender of roads, called Jacques. I met him\u2014by chance\u2014a day and a half outside Paris. He\u2019s a good soul, this mender of roads named Jacques. Give him something to drink, my wife!\u201d\\n\\nA second man stood up and left. Madame Defarge set wine in front of the mender of roads called Jacques. He removed his blue cap to the company and drank. He carried coarse dark bread in his blouse, eating in between sips, sitting near Madame Defarge\u2019s counter munching and drinking. A third man rose and left.\\n\\nDefarge refreshed himself with a draft of wine\u2014but took less than the stranger, being a man to whom wine was no rarity\u2014and stood waiting until the countryman finished his breakfast. He looked at no one there, and no one looked at him now; not even Madame Defarge, who had taken up her knitting and was working.\\n\\n\u201cAre you done with your meal, friend?\u201d he asked at the proper time.\\n\\n\u201cYes, thank you.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCome, then! You shall see the room I told you you could have. It will suit you perfectly.\u201d\\n\\nOut of the wine shop into the street, out of the street into a courtyard, out of the courtyard up a steep staircase, out of the staircase into a garret\u2014once the garret where a white-haired man sat on a low bench, bent forward and hard at work making shoes.\\n\\nNo white-haired man was there now; but the three men who had left the wine shop one by one were there. And between them and the distant white-haired man was the single small link: they had once watched him through cracks in the wall.\\n\\nDefarge shut the door carefully and spoke quietly:\\n\\n\u201cJacques One, Jacques Two, Jacques Three! This is the witness encountered by appointment by me, Jacques Four.\u201d\"}"
