          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"0d28082847f1ffbba2f2e6d1\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Recent reports from Rotterdam suggest the city is in a frenzy of philosophical excitement. Phenomena there have been so completely unexpected\u2014so entirely new\u2014so utterly at odds with accepted beliefs\u2014that I have no doubt by now all Europe is in an uproar, every branch of physics is in turmoil, and reason and astronomy are at each other\u2019s throats.\\n\\nIt seems that on the\u2014\u2014 day of\u2014\u2014 (I am uncertain of the date), a vast crowd, gathered for reasons not specified, filled the great square of the Exchange in the well-ordered city of Rotterdam. The day was warm\u2014unusually so for the season\u2014with hardly a breath of air. The crowd did not mind being occasionally sprinkled by brief, friendly showers falling from large white clouds that flickered across the blue sky. Nevertheless, around noon, a slight but remarkable stir began among the assembly: the chatter of ten thousand tongues followed; and a moment later, ten thousand faces turned skyward, ten thousand pipes dropped at once from the corners of ten thousand mouths, and a shout comparable only to the roar of Niagara echoed long, loud, and furious through every quarter of Rotterdam.\\n\\nThe cause of this commotion soon became clear enough. From behind the massive bulk of one of those sharply defined clouds already mentioned, a strange, mismatched, yet apparently solid object slowly emerged into a patch of open blue. It was so oddly shaped, so whimsically assembled, that the crowd of solid townsmen standing open-mouthed below could make nothing of it and never master their amazement. What could it be? For the love of every wife and devil in Rotterdam, what could it mean? No one knew, no one could guess; not even the burgomaster Mynheer Superbus Von Underduk had the slightest clue to unravel the mystery. So, as nothing more sensible could be done, everyone carefully replaced his pipe in the corner of his mouth, cocked his right eye at the phenomenon, puffed, paused, waddled about, and grunted meaningfully\u2014then waddled back, grunted, paused, and finally\u2014puffed again.\\n\\nMeanwhile, the object of all this curiosity\u2014and the cause of so much smoke\u2014was descending lower and lower toward the respectable city. Within a few minutes it came close enough to be clearly seen. It appeared to be\u2014yes! it was without doubt a kind of balloon; yet surely no balloon like this had ever been seen in Rotterdam before.\"}"
