          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"572a10dcd110cff648667921\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Of course he was very entertaining and all that, but I was terribly disappointed; and when I asked him about the coat of mail, he only laughed and said it was much too cold to wear in England. Ah, here is Mr. Podgers! Now, Mr. Podgers, I want you to read the Duchess of Paisley\u2019s hand. Duchess, you must take off your glove. No, not the left hand, the other one.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Dear Gladys, I really don\u2019t think it is quite proper,\u2019 said the Duchess, weakly unbuttoning a rather dirty kid glove.\\n\\n\u2018Nothing interesting ever is,\u2019 said Lady Windermere. \u2018We made the world that way. But I must introduce you. Duchess, this is Mr. Podgers, my favorite palm reader. Mr. Podgers, this is the Duchess of Paisley, and if you say she has a higher Mount of the Moon than I have, I will never believe in you again.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018I am sure, Gladys, there is nothing like that in my hand,\u2019 said the Duchess seriously.\\n\\n\u2018Your Grace is entirely right,\u2019 said Mr. Podgers, glancing at the little plump hand with its short square fingers. \u2018The Mount of the Moon is not developed. The life line, however, is excellent. Please bend your wrist. Thank you. Three distinct lines on the bracelet! You will live a very long life, Duchess, and be very happy. Ambition\u2014very moderate; head line not exaggerated; heart line\u2014\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Now, do be indiscreet, Mr. Podgers,\u2019 cried Lady Windermere.\\n\\n\u2018Nothing would give me greater pleasure,\u2019 said Mr. Podgers with a bow, \u2018if the Duchess ever had been, but I am sorry to say I see a great constancy of affection combined with a strong sense of duty.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Please go on, Mr. Podgers,\u2019 said the Duchess, looking quite pleased.\\n\\n\u2018Economy is one of your Grace\u2019s chief virtues,\u2019 continued Mr. Podgers, and Lady Windermere burst out laughing.\\n\\n\u2018Economy is a very good thing,\u2019 remarked the Duchess comfortably; \u2018when I married Paisley he had eleven castles and not a single house fit to live in.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018And now he has twelve houses and not a single castle,\u2019 cried Lady Windermere.\\n\\n\u2018Well, my dear,\u2019 said the Duchess, \u2018I like\u2014\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Comfort,\u2019 said Mr. Podgers, \u2018and modern improvements, and hot water in every bedroom. Your Grace is quite right. Comfort is the only thing our civilisation provides us.\\n\\n\u2018You have described the Duchess perfectly, Mr. Podgers, and now you must read Lady Flora,\u2019 and in answer to a nod from the smiling hostess, a tall girl with sandy Scottish hair and high shoulder blades stepped awkwardly from behind the sofa and held out a long, bony hand with spatulate fingers.\\n\\n\u2018Ah, a pianist! I see,\u2019 said Mr. Podgers, \u2018an excellent pianist, though perhaps not quite a musician.\u2019\"}"
