          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"2a1f140b60260957250b019d\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The heft of the insect was astonishing, and, considering everything, I could hardly fault Jupiter for his opinion of it; but I could not fathom why Legrand agreed with him.\\n\\n\u201cI sent for you,\u201d he said grandly after I finished examining the beetle, \u201cto get your counsel and help in carrying out the plans of Fate and of the bug\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Legrand,\u201d I broke in, \u201cyou must be unwell and should take precautions. You shall go to bed, and I will stay with you a few days until you recover. You are feverish and\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFeel my pulse,\u201d he said.\\n\\nI felt it and, honestly, found no trace of fever.\\n\\n\u201cBut you can be ill without a fever. Let me prescribe for you just this once. First, go to bed. Next\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou are mistaken,\u201d he interrupted. \u201cI am as well as I could expect under the excitement I feel. If you truly wish me well, you will ease this excitement.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd how am I to do that?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cVery easily. Jupiter and I are going on an expedition into the hills on the mainland, and we need someone we can trust. You are the only one. Whether we succeed or fail, the excitement you see in me will fade.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI want to oblige you in every way,\u201d I replied, \u201cbut do you mean to say this cursed beetle is linked to your expedition?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt is.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen, Legrand, I cannot join such nonsense.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019m sorry\u2014very sorry\u2014for we\u2019ll have to go alone.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGo alone! The man is mad! But wait\u2014how long will you be gone?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cProbably all night. We leave at once and return by sunrise, no matter what.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd will you promise, on your honor, that when this whim of yours is done and the bug business (good heavens!) resolved to your satisfaction, you will come home and follow my advice entirely, as that of your physician?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, I promise; now let us go, for we have no time to lose.\u201d\\n\\nWith a heavy heart I went with my friend. We set out around four o\u2019clock\u2014Legrand, Jupiter, the dog, and me. Jupiter carried the scythe and spades, insisting on bearing everything\u2014more from fear of leaving the tools within reach of his master than from any extra energy or good nature.\"}"
