          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"a9d718cd3115f46b065a64fd\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cI\u2019m going, Massa Will\u2014indeed I be,\u201d the negro answered at once\u2014\u201cnear bout to de very eend now.\u201d\\n\\n\u201c_Out to the end!_\u201d screamed Legrand, \u201cyou mean you\u2019re all the way at the tip of that limb?\u201d\\n\\n\u201c\u2019Most to de eend, massa\u2014o-o-o-o-oh! Lord-golly-mercy! what dis thing up here in de tree?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell!\u201d cried Legrand, in high delight, \u201cwhat do you see?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, \u2019tain\u2019t nuthin but a skull\u2014somebody done left his head up in de tree, and de crows eat every scrap o\u2019 meat off it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cA skull, you say! Very good\u2014how\u2019s it fixed there? What keeps it fast?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSure \u2019nough, massa; lemme look. Why dis mighty queer, sure\u2014there\u2019s a big nail through de skull nailing it to de tree.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNow, Jupiter, do exactly as I direct\u2014do you hear me?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, massa.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cListen close\u2014find the left eye of the skull.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHum! hoo! dat a funny notion! why ain\u2019t no eye left at all.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cConfound your dullness! you do know right hand from left?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYas, I knows dat\u2014knows dat fine\u2014\u2019tis wid my lef hand I chops wood.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOf course! you\u2019re left-handed; so your left eye\u2019s on the same side as that hand. Now you should manage to find the skull\u2019s left eye, or where it once was. Have you got it?\u201d\\n\\nA long silence followed. Finally the negro asked,\\n\\n\u201cDo de skull\u2019s left eye stay on same side as de skull\u2019s left hand, too?\u2014\u2019cause de skull ain\u2019t got nary bit o\u2019 hand\u2014never mind! I got the left eye now\u2014here de left eye! what I do with it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLet the beetle drop through it, as far down the cord will let it go\u2014but mind you don\u2019t lose hold of the string.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll done, Massa Will; real easy to send de bug through de hole\u2014watch for him down there!\u201d\\n\\nThrough all this exchange no part of Jupiter\u2019s body was visible; but the beetle he had lowered now shone at the string\u2019s end, glimmering like a polished golden globe in the last glimmers of the setting sun that still faintly lit the hill where we stood. The _scarab\u00e6us_ dangled free of every branch and, if released, would have dropped straight to our feet. Legrand at once seized the scythe and swept out a circular patch, three or four yards across, just under the insect; and when he finished, he told Jupiter to release the string and climb down from the tree.\"}"
