          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"cb496487d7e4349559bbb94c\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cBut do not think I considered it anything but a misfortune in itself.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDepend upon it, they were all quite comfortable.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI should not like them any better for that, perhaps. Such a crowd of women and children have no right to be at ease aboard ship.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Frederick, you are talking absolute nonsense. What would become of us poor sailors\u2019 wives, who so often wish to be transported from one port to another in pursuit of our husbands, if everyone felt as you do?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy feelings, you see, did not stop me from bringing Mrs Harville and her entire family to Plymouth.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut I cannot bear to hear you talk like some fine gentleman, as though women were fine ladies instead of rational creatures. None of us expect to sail on smooth seas all our lives.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAh, my dear,\u201d said the Admiral, \u201conce he has a wife, he will sing another song. When he is married, if we are fortunate enough to live through another war, we shall witness him doing as you and I, and many more, have done. He will be grateful to anyone who brings him his wife.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAy, indeed we shall.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNow I have finished,\u201d cried Captain Wentworth. \u201cAs soon as married folks begin attacking me with, \u2018Oh! you will think quite differently when you are married,\u2019 I can only answer, \u2018No, I shall not;\u2019 and then they retort, \u2018Yes, you will,\u2019 and that settles it.\u201d\\n\\nHe rose and walked away.\\n\\n\u201cWhat an extensive traveller you must have been, ma\u2019am!\u201d exclaimed Mrs Musgrove to Mrs Croft.\\n\\n\u201cPretty well, ma\u2019am, through the fifteen years of my marriage; though many ladies have accomplished more. I have crossed the Atlantic four times, and been once to the East Indies and home again, but just that once; besides visiting various places nearer home: Cork, Lisbon, and Gibraltar. But I never went past the Straits, and never was in the West Indies. We do not count Bermuda or the Bahamas, you know, as the West Indies.\u201d\\n\\nMrs Musgrove could not contest it; she could not accuse herself of ever having called them anything at all in her life.\\n\\n\u201cAnd I assure you, ma\u2019am,\u201d continued Mrs Croft, \u201cnothing surpasses the accommodations of a man-of-war; I refer, of course, to the larger classes. When you come to a frigate, naturally you are more cramped; yet any sensible woman may be perfectly content there; and I can truly say the happiest portion of my life has been spent on shipboard. While we were together, you know, there was nothing to fear.\u201d\"}"
