          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"253b626d25bfdadc3a91fe03\",\"rewritten_text\":\"In the acrid tirade against Chantilly that yesterday\u2019s \u201cMus\u00e9e\u201d carried, the satirist, having made some disgraceful jibes about the cobbler\u2019s adopted stage-name, quoted a Latin line we ourselves have often discussed: \u201cPerdidit antiquum litera prima sonum.\u201d \u201cI had mentioned to you that it referred to Orion, once written Urion; and, from certain barbed associations tied to that explanation, I knew it was impossible you could have forgotten. It followed that you would connect both notions\u2014Orion and Chantilly. That you did make this connection I saw in the cast of the smile that flitted across your lips. You envisioned the poor cobbler\u2019s sacrifice. Up to then you had been leaning in your walk; now I watched you straighten to full height. I knew at once your thoughts had flown to Chantilly\u2019s tiny stature. At that juncture I cut into your reflections to point out that, since he was such a diminutive fellow\u2014that Chantilly\u2014he ought rather to try the Th\u00e9\u00e2tre des Vari\u00e9t\u00e9s.\u201d Not long after, we were scanning an evening issue of the \u201cGazette des Tribunaux,\u201d when these paragraphs drew our eyes: \u201cExtraordinary Murders.\u2014This morning, about three o\u2019clock, residents of the Quartier St. Roch were startled from sleep by a series of dreadful screams apparently emanating from the fourth floor of a house on the Rue Morgue, known to be occupied exclusively by Madame L\u2019Espanaye and her daughter, Mademoiselle Camille L\u2019Espanaye. After some delay, caused by an unsuccessful attempt to gain entrance in the usual way, the gate was forced with a crowbar, and eight or ten neighbors went in with two gendarmes. By this moment the cries had ended; but as the group took the first stairs, two or more rough voices in angry dispute were heard and seemed to come from the upper stories. On reaching the second landing, these sounds also ceased and everything fell utterly silent. The party divided and rushed through room after room. Arriving at a large back chamber on the fourth story\u2014the door, found locked with the key inside, having been broken open\u2014they were confronted by a sight that filled each witness with awe no less than horror. The room lay in the wildest confusion\u2014furniture shattered and flung about every which way. There was only a single bedstead; its bedding had been stripped off and tossed to the center of the floor. Upon a chair rested a razor, smeared with blood.\u201d}\"}"
