          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"a9ec9abcd05a5614325f216c\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Once everything was settled both amicably and to their satisfaction, they ceremoniously sealed the contract with another teacup of peppermint cordial, which was all the more necessary given how fluttery and agitated the lady felt. As she finished the drink, she told Mr. Bumble about the old woman\u2019s death.\\n\\n\u201cVery good,\u201d said the gentleman, sipping his peppermint. \u201cI\u2019ll stop by Sowerberry\u2019s on my way home and tell him to send over in the morning. Was that what frightened you, my love?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt wasn\u2019t anything specific, dear,\u201d the lady answered evasively.\\n\\n\u201cIt must have been something, my love,\u201d Mr. Bumble pressed. \u201cWon\u2019t you tell your own B.?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot now,\u201d she replied. \u201cOne of these days. After we\u2019re married, dear.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAfter we\u2019re married!\u201d exclaimed Mr. Bumble. \u201cIt wasn\u2019t any impertinence from any of those male paupers that\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, no, love!\u201d the lady interrupted quickly.\\n\\n\u201cIf I thought it was,\u201d Mr. Bumble went on, \u201cif I thought any one of them had dared to lift his vulgar eyes to that lovely face\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThey wouldn\u2019t have dared, love,\u201d she answered.\\n\\n\u201cThey\u2019d better not!\u201d said Mr. Bumble, clenching his fists. \u201cLet me see any man, parish or extraparish, presume to try it, and I can promise he wouldn\u2019t try it twice!\u201d\\n\\nWithout those colorful gestures, the statement might not have sounded like much of a compliment. But since Mr. Bumble accompanied the warning with several martial flourishes, she was deeply moved by this proof of devotion and declared admiringly that he was a regular dove.\\n\\nThe dove promptly flipped up his coat collar and set his cocked hat on his head, and after exchanging a long, loving embrace with his future bride, he once more faced the cold night wind. He paused for a few minutes in the men\u2019s ward to scold the paupers a bit, just to reassure himself that he possessed the necessary harshness for the workhouse-master\u2019s job. Satisfied with his qualifications, Mr. Bumble left the building in high spirits, buoyed by bright visions of future promotion, which occupied his thoughts until he reached the undertaker\u2019s shop.\\n\\nMr. and Mrs. Sowerberry were out for tea and supper, and since Noah Claypole rarely took on more exertion than was required for eating and drinking, the shop remained open though it was past closing time. Mr. Bumble rapped his cane on the counter several times; receiving no response and seeing light shining through the glass window of the little back parlor, he boldly peered in to see what was happening\u2014and when he saw it, he was significantly surprised.\"}"
