          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"8aa1d1dc9fd234b59b69715a\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWell, well, Mr. Bumble,\u201d he remarked at last, \u201cthere\u2019s no disputing that, since the new feeding system took effect, the coffins are somewhat narrower and shallower than before; but we must turn some profit, Mr. Bumble. Well-seasoned wood is a costly commodity, sir; and all the iron handles come by canal from Birmingham.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, well,\u201d observed Mr. Bumble, \u201cevery trade has its inconveniences. A reasonable profit is, naturally, allowable.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cExactly so, exactly so,\u201d returned the undertaker; \u201cand if I fail to gain on this or that specific article, I make it up in the long run, you understand\u2014he! he! he!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cPrecisely,\u201d said Mr. Bumble.\\n\\n\u201cThough I must state,\u201d the undertaker resumed, picking up the thread of comments the beadle had stopped, \u201cthough I must state, Mr. Bumble, I labor under one major drawback: namely, that the stout folk are the first to depart. Those who have lived better and paid rates for years are the earliest to sink when they enter the house; and let me assure you, Mr. Bumble, that three or four inches beyond one\u2019s estimate cuts deeply into one\u2019s profits, particularly when there\u2019s a family to maintain, sir.\u201d\\n\\nAs Mr. Sowerberry delivered this with the proper indignation of a man mistreated, and as Mr. Bumble sensed it cast something of a slur on the parish\u2019s honor, he decided to shift the topic. Oliver Twist being foremost in his thoughts, he made him the subject.\\n\\n\u201cBy the bye,\u201d said Mr. Bumble, \u201cyou don\u2019t happen to know anyone who wants a boy, do you? A parochial \u2019prentice who is now a dead weight; a veritable millstone, if I may say, about the parochial throat? Favorable terms, Mr. Sowerberry, favorable terms?\u201d As he spoke, Mr. Bumble lifted his cane to the bill above and tapped three distinct times on the words \u201cfive pounds,\u201d printed there in Roman capitals of enormous size.\\n\\n\u201cGadso!\u201d exclaimed the undertaker, catching Mr. Bumble by the gilt-edged lapel of his official coat. \u201cThat\u2019s precisely what I intended to mention to you. You know\u2014dear me, what a remarkably elegant button this is, Mr. Bumble! I never noticed it before.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, I deem it rather handsome,\u201d replied the beadle, casting a proud glance downward at the large brass buttons adorning his coat. \u201cThe die matches the parochial seal\u2014the Good Samaritan tending the sick and bruised man. The board presented it to me on New Year\u2019s morning, Mr. Sowerberry. I recall putting it on for the first time to attend the inquest on that reduced tradesman who perished in a doorway at midnight.\u201d\"}"
