          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"943b0601681a935059aa4acc\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Biddy was crying; the garden growing darker, the lane, and the stars coming out were all blurred to me as well.\\n\\n\u201cNothing was ever found out, Biddy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNothing.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDo you know what\u2019s become of Orlick?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cJudging by the color of his clothes, I\u2019d say he\u2019s working in the quarries.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen you\u2019ve seen him, of course?\u2014Why are you staring at that dark tree in the lane?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI saw him there the night she died.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat wasn\u2019t the last time, was it, Biddy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo; I\u2019ve seen him there since we\u2019ve been walking here.\u2014It\u2019s no use,\u201d said Biddy, putting her hand on my arm as I was about to run out, \u201cyou know I wouldn\u2019t deceive you; he was there for barely a minute, and now he\u2019s gone.\u201d\\n\\nMy anger flared at learning that she was still being stalked by that man, and I felt relentless toward him. I told her so, and that I would spend whatever money or effort it took to drive him out of the region. Little by little she guided me into calmer conversation, and she told me how Joe loved me and never complained about anything\u2014she didn\u2019t have to say \u201cabout me\u201d; I knew what she meant\u2014always doing his duty in his own way, with strong hands, a quiet voice, and a gentle heart.\\n\\n\u201cHonestly, you could hardly praise him too much,\u201d I said. \u201cAnd Biddy, we have to talk about these things often, since I\u2019ll be down here a lot now. I\u2019m not leaving poor Joe alone.\u201d\\n\\nBiddy didn\u2019t say a word.\\n\\n\u201cBiddy, don\u2019t you hear me?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, Mr. Pip.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBesides your calling me Mr. Pip\u2014which seems in poor taste, Biddy\u2014what do you mean?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat do I mean?\u201d Biddy asked timidly.\\n\\n\u201cBiddy,\u201d I said, with a righteous air, \u201cI insist on knowing what you mean by this.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBy this?\u201d said Biddy.\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t repeat me,\u201d I snapped. \u201cYou didn\u2019t used to do that, Biddy.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDidn\u2019t used to!\u201d cried Biddy. \u201cOh, Mr. Pip! \u2018Used to\u2019!\u201d\\n\\nWell, I thought it best to drop that point too. After another silent turn in the garden, I returned to the main subject.\\n\\n\u201cBiddy,\u201d I said, \u201cI made a comment about coming down here often to see Joe, and you answered with a very pointed silence. Be so kind, Biddy, as to tell me why.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAre you quite sure, then, that you will come to see him often?\u201d Biddy asked, stopping in the narrow garden path and looking at me beneath the stars with a clear, honest gaze.\"}"
