          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"37e3b39c9ea3c7e1d6e7e3fa\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cJoseph! Joseph!\u201d He shook his head and tapped his temple, as if lamenting Joseph\u2019s shortcomings.\\n\\n\u201cBut my dear young friend,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, \u201cyou must be famished, you must be worn out. Sit down. Here\u2019s a chicken brought over from the Boar, here\u2019s a tongue from the same, here are one or two little extras from the Boar, which I trust you won\u2019t disdain. But do I,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, popping up the instant he had sat, \u201cbehold before me the very one I sported with in his days of cheerful infancy? And may I\u2014may I\u2014?\u201d\\n\\nThe question was whether he might shake hands. I consented, he did so with great zeal, and then re-seated himself.\\n\\n\u201cHere\u2019s wine,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook. \u201cLet us drink, Thanks to Fortune, and may she continue to select her darlings with equal wisdom! And yet I cannot,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, rising again, \u201clook upon One\u2014and likewise drink to One\u2014without once more expressing\u2014May I\u2014may I\u2014?\u201d\\n\\nI told him he might, and he shook hands again, drained his glass, and inverted it. I followed suit; and if I had upended myself before drinking, the wine could scarcely have rushed to my head faster.\\n\\nMr. Pumblechook carved the liver wing for me, and the prime slice of tongue (none of those eccentric No Thoroughfares of Pork now), and scarcely regarded his own plate. \u201cAh! poultry, poultry! Little you dreamed,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, addressing the bird, \u201cwhen you were a small chick, what awaited you. Little you thought you\u2019d be sustenance in this humble home for one who\u2014Call it a weakness if you choose,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, rising again, \u201cbut may I? may I\u2014?\u201d\\n\\nIt became needless to repeat that he might, so he simply did it. How he managed it so often without slashing himself with my knife, I cannot tell.\\n\\n\u201cAnd your sister,\u201d he went on after a spell of steady eating, \u201cwho had the honour of rearing you by hand! It\u2019s a melancholy picture, to think she\u2019s no longer capable of wholly comprehending the honour. May\u2014\u201d\\n\\nI saw him preparing to make another attempt at me, and I stopped him.\\n\\n\u201cWe\u2019ll drink her health,\u201d I said.\\n\\n\u201cAh!\u201d cried Mr. Pumblechook, leaning back in his chair, limp with admiration, \u201cthat\u2019s how you know \u2019em, sir!\u201d (Whoever Sir might be, it certainly wasn\u2019t myself, and nobody else was there.) \u201cThat\u2019s how you spot the noble-hearted, sir!\u201d\"}"
