          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"720a296dfe7607a53b14373c\",\"rewritten_text\":\"She studied me sharply for a moment before asking quietly, \u201cWhat do you want for them?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOnly,\u201d I replied, \u201cthat you wouldn\u2019t lump them in with the others. They might share the same blood, but believe me, they\u2019re not the same kind.\u201d\\n\\nStill watching me intently, Miss Havisham repeated, \u201cWhat do you want for them?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019m not clever enough,\u201d I admitted, feeling myself flush a little, \u201cto hide from you, even if I wished to, that I do want something. Miss Havisham, if you would spare the money to do my friend Herbert a lasting favor, which by its nature must be done without his knowledge, I can show you how.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy must it be done without his knowing?\u201d she asked, settling her hands on her stick so she could study me more closely.\\n\\n\u201cBecause,\u201d I said, \u201cI began helping him over two years ago without his knowing, and I don\u2019t want to be exposed. Why I can\u2019t finish what I started, I can\u2019t explain. It\u2019s part of a secret that belongs to someone else, not me.\u201d\\n\\nShe slowly turned her gaze from me to the fire. After staring at it for what felt like a long time in the stillness and dim candlelight, she was startled by a collapsing heap of red coals and looked back at me\u2014first blankly, then with growing focus. Throughout, Estella kept knitting. When Miss Havisham had fully fixed her attention on me, she spoke as if no time had passed in our conversation: \u201cWhat else?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cEstella,\u201d I said, turning to her and trying to steady my shaking voice, \u201cyou know I love you. You know I\u2019ve loved you deeply for a long time.\u201d\\n\\nShe raised her eyes to my face, her fingers still moving, her expression unchanged. I saw Miss Havisham glance between us.\\n\\n\u201cI would have said this sooner, if not for my long-standing misunderstanding. It made me hope Miss Havisham intended us for each other. While I believed you had no choice in it, I held back from speaking. But I must say it now.\u201d\\n\\nStill expressionless and still working her needles, Estella shook her head.\\n\\n\u201cI know,\u201d I said in response. \u201cI know. I have no hope of ever calling you mine, Estella.\u201d\"}"
        }
