          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"b9ec7dabbf828a5220abb866\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Just past noon the boys borrowed a little skiff from a townsman who wasn\u2019t home and set off right away. A few miles below Cave Hollow, Tom said, \u201cNow you see how this bluff looks exactly the same all the way down from the cave hollow\u2014no houses, no wood yards, nothing but identical bushes. But see that white patch up ahead where a landslide happened? That\u2019s one of my markers. We\u2019ll pull in now.\u201d\\n\\nThey beached the skiff.\\n\\n\u201cNow, Huck, right where we\u2019re standing you could touch the hole I crawled out of with a fishing pole. Try to find it.\u201d\\n\\nHuck searched all around and came up empty. Tom strutted into a dense clump of sumac and announced, \u201cHere it is! Look at it, Huck; there isn\u2019t a cozier hole in the whole county. You keep quiet about it. I\u2019ve always wanted to be a robber, but I knew I had to have a place like this, and figuring out where to find it was the hard part. Now we\u2019ve got it, and we\u2019ll keep it secret\u2014except we\u2019ll let Joe Harper and Ben Rogers in. You\u2019ve got to have a gang or else there\u2019s no style to it. Tom Sawyer\u2019s Gang\u2014it sounds grand, doesn\u2019t it, Huck?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt sure does, Tom. Who do we rob?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, pretty much anybody. We ambush folks\u2014that\u2019s the usual way.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd kill them?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, not every time. We stash them in the cave till they pay ransom.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s ransom?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMoney. You make them raise every bit they can from their friends, and if you\u2019ve kept them a whole year and they still haven\u2019t come up with it, then you kill them. That\u2019s the general method. Only you never kill the women. You lock the women up, but don\u2019t hurt them. They\u2019re always beautiful and rich and scared stiff. You take their watches and jewelry, but you always take off your hat and talk polite. No one is as polite as robbers\u2014you can see that in any book. The women end up falling for you, and after they\u2019ve been in the cave a week or two they stop crying, and then you couldn\u2019t get them to leave. If you drove them out, they\u2019d spin right around and come back. That\u2019s how it happens in all the stories.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s really prime, Tom. I think it beats being a pirate.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYeah, it\u2019s better in some ways because it\u2019s close to home and circuses and all that.\u201d\\n\\nBy then they had everything ready, and the boys climbed into the hole, Tom leading the way. They slogged to the far end of the tunnel, tied off their spliced kite strings, and pushed on.\"}"
