rman Embassy.\u201d Before Lord Arthur could recover from being recognized, he found himself in the back room, sipping exquisite Marcobr\u00fcnner from a pale yellow hock glass marked with the Imperial monogram, chatting amiably with the famous conspirator. \u201cExplosive clocks,\u201d Herr Winckelkopf said, \u201caren\u2019t ideal for shipping abroad because even if they slip past Customs, the trains are so unreliable that they usually go off before reaching their destination.\u201d\"}"
