          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"c11f78d78ee72d8be9c59fe6\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Winters on Sullivan\u2019s Island are rarely harsh, and even in autumn it is unusual to need a fire. Yet in mid-October, 18\u2014, one day turned bitterly cold. Just before sunset I pushed through the evergreens to my friend\u2019s hut, where I had not been for several weeks; I was living in Charleston then, nine miles away, and travel between the city and the island was nothing like it is now. I knocked, as usual, but no one answered. Knowing where the spare key was hidden, I found it, unlocked the door, and stepped inside. A bright fire blazed on the hearth\u2014a welcome surprise. I shrugged off my overcoat, settled into an armchair by the crackling logs, and waited for my hosts.\\n\\nThey came soon after dark and greeted me warmly. Jupiter, grinning widely, hurried to prepare marsh hens for supper. Legrand was in one of his spells\u2014what else could I call them?\u2014of excitement. He had discovered a new kind of bivalve, enough to create a new genus, and, more than that, with Jupiter\u2019s help he had tracked down and captured a scarab he believed no one had ever seen before. He wanted my opinion on it the next day.\\n\\n\u201cAnd why not tonight?\u201d I asked, rubbing my hands before the fire and cursing all scarabs.\\n\\n\u201cIf only I\u2019d known you were here!\u201d said Legrand. \u201cIt\u2019s been so long since I saw you; how could I guess you\u2019d visit me on this very night? As I was coming home I met Lieutenant G\u2014\u2014 from the fort, and foolishly I lent him the bug, so you can\u2019t see it until morning. Stay the night, and I\u2019ll send Jup down for it at sunrise. It\u2019s the loveliest creature alive!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat?\u2014sunrise?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNonsense! Not sunrise\u2014the bug. It\u2019s a brilliant gold, about the size of a large hickory nut, with two jet-black spots near one end of its back and another longer spot at the other end. The antennae are\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDey ain\u2019t no tin in him, Massa Will, I keeps tellin\u2019 you,\u201d Jupiter broke in. \u201cDe bug is a gold bug, solid all through, \u2019cept his wings\u2014I never felt a bug half so heavy in my life.\u201d\"}"
