          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"0de6eadb341403adc9090720\",\"rewritten_text\":\"That was all the encouragement she needed.\\n\\n\u201cWhy, my dear, you must know, Mrs. Long says Netherfield has been leased by a young man of great fortune from the north of England. He arrived on Monday in a coach and four to inspect the place, liked it so much that he struck a deal with Mr. Morris on the spot, plans to move in before Michaelmas, and some of his servants are expected to occupy the house by the end of next week.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat is his name?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBingley.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIs he married or single?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, single, my dear, of course! A single man of great fortune\u2014four or five thousand a year. What a splendid opportunity for our girls!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHow so? How could it matter to them?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Mr. Bennet,\u201d his wife answered, \u201chow can you be so provoking? Surely you realize I\u2019m thinking of him marrying one of them.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIs that why he\u2019s settling here?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy would you call it a plan? Don\u2019t be ridiculous! But he might easily fall in love with one of them, and therefore you must visit him the moment he arrives.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI see no need for that. You and the girls can go\u2014or you could send them alone, which might be even better; since you\u2019re as attractive as any of them, Mr. Bingley might prefer you to the rest.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear, you flatter me. I\u2019ve had my share of beauty, certainly, but I no longer claim anything extraordinary. Once a woman has five grown daughters, she ought to stop thinking about her own looks.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIn such situations, a woman usually hasn\u2019t much beauty left to consider.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut, my dear, you truly must go and call on Mr. Bingley when he arrives in the neighborhood.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI make no promises, I assure you.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut think of your daughters. Imagine what an establishment it would mean for one of them. Sir William and Lady Lucas are determined to go for that very reason, for you know they rarely visit newcomers. You absolutely must go, because it will be impossible for us to call on him if you do not.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou\u2019re being excessively scrupulous. I\u2019m sure Mr. Bingley will be delighted to see you, and I\u2019ll send a short note with you to give him my full permission to marry whichever of the girls he chooses\u2014though I must recommend my little Lizzy.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI insist you do no such thing. Lizzy is not the least bit better than the others, and I\u2019m sure she isn\u2019t half as pretty as Jane or half as good-natured as Lydia.\u201d\"}"
