          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"4e15a55946002a8a589569b8\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cDo you play?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI believe, sir,\u201d the spy said in his humblest manner, turning to Mr. Lorry, \u201cI may appeal to a gentleman of your age and kindness to put it to this other gentleman, so much younger than you, whether he can in any situation justify himself in playing that Ace he mentioned. I admit that I am a spy, and that it is considered a dishonorable occupation\u2014though somebody must do it; but this gentleman is no spy, so why should he degrade himself by becoming one?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019ll play my Ace, Mr. Barsad,\u201d said Carton, taking the reply on himself and glancing at his watch, \u201cwithout any hesitation, in just a few minutes.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI would have hoped, gentlemen,\u201d said the spy, always trying to pull Mr. Lorry into the conversation, \u201cthat your respect for my sister\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI could not better show my respect for your sister than by finally freeing her from her brother,\u201d said Sydney Carton.\\n\\n\u201cYou don\u2019t think so, sir?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy mind is completely made up about it.\u201d\\n\\nThe spy\u2019s smooth manner, oddly out of tune with his deliberately rough clothes and probably with his usual behavior, ran into a wall when faced with the impenetrability of Carton\u2014a man who was a mystery even to wiser and more honest men than he. The spy faltered and lost his footing. While he floundered, Carton said, slipping back into the pose of a man contemplating his cards:\\n\\n\u201cAnd actually, now that I think again, I have a strong feeling I possess another good card, not yet mentioned. That friend and fellow-Sheep who said he grazed in the country prisons\u2014who was he?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFrench. You don\u2019t know him,\u201d the spy answered quickly.\\n\\n\u201cFrench, eh?\u201d Carton repeated, reflecting, and seeming not to notice him at all, though he echoed the word. \u201cWell; he might be.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHe is, I assure you,\u201d said the spy; \u201cthough it\u2019s not important.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThough it\u2019s not important,\u201d Carton repeated in the same automatic way\u2014\u201cthough it\u2019s not important\u2014No, it\u2019s not important. No. Yet I know the face.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI think not. I\u2019m sure not. It can\u2019t be,\u201d said the spy.\\n\\n\u201cIt can\u2019t be,\u201d Sydney Carton muttered, thinking back and absently turning his glass (luckily a small one) again. \u201cCan\u2019t be. Spoke good French. Yet like a foreigner, I thought?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cProvincial,\u201d said the spy.\\n\\n\u201cNo. Foreign!\u201d Carton shouted, slapping his open hand on the table as sudden clarity struck. \u201cCly! Disguised, but the same man. We had that man before us at the Old Bailey.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNow there you\u2019re rash, sir,\u201d said Barsad, smiling in a way that made his aquiline nose tilt further to one side; \u201cthere you really hand me the advantage over you.\u201d\"}"
