          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"0e105e1fe4dcc70f22eb1751\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cOne more word, Rose. Dearest Rose, just one more!\u201d Harry cried, throwing himself in front of her. \u201cIf I had been less\u2014less fortunate, as people would say\u2014if my fate had been some quiet, hidden life\u2014if I had been poor, sick, helpless\u2014would you have turned away from me then? Or is this hesitation born from my likely rise to wealth and honour?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cPlease don\u2019t force me to answer,\u201d Rose replied. \u201cThe question doesn\u2019t exist, and never will. It\u2019s unfair, almost unkind, to push it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIf your answer is what I hardly dare to hope,\u201d Harry returned, \u201cit will cast a ray of happiness on my lonely road and light what lies ahead. It isn\u2019t trivial to do so much, with only a few words, for someone who loves you beyond all else. Oh, Rose, in the name of my fervent and lasting devotion, in the name of all I have suffered for you and all you condemn me to endure, answer this one question!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen, if your life had been different,\u201d Rose replied, \u201cif you had been only a little, but not too far, above me\u2014if I could have been a help and comfort to you in any quiet, humble place, instead of a stain and burden in ambitious, distinguished circles\u2014I would have been spared this trial. I have every reason to be happy, very happy, now; but then, Harry, I admit I would have been happier.\u201d\\n\\nOld hopes she had cherished as a girl rushed back into Rose\u2019s mind as she confessed this; yet they brought tears with them, as old hopes do when they return withered, and the tears eased her heart.\\n\\n\u201cI can\u2019t help this weakness, and it only strengthens my resolve,\u201d Rose said, holding out her hand. \u201cI truly must leave you now.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI ask for one promise,\u201d said Harry. \u201cJust once more\u2014say within a year, perhaps much sooner\u2014I may speak to you again about this, for the last time.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot to press me to change my rightful decision,\u201d Rose answered with a sad smile. \u201cIt will be useless.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo,\u201d said Harry. \u201cJust to hear you repeat it, if you will\u2014repeat it for good! I will lay at your feet whatever rank or fortune I possess, and if you still hold to your present resolve, I will never try, by word or deed, to alter it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen let it be so,\u201d Rose replied. \u201cIt is only one more pang, and by then I may be better able to bear it.\u201d\\n\\nShe held out her hand again.\"}"
