          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"49b11616328c3386ef55dcce\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The weight of the insect was remarkably heavy, and considering everything, I could hardly blame Jupiter for his opinion about it; what baffled me completely was how Legrand could agree with him.\\n\\n\u201cI sent for you,\u201d he declared in a grand tone once I\u2019d finished examining the beetle, \u201cI sent for you so I might have your counsel and assistance in carrying out the plans of Fate and this bug\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Legrand,\u201d I broke in, \u201cyou\u2019re definitely unwell, and should take some precautions. You\u2019ll go to bed, and I\u2019ll stay with you a few days until you\u2019re better. You\u2019re feverish and\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFeel my pulse,\u201d he said.\\n\\nI did, and honestly found not the slightest sign of fever.\\n\\n\u201cBut you can be sick without having a fever. Let me prescribe just this once. First, go to bed. Next\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou\u2019re mistaken,\u201d he interrupted. \u201cI\u2019m as well as I can expect to be under the excitement I\u2019m feeling. If you truly wish me well, you\u2019ll help relieve it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd how am I supposed to do that?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cVery easily. Jupiter and I are going on an expedition into the hills on the mainland, and we need help from someone we can trust. You\u2019re the only one. Whether we succeed or fail, this excitement you see in me will be calmed either way.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI want to help however I can,\u201d I said, \u201cbut do you mean to tell me this damned beetle has anything to do with your trip into the hills?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt does.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen, Legrand, I can\u2019t take part in any such ridiculous business.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019m sorry\u2014truly sorry\u2014because we\u2019ll have to attempt it alone.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTry it alone! The man has to be mad!\u2014but wait! How long do you plan to be away?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cProbably all night. We\u2019re leaving immediately and will be back by sunrise at the latest.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd will you promise, on your honor, that once this crazy phase is over and this bug business\u2014good God!\u2014is settled to your satisfaction, you\u2019ll come home and follow my advice completely, as your physician?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, I promise. Now let\u2019s go; we have no time to waste.\u201d\\n\\nHeavy-hearted, I went along with my friend. We set out around four o\u2019clock\u2014Legrand, Jupiter, the dog, and myself. Jupiter carried the scythe and spades\u2014insisting on bearing the whole lot\u2014more out of fear, it seemed to me, of letting either tool stay within his master\u2019s reach than from any great industry or politeness.\"}"
