          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"408b82e1467171a3fa3e76d3\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cI reckon it among the earliest refinements of well-bred societies.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMost assuredly, sir; and it enjoys the additional merit of being fashionable even among the least polished communities; every savage can dance.\u201d\\n\\nSir William merely smiled. \u201cYour friend acquits himself charmingly,\u201d he resumed, after a pause as Bingley joined the dancers; \u201cand I dare say, Mr. Darcy, that you are yourself no mean proficient in the art.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou saw me dance at Meryton, if you remember, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIndeed I did, and was by no means ill-pleased with the spectacle. Do you frequently honour St. James\u2019s with your dancing?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNever, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDo you not consider it a fit compliment to the place?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt is a compliment which I bestow on no place, whenever it can be avoided.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI presume you possess a house in town?\u201d\\n\\nMr. Darcy inclined his head.\\n\\n\u201cI once contemplated settling in town myself, being partial to superior society; but I doubted whether the London air would suit Lady Lucas.\u201d\\n\\nHe paused, expecting a response, but his companion showed no inclination to give one; and at that very moment Elizabeth approaching, he conceived the gallant notion of calling to her,\u2014\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Miss Eliza, why are you not dancing? Mr. Darcy, permit me to recommend this young lady to you as a most desirable partner. Surely you cannot decline when such beauty solicits.\u201d And, seizing her hand, he would have given it to Mr. Darcy, who, though much surprised, was not reluctant to accept it, when she instantly withdrew, and said, with some agitation, to Sir William,\u2014\\n\\n\u201cIndeed, sir, I have not the slightest intention of dancing. I beg you will not imagine that I came this way to solicit a partner.\u201d\\n\\nMr. Darcy, with grave propriety, requested the honour of her hand, but to no purpose. Elizabeth remained resolute; nor did Sir William shake that resolution by his renewed entreaties.\\n\\n\u201cYou dance with such excellence, Miss Eliza, that it is unkind to deny me the pleasure of witnessing it; and though this gentleman dislikes the pastime in general, I am sure he cannot object to oblige us for half an hour.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMr. Darcy is politeness itself,\u201d Elizabeth replied, smiling.\\n\\n\u201cSo he is: but considering the temptation, my dear Miss Eliza, we need not wonder at his complaisance; for who could reject such a partner?\u201d\\n\\nElizabeth cast a playful look and turned away. Her refusal had not lessened her in the gentleman\u2019s estimation, and he was regarding her with some complacency when Miss Bingley thus accosted him,\u2014\"}"
