          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"d4c20c21486db8e264eece5d\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cBut don\u2019t think I didn\u2019t feel it was wrong in itself.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTrust me, they were all perfectly comfortable.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI might not have liked them any better for that. So many women and children have no right to be comfortable on board.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Frederick, you\u2019re talking nonsense. What would become of us poor sailors\u2019 wives, who often need to travel from one port to another after our husbands, if everyone felt as you do?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou see, my feelings didn\u2019t stop me from taking Mrs. Harville and her whole family to Plymouth.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut I hate to hear you talk like a fashionable gentleman, as if women were delicate ladies instead of sensible creatures. None of us expects smooth water all our lives.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAh, my dear,\u201d said the Admiral, \u201cwhen he has a wife, he\u2019ll sing a different tune. Once he\u2019s married, if we\u2019re lucky enough to see another war, we\u2019ll watch him do as you and I and many others have done. He\u2019ll be grateful to anyone who brings him his wife.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, we certainly will.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNow I\u2019m done,\u201d Captain Wentworth declared. \u201cOnce married people start in on me with, \u2018Oh! you\u2019ll think differently when you\u2019re married,\u2019 I can only say, \u2018No, I won\u2019t,\u2019 and then they reply, \u2018Yes, you will,\u2019 and that\u2019s the end of it.\u201d\\n\\nHe stood up and walked away.\\n\\n\u201cWhat a great traveler you must have been, ma\u2019am!\u201d Mrs. Musgrove said to Mrs. Croft.\\n\\n\u201cNot bad, ma\u2019am, for the fifteen years of my marriage, though plenty of women have done more. I\u2019ve crossed the Atlantic four times, been to the East Indies and back once, and besides that, been in various places closer to home: Cork, Lisbon, Gibraltar. But I never went beyond the Straits, and never to the West Indies. We don\u2019t call Bermuda or the Bahamas the West Indies, you know.\u201d\\n\\nMrs. Musgrove had nothing to argue; she couldn\u2019t remember ever calling them anything in her life.\\n\\n\u201cAnd I assure you, ma\u2019am,\u201d continued Mrs. Croft, \u201cnothing beats the accommodations on a man-of-war\u2014speaking of the higher ranks, of course. On a frigate, naturally, you\u2019re more cramped, though any sensible woman can be perfectly content there; and I can say with confidence, the happiest part of my life was spent on board a ship. While we were together, you know, there was nothing to fear.\u201d\"}"
