          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"343840b569e328d21c336146\",\"rewritten_text\":\"He sprang up and gripped her arm hard. \u201cShow him to me. Which man is he? Point him out. I must see him!\u201d he cried; but right then the Duke of Berwick\u2019s four-in-hand drove between them, and once it had passed, the carriage they were seeking had already rolled out of the park. \u201cHe has gone,\u201d Sibyl said sadly. \u201cI wish you had seen him.\u201d \u201cI wish I had, for as surely as there is a God in heaven, if he ever does you harm, I shall kill him.\u201d She stared at him in horror. He said it again. The words slashed the air like a knife. People nearby began to gawk. A lady beside her gave a little laugh. \u201cCome away, Jim; come away,\u201d she murmured. He trailed after her stubbornly as she moved through the crowd. What he had declared filled him with grim satisfaction. When they came to the Achilles Statue, she turned back. Pity rested in her eyes, yet her lips broke into laughter. She shook her head at him. \u201cYou are foolish, Jim, utterly foolish; nothing but a bad-tempered boy. How can you utter such dreadful things? You have no idea what you\u2019re saying. You\u2019re simply jealous and cruel. Oh! I wish you would fall in love yourself. Love makes people kind, and what you said was wicked.\u201d \u201cI am sixteen,\u201d he retorted, \u201cand I know what I\u2019m doing. Mother is no protection to you. She hasn\u2019t a clue how to take care of you. I almost wish I were not heading to Australia. I feel tempted to throw it all up. I would, if my articles weren\u2019t already signed.\u201d \u201cOh, don\u2019t look so solemn, Jim. You are like one of those melodrama heroes Mother loved acting in. I won\u2019t quarrel with you. I have seen him, and oh! seeing him is perfect happiness. We won\u2019t quarrel. I know you would never harm anyone I love, would you?\u201d \u201cNot while you love him, I suppose,\u201d he muttered. \u201cI shall love him forever!\u201d she cried. \u201cAnd he?\u201d \u201cForever as well!\u201d \u201cHe had better.\u201d She recoiled from him, then laughed and laid her hand on his arm. After all, he was only a boy. At the Marble Arch they hailed an omnibus, which carried them close to their shabby place on the Euston Road. It was past five o\u2019clock, and Sibyl needed to lie down a couple of hours before performing. Jim insisted on it. He said he preferred to say goodbye while their mother was absent. She would surely make a scene, and he loathed scenes of every sort.\"}"
