          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"25dd443f4f45934da1a6275c\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Dawn had arrived when I set the manuscript aside. The rain had nearly stopped, the world looked gray and mournful, and the worn-out storm was sighing and sobbing itself to sleep. I went to the stranger\u2019s room and listened at his door, which stood slightly open. I heard his voice, so I knocked. There was no reply, though his voice continued. I peeked in. He lay on his back in bed, speaking in fits and starts but with energy, flinging his arms about restlessly like someone fevered and delirious. I slipped in quietly and bent over him. His mutterings and exclamations went on. I spoke\u2014just a word to get his attention. His glassy eyes and ashen face instantly lit up with pleasure, gratitude, joy, welcome.\\n\\n\u201cOh, Sandy, you\u2019ve come at last\u2014how I have longed for you! Sit beside me\u2014don\u2019t leave me\u2014never leave me again, Sandy, never again. Where is your hand?\u2014give it to me, dear, let me hold it\u2014there\u2014now everything is well, all is peaceful, and I\u2019m happy again\u2014we are happy again, aren\u2019t we, Sandy? You\u2019re so dim, so vague, you\u2019re only a mist, a cloud, but you are here, and that\u2019s blessing enough; and I have your hand; don\u2019t take it away\u2014it\u2019s only for a little while, I won\u2019t need it long.... Was that the child? ... Hello\u2014Central! ... she doesn\u2019t answer. Asleep, maybe? Bring her when she wakes, and let me touch her hands, her face, her hair, and tell her goodbye.... Sandy! Yes, you\u2019re there. I drifted for a moment and thought you were gone.... Have I been sick long? It must be so; it feels like months to me. And such dreams! such strange and terrible dreams, Sandy! Dreams as real as reality\u2014delirium, of course, but so real! I thought the king was dead, I thought you were in Gaul and couldn\u2019t get home, I thought there was a revolution; in the wild frenzy of these dreams, I imagined that Clarence, my cadets, and I fought and destroyed all of England\u2019s chivalry! But even that wasn\u2019t the strangest. I seemed to be a creature torn from some unborn age far in the future, and even that felt as real as the rest! Yes, I seemed to rush back from that age into our own, then forward again, and was dropped, a stranger, lonely in that unfamiliar England, with a gulf of thirteen centuries yawning between me and you! between me and my home and my friends! between me and all that I hold dear, all that could make life worth living!\u201d\"}"
