          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"267d698bbecf657bb7d79b6e\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cI\u2019m going, Master Will\u2014truly I am,\u201d the Black man replied promptly. \u201cAlmost out to the end now.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOut to the end?\u201d Legrand practically screamed. \u201cAre you saying you\u2019re all the way out on that limb?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAlmost to the end, sir\u2014o-o-o-oh! Lord have mercy! what\u2019s this on the tree?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell!\u201d cried Legrand, delighted. \u201cWhat is it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, it\u2019s nothing but a skull\u2014someone left his head up here, and the crows picked every bit of flesh off.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cA skull, you say! All right\u2014how\u2019s it fastened to the branch? What\u2019s holding it there?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSure enough, sir; let me look. Why, this is mighty curious, I swear\u2014there\u2019s a big nail in the skull fastening it to the tree.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNow, Jupiter, do exactly what I tell you\u2014understand?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cPay attention, then\u2014find the skull\u2019s left eye.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHuh! That\u2019s good! There isn\u2019t any eye left at all.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCurse your stupidity! Do you even know your right hand from your left?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, I know that\u2014I know everything about that\u2014it\u2019s my left hand I chop wood with.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOf course! You\u2019re left-handed, and your left eye is on the same side as your left hand. Now, I assume you can find the skull\u2019s left eye, or where it used to be. Have you found it?\u201d\\n\\nThere was a long silence. At last the man asked, \u201cIs the skull\u2019s left eye on the same side as its left hand too? Because the skull hasn\u2019t got a bit of a hand\u2014never mind! I\u2019ve got the left eye now\u2014here\u2019s the left eye! What should I do with it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLet the beetle drop through it as far as the string will reach\u2014but be careful not to let go of the string.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll done, Master Will; mighty easy thing to put the bug through the hole\u2014watch out down there!\u201d\\n\\nDuring this exchange no part of Jupiter\u2019s body could be seen, but the beetle he let down was now visible at the end of the string, glimmering like a polished gold globe in the last rays of the setting sun, some of which still faintly lit the high ground where we stood. The scarab hung clear of any branches and, if released, would have fallen at our feet. Legrand immediately grabbed the scythe and cleared a circular space three or four yards across directly beneath the insect, and, once he finished, he ordered Jupiter to drop the string and come down from the tree.\"}"
