          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"9e6033e112e40ef0121eab5f\",\"rewritten_text\":\"They were bringing along a fine-looking elderly gentleman, and a handsome younger fellow with his right arm trussed up in a sling. And land sakes, how the crowd hooted and hollered, and kept it going. But I couldn\u2019t spy any humor in it, and figured it\u2019d take all the duke and king had to spy any, either. I expected they\u2019d go white as sheets. But no, not a bit of color did they lose. The duke never let on he guessed the game, just kept goo-gooing around, cheerful and contented, like a jug gurgling out buttermilk; and the king, he only stared and stared down mournful at them new arrivals like it gave him a stomach cramp in the very heart to think the world held such cheats and scoundrels. Oh, he played it masterly. A heap of the leading folks crowded up around the king, to show they stood by him. That elderly gentleman newly arrived looked plum bewildered. After a minute he began to speak, and I could tell right off he talked _like_ an Englishman\u2014not the king\u2019s fashion, though the king\u2019s was tolerable for a sample. I can\u2019t give the old gent\u2019s exact talk, nor mimic him; but he swung round to the crowd, and said something like this:\\n\\n\u201cThis here is an astonishment to me that I wasn\u2019t expecting; and I confess, free and open, I ain\u2019t in good shape to meet it and answer it; for my brother and me has suffered misfortunes; he\u2019s cracked his arm, and our trunks got put off at a town up the river last night by a mistake. I\u2019m Peter Wilks\u2019 brother Harvey, and this here is his brother William, who can\u2019t hear nor speak\u2014and can scarce make signs fit to count, now he\u2019s only got one hand to do it with. We are who we claim; and in a day or two, when I fetch the baggage, I can prove it. Till then I won\u2019t say any more, but go to the hotel and wait.\u201d\\n\\nSo him and the fresh mute walked off; and the king he chuckles, and blurts out:\\n\\n\u201cBroken his arm\u2014_very_ likely, _ain\u2019t_ it?\u2014and mighty handy, too, for a cheat that\u2019s got to talk with signs and don\u2019t know how. Lost their baggage! That\u2019s _powerful_ rich!\u2014and mighty clever\u2014considering the _fix!_\u201d\\n\\nThen he laughed once more; and so did the rest, except maybe three or four, or maybe six. One of those was that doctor; another was a keen-faced gentleman, with an old-style carpet-bag made of carpet-cloth, that had just stepped off the steamboat and was speaking to him in a low tone, darting glances at the king now and again and nodding together\u2014it was Levi Bell, the lawyer that had gone up to Louisville; and another was a big rough husky chap that had come along and listened to every word the old gentleman said, and was listening to the king now.\"}"
