          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"e66773b6ae0fa676acb477c3\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Dear me, she could talk endlessly. It wouldn\u2019t do for me to hint that it was getting very late and that I was exhausted and sleepy. I wished I had gone to bed when I had the chance. Now I had to stay; there was no escape. So she kept tinkling along, and the sleeping castle was otherwise silent and ghostly, until at last there rose from somewhere deep below a distant sound, like a muffled shriek with such agony that it made my skin crawl. The queen stopped, her eyes lighting with delight; she tilted her graceful head like a bird listening. The sound forced its way up through the stillness again.\\n\\n\u201cWhat is it?\u201d I asked.\\n\\n\u201cIt is truly a stubborn soul, and it endures long. It has been many hours now.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cEndures what?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThe rack. Come\u2014you shall see a joyful sight. If he does not yield his secret now, you shall see him torn apart.\u201d\\n\\nWhat a silky smooth hellion she was; so calm and composed, while the cords down my legs tightened in sympathy with that man\u2019s pain. Guided by armored guards carrying blazing torches, we tramped through echoing corridors and down stone stairways that were damp and dripping and smelled of mold and ages of shut-up night\u2014a chill, eerie journey and a long one, and not made shorter or cheerier by the sorceress\u2019s talk about the sufferer and his crime. He had been accused by an anonymous informant of killing a stag in the royal preserves. I said:\\n\\n\u201cAnonymous testimony isn\u2019t quite right, your Highness. It would be fairer to bring the accused face to face with the accuser.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI had not thought of that, it being of little importance. But even if I wished to, I could not, for the accuser came masked by night, told the forester, then left at once, so the forester doesn\u2019t know him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen is this Unknown the only person who saw the stag killed?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo man saw the killing, but this Unknown saw this bold wretch near the spot where the stag lay and came with loyal zeal and betrayed him to the forester.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSo the Unknown was near the dead stag too? Isn\u2019t it possible he did the killing himself? His loyal zeal\u2014in a mask\u2014seems a bit suspicious. But what is your Highness\u2019s reason for racking the prisoner? Where is the gain?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHe will not confess otherwise; and then his soul would be lost. For his crime his life is forfeit by the law\u2014and surely I will see he pays it!\u2014but it would endanger my own soul to let him die unconfessed and without absolution.\u201d\"}"
