rtificate would be necessary. However, once Lord Arthur explained that he needed it for a large Norwegian mastiff that had to be dispatched because it was showing early signs of rabies and had already bitten the coachman twice on the calf, Mr. Pestle declared himself quite satisfied, praised Lord Arthur\u2019s remarkable knowledge of toxicology, and had the prescription prepared at once.\\n\\nLord Arthur slipped the capsule into a dainty little silver bonbonni\u00e8re he noticed in a Bond Street shop-window, tossed Pestle and Humbey\u2019s unsightly pill-box away, and drove straight to Lady Clementina\u2019s.\"}"
