          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"c4833b0c38bb9e90b3719805\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Biddy was in tears; the garden growing dim, the lane, and the stars beginning to show were blurred to me as well.\\n\\n\u201cNothing ever came to light, Biddy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNothing at all.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDo you know what has become of Orlick?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cJudging from the state of his clothes, I should imagine he is labouring at the quarries.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen you have seen him?\u2014Why fix your eyes on that dark tree down the lane?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI saw him there, the night she died.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat wasn\u2019t the final time, either, Biddy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo; I have noticed him there since we have been walking here.\u2014It is useless,\u201d said Biddy, laying her hand on my arm while I was ready to rush off, \u201cyou know I would not mislead you; he was scarcely there a minute, and he has gone.\u201d\\n\\nThe discovery that she was still dogged by this man flamed up my hottest anger, and I felt implacable toward him. I told her so, and said I would spend any money or endure any effort to hound him out of that district. Gradually she led me into calmer speech, and she spoke of Joe\u2019s love for me, and how Joe never murmured at anything,\u2014she didn\u2019t name me; she had no need; I understood her,\u2014but always did his duty in his station, with strong hands, a quiet tongue, and a tender heart.\\n\\n\u201cIndeed, one could hardly praise him too highly,\u201d said I; \u201cand Biddy, we must often talk of these matters, for of course I shall frequently be down here now. I have no intention of leaving poor Joe lonely.\u201d\\n\\nBiddy did not utter a word.\\n\\n\u201cBiddy, can\u2019t you hear me?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, Mr. Pip.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBesides your addressing me as Mr. Pip\u2014which strikes me as rather poor form, Biddy\u2014what is your meaning?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat do I mean?\u201d Biddy asked, timidly.\\n\\n\u201cBiddy,\u201d I said, with righteous self-assertion, \u201cI must insist on knowing what you mean by this?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBy this?\u201d repeated Biddy.\\n\\n\u201cNow, do not repeat,\u201d I snapped. \u201cYou used not to repeat, Biddy.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cUsed not!\u201d Biddy exclaimed. \u201cO Mr. Pip! Used!\u201d\\n\\nWell! I thought it best to drop that matter also. After another silent round through the garden, I returned to the principal point.\\n\\n\u201cBiddy,\u201d said I, \u201cI made a remark about my coming down here frequently to visit Joe, which you met with marked silence. Be so good as to tell me why.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAre you quite certain, then, that you WILL come to see him frequently?\u201d asked Biddy, pausing in the narrow garden path, and gazing at me beneath the stars with a clear and honest eye.\"}"
