          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"f95ebcc60a969b12fa577518\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cI consider it one of the first refinements of civilized societies.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDefinitely, sir; and it also has the advantage of being fashionable among the less civilized societies of the world: every savage can dance.\u201d\\n\\nSir William only smiled. \u201cYour friend dances wonderfully,\u201d he went on after a pause, having watched Bingley join the group. \u201cAnd I don\u2019t doubt that you\u2019re quite skilled yourself, Mr. Darcy.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou saw me dance at Meryton, I believe, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, indeed, and took considerable pleasure in the sight. Do you often dance at St. James\u2019s?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNever, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t you think it would be a proper compliment to the place?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s not a compliment I pay to any place if I can avoid it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou have a house in town, I suppose?\u201d\\n\\nMr. Darcy bowed.\\n\\n\u201cI once considered settling in town myself, for I\u2019m fond of first-rate company; but I wasn\u2019t entirely sure London\u2019s air would suit Lady Lucas.\u201d\\n\\nHe paused, hoping for a response, but his companion clearly wasn\u2019t inclined to give one; and just then Elizabeth moved toward them, which inspired him to attempt a very gallant gesture. He called out to her,\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Miss Eliza, why aren\u2019t you dancing? Mr. Darcy, you must allow me to present this young lady to you as a highly desirable partner. You surely can\u2019t refuse to dance when so much beauty is before you.\u201d And, taking her hand, he would have placed it in Mr. Darcy\u2019s, who, though quite surprised, wasn\u2019t unwilling to accept it, when she immediately pulled back and said, a little flustered, to Sir William,\\n\\n\u201cHonestly, sir, I have no intention of dancing. Please don\u2019t assume I came this way to ask for a partner.\u201d\\n\\nMr. Darcy, with grave courtesy, asked for the honor of her hand, but it was useless. Elizabeth was resolved; nor did Sir William shake her resolve with his attempt at persuasion.\\n\\n\u201cYou dance so well, Miss Eliza, that it\u2019s cruel to deny me the pleasure of watching you; and though this gentleman usually dislikes the amusement, I\u2019m sure he won\u2019t object to indulging us for half an hour.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMr. Darcy is the very picture of politeness,\u201d said Elizabeth, smiling.\\n\\n\u201cHe truly is. But with such enticement, my dear Miss Eliza, who can be surprised at his courtesy? Who would refuse such a partner?\u201d\\n\\nElizabeth gave him an impish look and turned away. Her refusal hadn\u2019t hurt her in the gentleman\u2019s estimation, and he was thinking of her with some satisfaction when Miss Bingley addressed him in this way,\u2014\"}"
