          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"7a7b55bb22d8af7ef48ba96e\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cI\u2019m in. It\u2019s the best plan. Should we just hold hands and swear that we\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh no, that\u2019s no good for this. That kind of thing only works for small, silly stuff\u2014especially with girls, because they\u2019ll turn on you anyway and spill everything if they get mad. But something this big needs writing. And blood.\u201d\\n\\nTom\u2019s whole being cheered this idea. It was deep, grim, and frightening; the hour, the situation, the setting all matched it. He picked up a clean pine shingle glinting in the moonlight, took a small piece of red chalk from his pocket, angled it toward the moon, and slowly scratched out these lines, biting his tongue on each downward stroke and easing up on the upward ones.\\n\\n\u201cHuck Finn and Tom Sawyer swear they will keep quiet about This and they wish they may drop dead on the spot if they ever tell and rot.\u201d\\n\\nHuckleberry was awed by Tom\u2019s skill with a pencil and the grandeur of his words. He immediately pulled a pin from his lapel to prick himself, but Tom stopped him.\\n\\n\u201cWait! Don\u2019t do that. A pin\u2019s brass. It might have verdigris on it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s verdigris?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s poison, that\u2019s what. Just swallow some once\u2014you\u2019ll find out.\u201d\\n\\nSo Tom unwound the thread from one of his needles, and each boy jabbed the pad of his thumb and squeezed out a drop of blood. After many squeezes, Tom finally managed to sign his initials, using the tip of his little finger as a pen. Then he showed Huckleberry how to make an H and an F, and the oath was sealed. They buried the shingle near the wall with some gloomy rites and muttered spells, and the bonds that held their tongues were declared locked with the key thrown away.\\n\\nA figure crept stealthily through a gap at the far end of the ruined building just then, but they didn\u2019t see it.\\n\\n\u201cTom,\u201d Huckleberry whispered, \u201cdoes this mean we can never tell\u2014ever?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOf course it does. No matter what happens, we have to stay quiet. We\u2019d drop dead\u2014don\u2019t you know that?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYeah, I guess that\u2019s true.\u201d\\n\\nThey kept whispering for some time. Suddenly a dog began a long, mournful howl just outside\u2014barely ten feet away. The boys grabbed each other, shaking with terror.\\n\\n\u201cWhich one of us is he warning?\u201d Huckleberry gasped.\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t know\u2014peek through the crack. Hurry!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, you do it, Tom!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI can\u2019t\u2014I can\u2019t do it, Huck!\u201d\"}"
