          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"4b6d10b4bba10c2a25acb753\",\"rewritten_text\":\"At these cries, many of the women, whipped into blind frenzy, spun around, striking and clawing their own friends until they collapsed in wild swoons. Only the men who belonged to them kept them from being trampled underfoot.\\n\\nStill, not a moment was wasted; not one moment! Foulon was at the Hotel de Ville and might be freed. Never, if Saint Antoine remembered his suffering, insults, and wrongs! Armed men and women poured out of the Quarter so quickly, pulling even the last dregs with them as if by suction, that in fifteen minutes only a few old crones and wailing children were left in Saint Antoine\u2019s heart.\\n\\nNo, by that time they were all jammed into the Hall of Examination where the old ugly villain sat, overflowing into the open space and streets. The Defarges, husband and wife, The Vengeance, and Jacques Three pushed in with the first crowd and stood close to him.\\n\\n\u201cLook!\u201d cried Madame, pointing with her knife. \u201cLook at the old monster bound with ropes. It was well done to tie that bundle of grass on his back. Ha, ha! Well done. Let him eat it now!\u201d She tucked the knife under her arm and clapped like she was watching a play.\\n\\nPeople immediately behind Madame Defarge explained what pleased her to those behind them, who passed it farther along, and so on, until the nearby streets echoed with clapping. Likewise, during two or three hours of slow talk and endless words, Madame Defarge\u2019s bursts of impatience were caught and repeated, almost instantly, even far away. Certain men had amazingly climbed the outside of the building to stare through the windows. They knew Madame Defarge well and acted like telegraphs between her and the crowd outside.\\n\\nAt last the sun rose high enough to shine a kind, hopeful beam directly on the old prisoner\u2019s head. The mercy was too much to stand; in a heartbeat the wall of dust and chaff that had held surprisingly long was blown away, and Saint Antoine had him.\\n\\nThe news spread at once, all the way to the edges of the crowd. Defarge had barely leaped over a railing and a table and squeezed the miserable creature in a deadly embrace\u2014Madame Defarge had barely followed and twisted one of the ropes that bound him\u2014The Vengeance and Jacques Three hadn\u2019t yet reached them, and the men at the windows hadn\u2019t yet swooped into the Hall like hawks from their high perches\u2014when the cry seemed to rise across the city: \u201cBring him out!\u201d\"}"
