          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"d53bb55b15f446c65aac90f1\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cI wrapped him in the paper and shoved a piece into his mouth\u2014like I said.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd you really think your master was bitten by the beetle, and that the bite made him ill?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI ain\u2019t guessing\u2014I know. Why else he dream \u2019bout the gold so much if it ain\u2019t \u2019cause the gold-bug bit him? I\u2019ve heard about them gold-bugs before now.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut how do you know he dreams about gold?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHow I know? Because he talks about it in his sleep\u2014that\u2019s how.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, Jup, maybe you\u2019re right. But what lucky event do I owe the honor of your visit today?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s wrong, massa?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDid you bring a message from Mr. Legrand?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, massa, I brought this here letter.\u201d Jupiter handed me a note that read:\\n\\n\u201cMy dear \u2014\u2014 Why have I not seen you for so long? I hope you haven\u2019t been foolish enough to take offense at some little brusqueness of mine; but no, that seems unlikely. Since I saw you I\u2019ve had great cause for worry. I have something to tell you, yet hardly know how to tell it, or whether I should at all.\\n\\n\u201cI haven\u2019t been well for a few days, and poor old Jup almost drives me mad with his well-meant care. Would you believe it?\u2014he prepared a huge stick the other day to beat me for slipping away and spending the day alone in the hills on the mainland. I truly think my sickly looks saved me from a whipping.\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019ve made no additions to my cabinet since we met.\\n\\n\u201cIf you can manage it, come over with Jupiter. Do come. I want to see you tonight on business of importance. I assure you it is of the highest importance.\\n\\n\u201cEver yours,\\n\u201cWilliam Legrand.\u201d\\n\\nThe tone of this note filled me with uneasiness. Its whole style was unlike Legrand\u2019s. What could he be thinking? What new whim seized his excitable mind? What \u201cbusiness of the highest importance\u201d could he have? Jupiter\u2019s story did not sound hopeful. I feared that steady misfortune had finally unhinged my friend\u2019s mind. So without hesitation, I got ready to go with the man.\\n\\nWhen we reached the wharf, I saw a scythe and three spades, all apparently new, lying in the bottom of the boat we were to take.\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s the meaning of this, Jup?\u201d\"}"
