          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"588c63c01b19b89f08141388\",\"rewritten_text\":\"A little after noon the boys borrowed a small skiff from a citizen who was away and pushed off right then. When they were several miles below Cave Hollow, Tom said: \u201cSee how this bluff looks the same all the way down from the cave hollow\u2014no houses, no wood-yards, just the same bushes. But do you see that white spot up there where a landslide happened? That\u2019s one of my marks. We\u2019ll go ashore now.\u201d They landed. \u201cNow, Huck, where we\u2019re standing you could touch that hole I came out of with a fishing pole. See if you can find it.\u201d Huck searched all around and found nothing. Tom proudly stepped into a thick bunch of sumach bushes and said: \u201cHere it is! Look at it, Huck; it\u2019s the tightest little hole in this country. Keep quiet about it. I\u2019ve always wanted to be a robber, but I knew I needed a place like this, and finding one was the trouble. Now we\u2019ve got it, and we\u2019ll keep it secret, though we\u2019ll let Joe Harper and Ben Rogers in\u2014because of course there has to be a Gang, or else it wouldn\u2019t have any style. Tom Sawyer\u2019s Gang\u2014it sounds grand, doesn\u2019t it, Huck?\u201d \u201cIt sure does, Tom. Who will we rob?\u201d \u201cOh, almost anyone. We\u2019ll ambush people\u2014that\u2019s mostly how.\u201d \u201cAnd kill them?\u201d \u201cNo, not always. Hide them in the cave until they come up with a ransom.\u201d \u201cWhat\u2019s a ransom?\u201d \u201cMoney. You make them get all they can from their friends; and after you\u2019ve kept them a year, if it isn\u2019t raised, then you kill them. That\u2019s the usual way. Only you don\u2019t kill women. You shut up the women, but you don\u2019t kill them. They\u2019re always beautiful and rich and terribly scared. You take their watches and things, but you always take off your hat and talk polite. Nobody is as polite as robbers\u2014you can see that in any book. Well, the women start loving you, and after they\u2019ve been in the cave a week or two they stop crying, and after that you couldn\u2019t get them to go away. If you drove them out they would turn right around and come back. It\u2019s that way in all the books.\u201d \u201cWhy, that\u2019s real bully, Tom. I think it\u2019s better than being a pirate.\u201d \u201cYes, it\u2019s better in some ways, because it\u2019s close to home and circuses and all that.\u201d By then everything was ready and the boys went into the hole, Tom leading. They worked their way to the far end of the tunnel, fastened their spliced kite strings, and moved on.\"}"
