          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"2863c7853b545791ef15b8e3\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cBut that hardly matters.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI might as well ask,\u201d she answered, \u201cwhy, if you meant to offend and insult me, you chose to confess that you liked me against your will, against your reason, and even against your character. Wasn\u2019t that enough excuse for me to be rude, if I was? But I have other grievances\u2014you know I do. Even if my feelings hadn\u2019t already been against you, even if they were neutral, or even favorable, do you imagine anything would persuade me to accept the man who has probably ruined, perhaps forever, the happiness of a sister I love more than anyone?\u201d\\n\\nAt these words, Mr. Darcy changed color; but the feeling quickly passed, and he listened without interrupting her while she went on\u2014\\n\\n\u201cI have every reason in the world to think the worst of you. No motive can excuse the unjust and ungenerous part you played there. You wouldn\u2019t dare, you couldn\u2019t deny that you were the main\u2014if not the sole\u2014cause of separating them, leaving one to be judged by the world for caprice and instability, the other to its ridicule for disappointed hopes, and dragging them both into the sharpest misery.\u201d\\n\\nShe stopped and, with growing anger, saw that he listened with an expression that showed he felt no remorse. He even gave her a smile of false disbelief.\\n\\n\u201cCan you deny you did it?\u201d she repeated.\\n\\nWith forced calm he replied, \u201cI have no desire to deny that I did everything I could to separate my friend from your sister, or that I\u2019m pleased it worked. Toward him I\u2019ve been kinder than toward myself.\u201d\\n\\nElizabeth refused to acknowledge this polite remark, though she understood it perfectly, and it certainly did nothing to soften her.\\n\\n\u201cBut my dislike isn\u2019t based solely on that,\u201d she continued. \u201cLong before that happened, my opinion of you was settled. Your character was revealed in the account I heard months ago from Mr. Wickham. What can you possibly say about that? What supposed act of friendship can you claim now? With what distortion can you deceive people here?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou seem very interested in that gentleman\u2019s affairs,\u201d Darcy said, less calmly and with a flush of anger.\\n\\n\u201cWho that knows his misfortunes could fail to care about him?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHis misfortunes!\u201d Darcy repeated with scorn. \u201cYes, they\u2019ve certainly been great.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd all caused by you,\u201d Elizabeth cried passionately. \u201cYou\u2019re the one who has brought him to his current state of poverty\u2014relative poverty.\u201d\"}"
