          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"a42962f9b92e6139ea0c96e0\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cYou have hardly stayed in Bath long enough,\u201d said he, \u201cto sample the evening parties here.\u201d \u201cOh! no. Their usual style offers nothing to me. I am no card-player.\u201d \u201cYou never were, I know. Cards were not to your taste then; but time alters many things.\u201d \u201cI am not yet so altered,\u201d Anne exclaimed, then faltered, uneasy at she scarcely knew what misconstruction. After a brief silence he spoke again, as if prompted by sudden feeling, \u201cIt is a span indeed! Eight years and a half is a span.\u201d Whether he meant to say more was left to Anne\u2019s imagination for a quieter moment; for even as his words still sounded in her ear, Henrietta, eager to seize the present leisure for an outing and urging her companions to make haste lest someone else arrive, startled her attention to other matters. They had to stir. Anne declared herself perfectly ready, and tried to seem so; yet she felt that had Henrietta known the regret and unwillingness in her heart at leaving that chair, at preparing to leave the room, she would have found in her own feelings for her cousin, in the very assurance of his attachment, ample cause to pity her. Their preparations, however, were abruptly checked. Alarming noises were heard; other visitors were approaching, and the door flew open for Sir Walter and Miss Elliot, whose entrance produced a general chill. Anne felt oppression at once, and wherever her eye roved she saw signs of the same. The comfort, freedom, and liveliness of the room vanished, subdued into cold composure, resolved silence, or flat talk, in order to match the heartless elegance of her father and sister. How mortifying to perceive it so! Her watchful eye was satisfied on one point. Captain Wentworth was recognized again by both, Elizabeth even more gracious than before. She spoke to him once, and looked at him more than once. Elizabeth was in truth meditating a great move. The result made it clear. After frittering away a few minutes with the proper nothings, she began to issue the invitation that was to cover all the remaining obligations to the Musgroves. \u201cTomorrow evening, to meet a few friends: no formal party.\u201d It was delivered very gracefully, and the cards she had brought, \u201cMiss Elliot at home,\u201d were placed on the table with a polite, inclusive smile for everyone, and one smile and one card most pointedly for Captain Wentworth. The fact was, Elizabeth had been in Bath quite long enough to appreciate the value of a gentleman whose air and appearance were like his.\"}"
