          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"62541b6d548577541b890929\",\"rewritten_text\":\"These thoughts calmed me, and by afternoon I fell into a deep sleep, though the fever in my blood kept peaceful dreams away. The awful scene from the day before played endlessly before my eyes: the women fleeing, Felix dragging me from his father\u2019s feet in fury. I awoke weak, saw it was already night, slipped out of my hiding place, and searched for food.\\n\\nOnce my hunger was satisfied, I followed the familiar path to the cottage. All was quiet there. I crept into my hovel and waited silently for the usual hour when the family would rise. That hour passed, the sun climbed high, yet no one appeared. I shook with fear, imagining some terrible misfortune. The inside of the cottage was dark, and no sound came from within; the agony of waiting is beyond words.\\n\\nTwo countrymen soon walked by, and when they paused near the cottage they began talking with fierce gestures. I could not understand them, for they spoke the local language, not that of my protectors. Soon afterward Felix arrived with another man; I was astonished, for he had not left the cottage that morning, and I listened anxiously to learn the meaning of these strange events.\\n\\n\u201cDo you realize,\u201d his companion asked, \u201cthat you will have to pay three months\u2019 rent and lose the harvest from your garden? I do not want to treat you unfairly, so please take a few days to think about your decision.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt is completely useless,\u201d Felix answered. \u201cWe can never live in your cottage again. My father\u2019s life is in extreme danger because of the horrible event I told you about. My wife and sister will never recover from their terror. Do not try to argue with me any longer. Take back your house and let me escape from this place.\u201d\\n\\nFelix shook violently as he spoke. He and his companion went into the cottage, stayed only a few minutes, and then left. I never saw any member of the De Lacey family again.\\n\\nI remained in my hovel for the rest of the day, sunk in dull despair. My protectors had gone and severed the only bond that tied me to the world. For the first time, feelings of revenge and hatred filled my heart, and I did nothing to resist them. Letting the current carry me, I turned my thoughts toward harm and death.\"}"
