          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"0b538d8d9085e64f34b00254\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The little man\u2019s body was disproportionately wide, lending his whole figure an absurd rotundity. His feet remained invisible, though now and then a horny-looking substance of dubious nature poked through a rip in the bottom of the car\u2014or rather, the top of his hat. His hands were huge, his hair an exceedingly gray queue gathered behind. His nose was monstrously long, crooked, and inflamed; his eyes round, gleaming, and sharp; his chin and cheeks, though lined with age, were broad, puffy, and double. Yet no hint of ears could be found anywhere on his head. This curious gentleman wore a loose sky-blue satin surtout with snug breeches of the same shade, each knee secured by silver buckles. His waistcoat was fashioned from some vivid yellow cloth; a white taffeta cap perched rakishly to one side; and, to finish his ensemble, a blood-red silk handkerchief swathed his neck and fell lightly on his chest in an elaborate, oversized bow of fantastical design.\\n\\nAfter descending, as mentioned, to roughly a hundred feet above the ground, the little elder was instantly overtaken by a bout of trepidation and seemed unwilling to come any closer to terra firma. Accordingly, he cast out a measure of sand from a canvas bag he could barely hoist, and in an instant he was motionless. Next, in hurried agitation, he pulled from a side pocket of his surtout a large morocco pocketbook. He balanced it warily in his palm, studied it with pure astonishment, and clearly marveled at its heft. Finally he opened it and produced a huge letter secured with red wax and neatly tied with red tape, which he dropped exactly at the feet of the burgomaster, Superbus Von Underduk. His Excellency bent to retrieve it. But the air-voyager, still terribly flustered and apparently having no further dealings in Rotterdam, immediately began feverish preparations to depart; and needing to jettison some ballast in order to rise again, he hurled out half a dozen bags, one after another, without bothering to empty them. Each and every one struck the burgomaster squarely in the back and sent him sprawling, somersaulting a full one-and-twenty times before the eyes of the entire city. Needless to say, the mighty Underduk did not allow such insolence from the little old man to go unchecked.\"}"
