          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"e73e2919624e4165456cde74\",\"rewritten_text\":\"From shop to shop I went, purchasing whatever the change in his appearance required. Once that business was settled, I set out for Little Britain on my own account. Mr. Jaggers, though at his desk when I entered, rose at once and planted himself before the fire.\\n\\n\u201cNow, Pip,\u201d he said, \u201cbe cautious.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI will, sir,\u201d I replied, for I had arranged in my mind, as I came along, what I meant to say.\\n\\n\u201cDo not commit yourself,\u201d Mr. Jaggers warned, \u201cand do not commit anyone. You grasp that\u2014anyone. Do not confide in me; I desire no information; curiosity does not trouble me.\u201d\\n\\nNaturally I perceived he knew the man had arrived.\\n\\n\u201cI merely desire, Mr. Jaggers,\u201d I said, \u201cto make sure that what I have been told is fact. I cherish no hope of its being otherwise, but at least I may verify it.\u201d\\n\\nMr. Jaggers nodded. \u201cBut did you say \u2018told\u2019 or \u2018informed\u2019?\u201d he inquired, with his head inclined and his gaze turned, listeningly, toward the floor. \u201cTold would suggest oral communication. One cannot converse orally with a man in New South Wales, you know.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI will say informed, Mr. Jaggers.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGood.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have been informed by a person called Abel Magwitch, that he is the benefactor so long concealed from me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat is the man,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, \u201cin New South Wales.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd only he?\u201d I asked.\\n\\n\u201cAnd only he,\u201d returned Mr. Jaggers.\\n\\n\u201cI am not so unreasonable, sir, as to regard you as in any way accountable for my errors and mistaken conclusions; yet I had always supposed it to be Miss Havisham.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAs you observe, Pip,\u201d replied Mr. Jaggers coolly, taking a bite at his forefinger, \u201cI bear no responsibility for that.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cStill, it seemed so like her, sir,\u201d I urged, heavy at heart.\\n\\n\u201cNot a trace of evidence, Pip,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, shaking his head and drawing up his skirts. \u201cTake nothing on appearances; rest everything on evidence. No better rule exists.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have nothing further,\u201d I sighed, after a brief silence. \u201cI have confirmed my information, and that is the end.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd Magwitch\u2014in New South Wales\u2014having now revealed himself,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, \u201cyou will recognize, Pip, how strictly in all my dealings with you I have held to the precise line of fact. There has never been the slightest deviation from the strict line of fact. You are fully aware of that?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cEntirely, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI informed Magwitch\u2014in New South Wales\u2014when he first wrote to me\u2014from New South Wales\u2014that he must not expect me to swerve from the strict line of fact.\u201d\"}"
