          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"91ec32315199e40b2492685d\",\"rewritten_text\":\"It seemed like a jumble of back lanes, ditches, and tiny gardens, giving off the air of a rather dull retreat. Wemmick\u2019s house was a small wooden cottage surrounded by garden plots, and the rooftop was cut out and painted to resemble a battery with guns.\\n\\n\u201cMy own handiwork,\u201d Wemmick said. \u201cLooks nice, doesn\u2019t it?\u201d\\n\\nI praised it highly; I think it was the smallest house I\u2019d ever seen, with the oddest Gothic windows (most of them blatantly fake) and a Gothic door barely big enough to squeeze through.\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s a real flagpole, you see,\u201d Wemmick continued, \u201cand on Sundays I run up a real flag. Then look here. After I cross this bridge, I haul it up\u2014like so\u2014and cut off the connection.\u201d\\n\\nThe bridge was only a plank spanning a gap about four feet wide and two feet deep. But it was delightful to watch the pride with which he hoisted it and secured it, smiling as he did so, with genuine enjoyment rather than mere routine.\\n\\n\u201cAt nine o\u2019clock every night, Greenwich time,\u201d said Wemmick, \u201cthe gun goes off. There he is, you see! And when you hear him fire, I think you\u2019ll agree he\u2019s a Stinger.\u201d\\n\\nThe cannon he mentioned was mounted in a separate little fortress made of latticework. It was shielded from the weather by a clever tarpaulin contraption shaped like an umbrella.\\n\\n\u201cThen, at the back,\u201d Wemmick said, \u201cout of sight so it doesn\u2019t interfere with the fortification theme\u2014because it\u2019s a principle with me: if you have an idea, carry it through and keep it up\u2014I don\u2019t know whether you agree\u2014\u201d\\n\\nI answered firmly that I did.\\n\\n\u201c\u2014At the back there\u2019s a pig, and there are chickens and rabbits; then I knock together my own frames, you see, and grow cucumbers; and you\u2019ll judge at supper what sort of salad I can produce. So, sir,\u201d said Wemmick, smiling again yet with a serious nod, \u201cif you imagine the little place under siege, it would hold out a devilishly long time when it comes to provisions.\u201d\\n\\nThen he led me to a bower about a dozen yards away, though the path twisted so cleverly that it took a good while to reach; in this hideaway our glasses were already set out. Our punch was chilling in an ornamental lake, on whose edge the bower stood. This pool\u2014circular in shape, with an island in the center that could just as well have supplied the salad for supper\u2014had a fountain he had built. When you set a little wheel going and pulled a cork from a pipe, it sprayed so strongly that it soaked the back of your hand.\"}"
