          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"c5ef726f2e7e543b3cc85f7f\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Yet for all this zeal, the boy grew only gloomier, paler, and more despondent. She added steaming baths, sitz baths, showers, and plunges. Tom stayed as mournful as a hearse. Next she supplemented the water regimen with thin oatmeal gruel and blister plasters. She gauged his capacity like that of a pitcher, stuffing him daily with patent remedies.\\n\\nBy now Tom had ceased to care about being tormented. This new attitude filled the old lady with alarm. The indifference had to be shattered no matter what. Just then she heard of Pain-killer for the first time. She ordered a supply immediately. One taste filled her with gratitude. It was nothing less than fire in liquid shape. She scrapped the water cures and everything else and concentrated her faith on Pain-killer. She delivered Tom a teaspoonful and watched, quivering with anxiety, for the effect. Her distress vanished at once, her soul settling into calm; the \u201cindifference\u201d had been smashed. The boy could not have displayed a livelier or more enthusiastic response if she had kindled a blaze beneath him.\\n\\nTom decided it was time to rouse himself; this existence might suit a ruined heart, but it was coming to hold too little romance and too much harrying variety. So he considered different escape plans and finally settled on pretending he fancied Pain-killer. He asked for it so frequently he became unbearable, and his aunt at last told him to serve himself and quit pestering her. Had it been Sid, her delight would have been unmixed; but since it was Tom, she kept a secret watch on the bottle. She noticed the medicine really dwindling, yet never guessed the boy was doctoring a crack in the sitting-room floor with it.\\n\\nOne afternoon Tom was in the act of dosing the crevice when his aunt\u2019s yellow cat strolled by, purring, eyeing the spoon greedily, begging for a sample. Tom said:\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t ask for it unless you want it, Peter.\u201d\\n\\nBut Peter indicated he did.\\n\\n\u201cYou better be sure.\u201d\\n\\nPeter was certain.\\n\\n\u201cNow you\u2019ve asked for it, and I\u2019ll hand it over, because there\u2019s nothing mean about me; but if you find it doesn\u2019t suit, you\u2019ve only yourself to blame.\u201d\\n\\nPeter consented. Tom pried the cat\u2019s jaws apart and poured in the Pain-killer. Peter shot two yards into the air, let out a war-whoop, and tore off around the room, crashing into furniture, knocking over flowerpots, and wreaking general destruction.\"}"
