          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"93cb4e6ec26750d96fc2900d\",\"rewritten_text\":\"One day, while I was bent over my studies with Mr. Pocket, the post brought me a note whose outer appearance alone sent my heart racing; for although I had never seen the handwriting, I guessed whose it must be. The note had no formal opening\u2014no Dear Mr. Pip, Dear Pip, Dear Sir, nor any such salutation\u2014but ran straight on in these words:\u2014\\n\\n\u201cI am to be in London the day after to-morrow by the midday coach. I believe it was arranged that you should meet me? At least Miss Havisham thinks so, and I write in compliance with her belief. She sends you her regards.\\n\\n\u201cYours, ESTELLA.\u201d\\n\\nHad there been sufficient time, I would likely have ordered several new suits for the occasion; lacking that, I had to make do with what I already possessed. My appetite vanished on the spot, and I found no peace or rest until the day came. Yet its coming brought no relief; I became more frantic than before and began haunting the coach-office in Wood Street, Cheapside, even before the coach had left the Blue Boar in our town. Though I knew this perfectly well, still I felt it perilous to let the coach-office out of sight for more than five minutes together; and in this unreasonable state I had completed the first half-hour of a four or five hour vigil when Wemmick collided with me.\\n\\n\u201cHalloa, Mr. Pip,\u201d said he; \u201chow do you do? I should hardly have imagined this was _your_ beat.\u201d\\n\\nI explained that I was waiting for someone arriving by coach, and asked after the Castle and the Aged.\\n\\n\u201cBoth thriving, thankee,\u201d said Wemmick, \u201cespecially the Aged. He\u2019s in rare feather. He\u2019ll be eighty-two next birthday. I have half a mind to fire eighty-two times, if the neighbourhood doesn\u2019t object and that little cannon of mine can stand the strain. However, this isn\u2019t London talk. Where do you suppose I\u2019m bound?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTo the office?\u201d said I, since he was heading that way.\\n\\n\u201cNearest thing to it,\u201d he answered. \u201cI\u2019m going to Newgate. We\u2019re engaged in a banker\u2019s-parcel affair at present, and I\u2019ve been down the road taking a look at the scene, so now I must have a word or two with our client.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDid your client commit the robbery?\u201d I inquired.\\n\\n\u201cBless your soul and body, no,\u201d replied Wemmick, very dryly. \u201cBut he\u2019s charged with it. So might you or I be. Either of us might be accused, you know.\u201d\"}"
