          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"c4ef83ccf938f705c8cfc07e\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The oaks around us were alive with a tribe of nightingales\u2014there I am now. Idris, glowing with young life, stands at my side\u2014remember, I am only twenty-two, and the beloved of my heart has barely seen seventeen summers. The river, swollen by autumn rains, flooded the low fields, and Adrian in his favorite boat amused himself with the dangerous game of snapping off the topmost branch of a submerged oak. Are you tired of life, Adrian, that you flirt with danger like this?\u2014\\n\\nHe has won his prize, and now he steers his boat through the flood. Our eyes stayed anxiously on him, but the current carried him away from us; he had to land much farther down and make a wide circle before he could return. \u201cHe is safe!\u201d said Idris when he sprang ashore and waved the bough over his head in triumph. \u201cWe will wait for him here.\u201d\\n\\nWe were alone. The sun had set. The nightingales began their song. The evening star shone sharply in the lingering glow of light in the west. My angel\u2019s blue eyes fixed on that sweet emblem of herself. \u201cHow the light pulses,\u201d she said, \u201cthat is the star\u2019s life. Its flickering shine seems to tell me its state, like ours on earth, is fragile and restless; it fears, I think, and it loves.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDo not gaze on the star, dear, generous friend,\u201d I cried. \u201cDo not read love in its trembling rays. Do not look to distant worlds or speak of the mere idea of a feeling. I have held my peace too long; so long I have been sick with the need to speak to you, to offer you my soul, my life, my whole existence. Do not look on the star, dear love\u2014or do, and let that eternal spark speak for me. Let it be my witness and advocate, silent as it shines. Love is to me as light is to that star; as long as it is not destroyed into darkness, I will love you.\u201d\\n\\nThat moment\u2019s ecstasy must stay veiled forever from the world\u2019s unfeeling gaze. Still I feel her graceful form against my overflowing heart; still my sight, pulse, and breath fail when I recall that first kiss. Slowly and quietly we walked to meet Adrian, whose footsteps we heard approaching.\\n\\nI begged Adrian to return to me after he brought his sister home. That same evening, strolling along the moonlit forest paths, I poured out to my friend my whole heart\u2014its joy and its hope. For a moment he seemed troubled. \u201cI might have foreseen this,\u201d he said. \u201cWhat struggle will now arise!\u201d\"}"
