          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"e087da4d92c0eb0863302a17\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cGood heavens!\u201d the Duchess thought, \u201che\u2019s some kind of chiropodist after all. How dreadful. I do hope he\u2019s at least foreign\u2014it wouldn\u2019t seem quite so bad then.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI absolutely must introduce him to you.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIntroduce him!\u201d cried the Duchess. \u201cYou don\u2019t mean he\u2019s here, do you?\u201d She began searching for a small tortoiseshell fan and a very frayed lace shawl so she could leave at a moment\u2019s notice.\\n\\n\u201cOf course he\u2019s here; I\u2019d never dream of throwing a party without him. He says I have a perfectly psychic hand, and that if my thumb were the slightest bit shorter I\u2019d be a confirmed pessimist and would have gone into a convent.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, I see,\u201d said the Duchess, greatly relieved. \u201cHe reads fortunes, I suppose?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd misfortunes as well,\u201d replied Lady Windermere. \u201cPlenty of them. Next year I\u2019m apparently in terrible danger on land and sea, so I\u2019m going to live in a balloon and haul up my dinner in a basket every evening. It\u2019s all written on my little finger, or the palm of my hand\u2014I forget which.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut surely that\u2019s tempting Providence, Gladys.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Duchess, surely Providence can resist temptation by now. I think everyone should have their palms read once a month, just to know what not to do. Of course, you go ahead and do it anyway, but it\u2019s such fun to be warned. If someone doesn\u2019t fetch Mr. Podgers immediately, I shall have to go myself.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAllow me, Lady Windermere,\u201d said a tall, handsome young man who had been listening with an amused smile.\\n\\n\u201cThank you so much, Lord Arthur, but I\u2019m afraid you wouldn\u2019t recognize him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIf he\u2019s as remarkable as you say, I can\u2019t very well miss him. Describe him and I\u2019ll bring him straight back.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, he\u2019s not the least like a palm reader. I mean he isn\u2019t mysterious or exotic or the least bit romantic-looking. He\u2019s a small, stout man with a funny bald head and big gold-rimmed spectacles\u2014something between a family doctor and a country solicitor. I\u2019m truly sorry, but there\u2019s nothing I can do. People are so exasperating. All my pianists look exactly like poets, and all my poets look exactly like pianists. I remember last season I invited a perfectly dreadful conspirator to dinner\u2014a man who had blown up scores of people, always wore chain mail, and carried a dagger up his sleeve\u2014and when he arrived he looked just like a pleasant old clergyman and spent the evening telling jokes.\u201d\"}"
