          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"157706416f5fc440782e8a82\",\"rewritten_text\":\"But in that vicious tirade against Chantilly that ran in yesterday\u2019s Mus\u00e9e, the satirist, tossing out some disgraceful digs about the cobbler changing his name when he took to the stage, quoted a Latin line we\u2019ve often discussed. I mean the line: Perdidit antiquum litera prima sonum.\\n\\n\u201cI told you it referred to Orion, which used to be written Urion, and because that explanation carried certain sharp hints, I knew you couldn\u2019t have forgotten it. So it was obvious you wouldn\u2019t fail to connect the ideas of Orion and Chantilly. I knew you made the connection from the kind of smile that crossed your lips. You thought of the poor cobbler\u2019s sacrifice. Up to then, you\u2019d been walking with a stoop, but now I saw you straighten to your full height. Then I knew you were thinking about Chantilly\u2019s small stature. At that point I broke into your thoughts to point out that since he was such a little fellow\u2014that Chantilly\u2014he\u2019d be better suited to the Th\u00e9\u00e2tre des Vari\u00e9t\u00e9s.\u201d\\n\\nNot long after that, we were scanning an evening edition of the Gazette des Tribunaux when the following paragraphs caught our eye.\\n\\n\u201cExtraordinary Murders.\u2014At about three o\u2019clock this morning, the residents of the Quartier St. Roch were jolted from their sleep by a series of terrifying shrieks, apparently coming from the fourth floor of a house on the Rue Morgue, occupied solely by a Madame L\u2019Espanaye and her daughter, Mademoiselle Camille L\u2019Espanaye. After a delay caused by failing to gain entry through the usual means, the gateway was smashed with a crowbar, and eight or ten neighbors entered with two gendarmes. By that time the screams had stopped; but as the group rushed up the first flight of stairs, they heard two or more harsh voices arguing angrily, seeming to come from higher up. By the time they reached the second landing, these sounds had also ceased and everything was completely silent. The group spread out and hurried from room to room. When they reached a large back chamber on the fourth floor (the door was found locked with the key inside and had to be forced open), they were confronted with a scene that filled everyone present with horror as much as astonishment.\\n\\n\u201cThe room was in total chaos\u2014the furniture was smashed and scattered in every direction. There was only one bedstead, but the mattress had been removed and dumped in the middle of the floor. On a chair lay a razor, smeared with blood.\u201d\"}"
        }
      ],
