          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"c023a89e7ffb153765109966\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Without warning Mr. Podgers released Lord Arthur\u2019s right hand, caught the left instead, and stooped so close in his scrutiny that the gold rims of his spectacles seemed to graze the palm. For an instant his features froze into a pale mask of terror, but he promptly regained his composure and, glancing up at Lady Windermere with a strained smile, declared, \u2018It is the hand of a delightful young gentleman.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Of course it is!\u2019 retorted Lady Windermere. \u2018But will he make a delightful husband? That is what interests me.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Every delightful young gentleman does,\u2019 replied Mr. Podgers.\\n\\n\u2018I am not sure a husband ought to be too fascinating,\u2019 mused Lady Jedburgh softly; \u2018it is frightfully risky.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018My dear child, they never are too fascinating,\u2019 cried Lady Windermere. \u2018But I require particulars. Particulars are the only things worth hearing. What lies ahead for Lord Arthur?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Within the next few months Lord Arthur will take a voyage\u2014\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Oh, certainly, his honeymoon, naturally!\u2019\\n\\n\u2018And he will lose a relative.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Not his sister, I trust?\u2019 said Lady Jedburgh anxiously.\\n\\n\u2018Most assuredly not his sister,\u2019 answered Mr. Podgers with a soothing gesture, \u2018only a distant kinsman.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018I am miserably let down,\u2019 exclaimed Lady Windermere. \u2018I shall have nothing to tell Sybil tomorrow. No one bothers about distant relatives now. They went out of fashion ages ago. Still, she had better keep a black silk handy; it always suits for church. And now we should get to supper. They will have devoured everything, but we may secure some hot soup. Fran\u00e7ois used to make splendid soup, but politics keep him so excited I never feel secure. I wish General Boulanger would behave himself. Duchess, surely you are worn out?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Not in the least, dear Gladys,\u2019 replied the Duchess, waddling toward the door. \u2018I have had an enchanting evening, and the cheiropodist\u2014 I mean cheiromantist\u2014 is most absorbing. Flora, where is my tortoise-shell fan? Oh, thank you, Sir Thomas, so very much. And my lace shawl, Flora? Thank you again, Sir Thomas, exceedingly kind\u2019; and the good soul contrived to reach the stairs without dropping her scent-bottle more than twice.\\n\\nMeanwhile Lord Arthur Savile had stayed motionless by the fireplace, oppressed by the same nameless terror, the same nauseating foreboding. He gave his sister a melancholy smile as she swept by on Lord Plymdale\u2019s arm, radiant in pink brocade and pearls, and scarcely registered Lady Windermere\u2019s summons to follow. Sybil Merton filled his thoughts, and the notion that anything might divide them brought tears to his eyes.\"}"
