          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"7fdf9635db9eeed219faf4b0\",\"rewritten_text\":\"This marriage is exactly right. I didn\u2019t think so at first, but I admit it now. The gods made Sibyl Vane for you. Without her you would have been incomplete.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThanks, Basil,\u201d said Dorian Gray, squeezing his hand. \u201cI knew you would understand me. Harry is so cynical that he frightens me. But here comes the orchestra. It\u2019s dreadful, but it only lasts about five minutes. Then the curtain goes up, and you will see the girl to whom I plan to give my entire life, to whom I have already given everything good in me.\u201d\\n\\nFifteen minutes later, amid an extraordinary roar of applause, Sibyl Vane stepped onstage. She was indeed lovely\u2014one of the loveliest creatures Lord Henry thought he had ever seen. There was something of a fawn in her shy grace and startled eyes. A faint blush, like the shadow of a rose on silver glass, touched her cheeks as she looked at the packed, excited audience. She stepped back a few paces and her lips seemed to tremble. Basil Hallward jumped to his feet and began applauding. Dorian Gray sat motionless, as if in a dream, staring at her. Lord Henry peered through his glasses, murmuring, \u201cCharming! Charming!\u201d\\n\\nThe scene was the hall of the Capulet house, and Romeo, in his pilgrim\u2019s costume, had entered with Mercutio and his other friends. The band, poor as it was, played a few bars of music, and the dance began. Through the crowd of clumsy, badly dressed actors, Sibyl Vane moved like someone from a finer world. Her body swayed as she danced, like a plant swaying in water. The curve of her throat was like that of a white lily. Her hands seemed carved from cool ivory.\\n\\nYet she seemed strangely dull. She showed no joy when her eyes met Romeo\u2019s. The few lines she had to speak\u2014\\n\\nGood pilgrim, you do wrong your hand too much,\\nWhich mannerly devotion shows in this;\\nFor saints have hands that pilgrims\u2019 hands do touch,\\nAnd palm to palm is holy palmers\u2019 kiss\u2014\\n\\nalong with the short dialogue that follows, were spoken in a completely artificial way. Her voice was exquisite, but the tone was entirely wrong. It lacked the right colour. It drained all life from the verse. It made the passion feel unreal.\\n\\nDorian Gray grew pale as he watched her, puzzled and worried. Neither of his friends dared say anything to him. To them she seemed utterly incompetent.\"}"
