{"request_id":"1bc4f813431ff95af446342b","rewritten_text":"While passing my hand through the valve to offer a cup of water to the old cat, the sleeve of my shirt snagged in the loop that held the basket, and in that instant I loosened it from its fastenings. If the whole affair had evaporated into thin air it could scarcely have vanished from my sight with more suddenness. Truly, not a tenth of a second could have elapsed between the basket’s release and its utter disappearance with everything inside. My well wishes pursued it earthward, yet I felt no expectation that either the cat or her kittens would survive to recount their misfortune.

“At six o’clock I saw a great stretch of the eastern horizon buried in thick shadow, which swept forward at high speed until, at five minutes to seven, the entire landscape lay wrapped in nighttime darkness. The balloon, however, remained bathed in the sun’s parting glow for a long while after; and though I had foreseen this, it delighted me beyond measure. Clearly, come morning, I should greet the rising luminary hours before the citizens of Rotterdam, despite their more easterly position, and thus, with each day and each increase in altitude, I would enjoy the sun’s light for longer spans. I now resolved to keep a journal of the voyage, counting the days in uninterrupted stretches of twenty-four hours, without regard to the intervals of night.

“At ten o’clock, feeling drowsy, I resolved to lie down for the remainder of the night; but a difficulty arose, obvious enough yet unnoticed by me until that moment. If I slept as planned, how was the air within the chamber to be renewed meanwhile? It would be impossible to breathe it for more than an hour at most, or, even stretching the limit to an hour and a quarter, the consequences might prove disastrous. This dilemma troubled me greatly; and it seems scarcely credible that, after all the perils already faced, I should contemplate it so seriously as to surrender any hope of achieving my final objective and to decide I must descend. Yet this wavering lasted only an instant.”}"}

