h her sister, for Jane had no attention to spare while he was around. But she found herself quite useful to both of them in those necessary intervals of separation. When Jane was absent, he always sought out Elizabeth so he could enjoy talking about her; and when Bingley was away, Jane always looked to Elizabeth for the same comfort. \u201cHe made me so happy,\u201d she said one evening, \u201cby telling me he had no idea I was in town last spring!\u201d\"}"
