          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"4b9222f45c2b648adec69699\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Sydney Carton paused in the street, still uncertain of his direction. \u201cAt Tellson\u2019s banking-house at nine,\u201d he murmured, his expression pensive. \u201cShall I show myself meanwhile? I believe so. These people ought to know that I am here; it\u2019s a sensible precaution, perhaps even an essential preparation. But caution, caution, caution! Let me deliberate!\u201d\\n\\nChecking the steps that had begun to veer toward a destination, he paced the already dim street once or twice more, tracing the course of his thoughts to their possible outcomes. His first idea stood firm. \u201cIt is best,\u201d he said, suddenly determined, \u201cthat these people should know there is such a man as I here.\u201d Then he turned his face toward Saint Antoine.\\n\\nThat day Defarge had described himself as the keeper of a wine-shop in the Saint Antoine quarter. For someone well acquainted with the city, locating his house without inquiry was not difficult. After finding the place, Carton emerged from those narrower streets again, dined at a small eating-house, and after dinner fell fast asleep. For the first time in years, he abstained from strong drink. Since the previous night he had taken only a little thin wine; and the night before he had poured the brandy slowly onto Mr. Lorry\u2019s hearth like a man finished with it.\\n\\nIt was as late as seven when he awoke refreshed and ventured into the streets again. On his way to Saint Antoine, he paused before a shop window containing a mirror to slightly tidy the loose knot of his cravat, his coat collar, and his unkempt hair. That done, he headed straight to Defarge\u2019s and went inside.\\n\\nOnly Jacques Three, with his twitching fingers and hoarse voice, stood there as a customer. This man, whom he had seen on the Jury, sipped at the little counter while conversing with Monsieur and Madame Defarge. The Vengeance joined the talk as if she were a regular fixture of the place.\\n\\nWhen Carton entered, sat down, and requested (in very indifferent French) a small measure of wine, Madame Defarge gave him a casual look, then a sharper one, sharper again, and finally stepped up to him to ask what he had ordered.\\n\\nHe repeated his request.\\n\\n\u201cEnglish?\u201d inquired Madame Defarge, inquisitively lifting her dark brows.\\n\\nAfter gazing at her, as if even a single French word came slow to him, he responded in the same strong foreign accent.\"}"
