{"request_id":"73b615f91041d5815104f166","rewritten_text":"Some time passed before I was calm enough to handle the regular duties of the balloon. When I finally examined it closely, I was greatly relieved to find it unhurt. All my tools were safe, and I had lost neither ballast nor supplies. I had secured them so well that such a loss was impossible. When I checked my watch, it was six o’clock. I was still climbing fast, and my barometer showed an altitude of three and three-quarter miles. Directly below me in the ocean lay a small black shape, slightly oblong, about the size and shape of a child’s domino. Looking through my telescope, I clearly saw it was a British ninety-four-gun ship, close-hauled and rising and falling heavily with her head to the west-southwest. Apart from this ship, I saw nothing but the sea, the sky, and the sun, which had long since risen.

“It is now time I explain to Your Excellencies the purpose of my dangerous voyage. You will recall that my hopeless situation in Rotterdam had finally driven me to plan suicide. It was not that I truly hated life, but that I was tormented beyond endurance by the external miseries of my condition. In this state, wanting to live yet tired of living, the treatise I found at the bookseller’s stall awakened my imagination. I then made my final decision. I would leave yet live—to quit the world yet continue to exist. To end the riddles, I resolved, whatever might happen, to force a passage to the moon if I could. So that you will not think me more insane than I am, I will explain, as well as I can, the reasons that convinced me that such an effort, though undeniably hard and full of danger, was not, for a bold spirit, beyond the limits of possibility.

“The moon’s true distance from Earth was the first point to consider. The average span between the centers of the two bodies is 59.9643 of Earth’s equatorial radii, or roughly 237,000 miles. I say average, but remember that the moon’s orbit is an ellipse with an eccentricity of 0.05484 of the ellipse’s major semi-axis, and Earth’s center sits at one focus. If I could somehow meet the moon, so to speak, at its perigee, the distance just mentioned would be considerably reduced.”"}

