          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"df41834ef90c082e757eaf7d\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cOh, I got you wrong. I thought you said \u2018anybody,\u2019 and so I assumed \u2018anybody\u2019 included\u2014well, anybody; meaning everybody.\u201d \u201cIt does\u2014anybody of high birth; and better still if he\u2019s royal.\u201d \u201cThat, it seems to me, might well be,\u201d said the abbot, seizing his chance to smooth things over and head off disaster. \u201cIt\u2019s unlikely that so marvelous a gift would be granted for revealing the affairs of lesser folk than those born near the heights of greatness. Our Arthur the king\u2014\u201d \u201cDo you wish to know of him?\u201d the enchanter cut in. \u201cMost gladly, yes, and gratefully.\u201d Instantly everyone was full of awe and interest again, the incorrigible fools. They watched the spells being cast with rapt attention and looked at me with a \u201cThere now, what do you say to that?\u201d expression when the announcement came: \u201cThe king is weary from the hunt, and has been lying in his palace these two hours, sleeping a dreamless sleep.\u201d \u201cGod\u2019s blessing on him!\u201d said the abbot, crossing himself. \u201cMay that sleep refresh his body and soul.\u201d \u201cAnd so it might, if he were sleeping,\u201d I said, \u201cbut the king isn\u2019t sleeping; the king is riding.\u201d Trouble again\u2014a clash of authority. No one knew which of us to believe; I still had some reputation. The magician\u2019s scorn was roused, and he said: \u201cI have seen many wonderful soothsayers and prophets and magicians in my day, but never one who could sit idle and perceive the truth of things without so much as an incantation.\u201d \u201cYou\u2019ve lived in the woods and missed a lot by it. I use incantations myself, as this good brotherhood knows\u2014but only on important occasions.\u201d When it comes to sarcasm, I can hold my own. That barb made the fellow squirm. The abbot asked after the queen and the court and received this answer: \u201cThey\u2019re all asleep, overcome by fatigue, just like the king.\u201d I said, \u201cThat\u2019s simply another lie. Half of them are busy with their entertainments; the queen and the other half aren\u2019t sleeping\u2014they\u2019re out riding. Now maybe you can show off a little and tell us where the king and queen, and whoever\u2019s riding with them right now, are heading?\u201d \u201cThey sleep now, as I said; but tomorrow they will ride, for they\u2019re going on a journey toward the sea.\u201d \u201cAnd where will they be the day after tomorrow at vespers?\u201d \u201cFar north of Camelot, with half their journey done.\u201d \u201cThat\u2019s another lie\u2014off by a hundred and fifty miles.\u201d\"}"
