          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"e98146eb4c031285c55c77b2\",\"rewritten_text\":\"So the ring-master got up and made a little speech, saying he hoped there wouldn\u2019t be any disturbance, and if the fellow would swear off causing any more trouble he could ride, provided he figured he could stay on the horse. Everyone laughed and agreed, and up the man climbed. No sooner was he seated than the horse began ripping and tearing and leaping and prancing, while two circus men clung to the bridle trying to keep him in hand, and the drunk clutched his neck, heels shooting sky-high with every bound, while the crowd rose up yelling and laughing till the tears streamed. At last, despite all the circus men\u2019s efforts, the horse busted loose and tore off like all creation around the ring, with that lush lying flat on him and hugging his neck, one leg nearly scraping the ground on one side, then the other leg on the other side, the folks near beside themselves. It wasn\u2019t a bit amusing to me; I shook all over watching his peril. But in a minute he fought his way astride again and caught the bridle, lurching this way and that; the next instant he sprang upright, dropped the bridle, and stood there, with the horse tearing along like a burning house. He simply stood there, floating around as calm and comfortable as if drink had never touched him\u2014and then he commenced peeling off his clothes and flinging them about. He shed them so fast they near clogged the air, and altogether he shed seventeen suits. And there he stood at last, lean and handsome, dressed as gaudy and fine as you ever saw, and he laid into that horse with his whip till the beast fairly buzzed\u2014and finally he hopped off, bowed, and danced away to the dressing-room, the crowd howling with delight and amazement.\\n\\nThen the ring-master realized how he had been duped, and he was the sickest ring-master you ever set eyes on, I\u2019d bet. Why, the joker was one of his own men! He had dreamed up that whole trick himself and breathed not a word to anyone. I felt plenty foolish being fooled so, but I wouldn\u2019t have stood in the ring-master\u2019s boots for a thousand dollars. Maybe there are bigger circuses than that one, but I haven\u2019t come across them yet. Anyhow, it suited me just fine; whenever I meet up with it again, it can count on getting all my trade every time.\"}"
