hat moment to make brisk preparations to leave; and since he had to unload some ballast in order to rise again, the half dozen bags he tossed out, one after another, without bothering to empty them, landed, every single one, squarely on the burgomaster\u2019s back and rolled him over and over no fewer than twenty-one times, right in front of everyone in Rotterdam. Nevertheless, one cannot assume that the great Underduk let this impertinence from the little old man go unpunished.\"}"
