          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"165d811b8d0921639a6b44e0\",\"rewritten_text\":\"These thoughts calmed me, and that afternoon I fell into a deep sleep, but the fever running through my blood kept peaceful dreams away. The horrible scene from the day before replayed endlessly before my eyes: the women fleeing, Felix raging as he tore me from his father\u2019s feet. I woke drained, realized night had already fallen, and crept out of my hiding place in search of food.\\n\\nOnce my hunger was satisfied, I headed along the familiar path that led to the cottage. Everything there was quiet. I slipped back into my hut and waited silently for the time when the family usually rose. That time came and went; the sun climbed high, yet the cottagers never appeared. I shook with dread, afraid some terrible misfortune had occurred. The cottage interior was dark, and I heard no movement; I cannot describe the torture of that suspense.\\n\\nSoon two countrymen passed by. They stopped near the cottage and began talking in animated gestures, but I could not understand their language, so different from that of my protectors. Shortly after, however, Felix arrived with another man. I was startled, knowing he had not left the cottage that morning, and I watched anxiously for some clue in their conversation to explain these strange events.\\n\\n\u201cDo you realize,\u201d his companion said, \u201cthat you\u2019ll have to pay three months\u2019 rent and lose the harvest from your garden? I don\u2019t want to take unfair advantage, so I beg you to take a few days to think about your decision.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s completely hopeless,\u201d Felix replied. \u201cWe can never live in your cottage again. My father\u2019s life is in grave danger because of the dreadful event I told you about. My wife and sister will never recover from their terror. Please don\u2019t argue with me. Take back your property and let me flee this place.\u201d\\n\\nFelix shook violently as he spoke. He and the other man went into the cottage, stayed only a few minutes, then left. I never saw any member of the De Lacey family again.\\n\\nI remained in my hovel the rest of the day, sunk in utter, stupefying despair. My protectors were gone, severing the only tie that bound me to mankind. For the first time, my heart filled with feelings of revenge and hatred, and I made no effort to resist them. Letting myself be carried away by that current, I turned my thoughts toward harm and death.\"}"
