          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"285859b95b480289c5dbb79c\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cStarve you? Oh, Mr. Ghost\u2014Sir Simon\u2014are you hungry? I have a sandwich in my bag. Would you like it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, thank you. I never eat anything now, but you are very kind, and far nicer than the rest of your nasty, rude, vulgar, dishonest family.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cStop!\u201d Virginia cried, stamping her foot. \u201cYou\u2019re the rude, horrid, vulgar one, and talking about dishonesty\u2014how dare you? You stole the paints from my box to try to touch up that absurd bloodstain in the library. You took every shade of red, even the vermilion, and I couldn\u2019t paint another sunset. Then you snatched the emerald green and the chrome yellow, and finally I had only indigo and Chinese white left, so all I could do were moonlit scenes, which are always grim to look at and terribly difficult to paint. I never told on you, though I was furious. The whole thing was ridiculous; who ever heard of emerald-green blood?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, really,\u201d said the Ghost, rather meekly, \u201cwhat else could I do? It\u2019s extremely hard to get real blood these days, and since your brother started it with his Paragon Detergent, I saw no reason I shouldn\u2019t use your paints. As for colour, that is entirely a matter of taste. The Cantervilles have blue blood, in fact the bluest in England, though I know you Americans don\u2019t care about such things.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou know nothing, and the best thing you can do is emigrate and broaden your mind. My father will gladly pay your fare, and although there\u2019s a heavy duty on spirits of any sort, there won\u2019t be any trouble with the Customs because the officers are all Democrats. Once in New York you\u2019ll be an instant success. I know plenty of people there who would pay a hundred thousand dollars for a grandfather, and more than that for a family ghost.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t think I should like America.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI imagine that\u2019s because we have no ruins or curiosities,\u201d Virginia said tartly.\\n\\n\u201cNo ruins! No curiosities!\u201d the Ghost retorted. \u201cYou have your navy and your manners.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGood evening. I\u2019ll go ask Papa to get the twins another week\u2019s vacation.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cPlease don\u2019t go, Miss Virginia,\u201d he cried. \u201cI\u2019m so lonely and unhappy, and I simply don\u2019t know what to do. I want to sleep, and I cannot.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s nonsense. All you need is to go to bed and blow out the candle.\u201d\"}"
