          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"6d1eb63d15bbf681bb98beff\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Well, I told him I wanted the watermelon. But he said I didn\u2019t need it for busting out of prison; that\u2019s where the hitch was. He said if I\u2019d wanted it to stash a knife in and slip it to Jim so he could stab the seneschal, that would have been acceptable. So I dropped it, though I couldn\u2019t see what good it did me to stand for a prisoner if I had to sit around and chew over a batch of gilt-edge distinctions like that every time I spotted a chance to swipe a watermelon.\\n\\nAnyway, like I was saying, we waited that morning till everybody had settled into their work and the yard was empty; then Tom carried the sack into the lean-to while I hung back a little to keep watch. Soon he came out, and we went and perched on the woodpile to talk. He says:\\n\\n\u201cEverything\u2019s settled now except tools; and that\u2019s simple enough.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTools?\u201d I says.\\n\\n\u201cYep.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTools for what?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, for digging. We aren\u2019t fixing to gnaw him out, are we?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAin\u2019t those wore-out picks and such in there good enough to dig a nigger out with?\u201d I says.\\n\\nHe wheels around on me, looking mournful enough to make a body cry, and says:\\n\\n\u201cHuck Finn, did you ever hear of a prisoner keeping picks and shovels and every modern convenience in his closet to dig himself free with? Now I got to ask you\u2014if you\u2019ve got a lick of reason in you\u2014what kind of a chance would that give him to be a hero? They might as well hand him the key and be done. Picks and shovels\u2014why, they wouldn\u2019t even let a king have such things.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, then,\u201d I says, \u201cif we don\u2019t want the picks and shovels, what do we want?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cA couple of case-knives.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTo scrape the foundations out from under that cabin with?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHang it, that\u2019s nonsense, Tom.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt don\u2019t matter how silly it seems, it\u2019s the proper way\u2014and the regular way. And there ain\u2019t no other way, that ever I heard of, and I\u2019ve read every book that gives any light on the subject. They always dig out with a case-knife\u2014and not through dirt, mind you; it\u2019s usually solid rock. And it takes them weeks and weeks and weeks, and forever besides. Why, think of that prisoner in the lowest cell of the Castle Deef, in the harbor of Marseilles, that carved himself out that way; how long do you calculate he was at it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t know.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, make a guess.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t know. Six weeks.\u201d\"}"
