t as he was to his? Were they, like him, simply puppets in a monstrous spectacle?\\n\\nStill, it wasn\u2019t the mystery but the absurdity of suffering that struck him\u2014the sheer uselessness of it, the grotesque lack of meaning. Everything felt jumbled, stripped of harmony. He marveled at the clash between the era\u2019s shallow optimism and the harsh truths of life. He was still very young.\\n\\nEventually he found himself standing before Marylebone Church. The silent roadway stretched out like a long ribbon of polished silver, dotted here and there with dark arabesques of shifting shadows.\"}"
