          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"cf5e12f64083cd463af765d2\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cI have two questions to ask you\u2014is that allowed?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou can ask,\u201d Monks replied, with a hint of surprise. \u201cWhether I answer is another matter.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat makes three,\u201d Mr. Bumble said in a weak attempt at wit.\\n\\n\u201cIs this what you expected from me?\u201d the matron demanded.\\n\\n\u201cIt is,\u201d said Monks. \u201cAnd the other question?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat are you going to do with it? Could it be used against me?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNever,\u201d said Monks. \u201cNot against me either. Look! But don\u2019t take a single step forward, or your life isn\u2019t worth a reed.\u201d\\n\\nWith that, he suddenly dragged the table aside. Grabbing an iron ring set into the floorboards, he yanked open a large trapdoor right at Mr. Bumble\u2019s feet, forcing the man to retreat several paces in a rush.\\n\\n\u201cLook down,\u201d Monks said as he lowered the lantern into the chasm. \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid of me. I could have dropped you without effort while you sat over it, if that had been my plan.\u201d\\n\\nReassured, the matron edged toward the rim, and even Mr. Bumble, driven by curiosity, inched forward. The murky water, swollen by heavy rain, roared below; all other sounds vanished in the rush and swirl against the green, slimy pilings. There had once been a mill there; the tide, foaming and raging around the remaining rotten stakes and scraps of machinery, seemed to race forward with fresh fury once free of the useless barriers that had tried to slow it.\\n\\n\u201cIf you threw a man\u2019s body down there, where would it be by morning?\u201d Monks asked, swinging the lantern over the dark shaft.\\n\\n\u201cTwelve miles downriver, hacked to pieces,\u201d Bumble answered, shrinking from the idea.\\n\\nMonks pulled the small packet from inside his coat, where he had stuffed it in haste, tied it to a lead weight from an old pul