w\u2014and to blush for your unworthiness in bearing his name.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat does the name have to do with anything?\u201d the other asked, half silently and half in stubborn amazement at the other\u2019s emotion. \u201cWhat is that name to me?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNothing,\u201d said Mr. Brownlow, \u201cnothing to you. But it was hers, and even after all this time it brings back to me, an old man, the warmth and thrill I once felt just hearing a stranger repeat it. I\u2019m very glad you changed it\u2014very, very glad.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThis is all very impressive,\u201d said Monks (still holding to his assumed name) after a long silence, during which he had twisted himself in sullen defiance, while Mr. Brownlow sat with his face shaded by his hand.\"}"
