          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"aba5e9e5bfcc4dc86af7f5b7\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cI\u2019m very ignorant, and it troubles me\u2014just a little.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTell me what it is.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have a cousin, my only relative and an orphan like me, whom I love dearly. She\u2019s five years younger than I am and lives on a farm in the south. Poverty separated us, and she knows nothing of what has become of me\u2014for I cannot write, and even if I could, how could I explain everything? It\u2019s better as it is.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, yes: better as it is.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat I have been thinking as we walked here, and what I still think now as I look into your kind, strong face that gives me so much support, is this: If the Republic truly helps the poor, if they become less hungry and suffer less in every way, she might live a long time. She might even grow old.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat then, my gentle sister?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDo you think\u201d\u2014the patient eyes, so full of endurance, fill with tears, and her lips part a little more and tremble\u2014\u201cthat it will feel long to me while I wait for her in the better world where I trust both you and I will be mercifully sheltered?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt cannot be, my child; there is no Time there, and no trouble there.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou comfort me so much! I\u2019m so ignorant. Should I kiss you now? Is it time?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes.\u201d\\n\\nShe kisses his lips; he kisses hers; they bless each other solemnly. His free hand doesn\u2019t shake as he lets go; nothing worse than a sweet, bright steadfastness shows in her patient face. She steps forward before him\u2014she is gone; the knitting women count Twenty-Two.\\n\\n\u201cI am the Resurrection and the Life, saith the Lord: he that believeth in me, though he were dead, yet shall he live: and whosoever liveth and believeth in me shall never die.\u201d\\n\\nThe murmur of many voices, faces lifted upward, the push of countless footsteps at the edge of the crowd, swelling forward like one great heave of water, all vanish. Twenty-Three.\\n\\n*****\\n\\nThey said of him, throughout the city that night, that his was the most peaceful face ever seen there. Many added that he looked sublime and prophetic.\\n"
