          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"fb134036b615e4421098ad0b\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Just then his eyes, and mine as well, fell on the scrap of parchment, which I first thought was plain paper. It lay half buried in the sand, with one corner sticking out. Nearby I noticed the remains of what looked like the hull of a ship\u2019s longboat. The wreck must have been there a very long time, because it was barely recognizable as boat timbers.\\n\\n\u201cAnyway, Jupiter picked up the parchment, wrapped the beetle in it, and handed it to me. Soon after, we started for home and ran into Lieutenant G\u2014\u2014. I showed him the insect, and he begged to take it to the fort. When I agreed, he immediately slipped it into his waistcoat pocket, without the parchment it had been wrapped in, which I still held while he inspected the beetle. Maybe he was afraid I might change my mind and wanted to secure his prize right away\u2014you know how passionate he is about anything related to natural history. At the same time, without realizing it, I must have put the parchment in my own pocket.\\n\\n\u201cYou remember I went to the table to sketch the beetle and found no paper where it was usually kept. I checked the drawer and nothing was there. I searched my pockets, hoping for an old letter, when my hand touched the parchment. I\u2019m giving you the exact details because the whole incident struck me strongly.\\n\\n\u201cSurely you\u2019ll think I\u2019m fanciful, but I already felt a sort of connection. I had two links in a longer chain: a boat on a shoreline, and near the boat a parchment\u2014not paper\u2014with a skull drawn on it. Naturally you ask, \u2018What is the connection?\u2019 I answer that the skull, or death\u2019s-head, is the well-known symbol of pirates. The death\u2019s-head flag is raised in every battle.\\n\\n\u201cI said the scrap was parchment, not paper. Parchment lasts a long time\u2014almost forever. People rarely use it for trivial matters, since it is not as convenient as paper for everyday writing or drawing. That made me suspect there was some meaning\u2014some purpose\u2014to the death\u2019s-head. I also noticed the shape of the parchment. Even though one corner had been damaged somehow, it was still clear that the original shape was oblong.\u201d}\"}"
