{"request_id":"ada975bc3d71fc94014eb40a","rewritten_text":"Each listener compares the mysterious voice not to the speech of any people whose language he knows, but to one he does not. The Frenchman thinks it belongs to a Spaniard and says he might have understood some words if he knew Spanish. The Dutchman insists it was a French voice, yet he himself had to testify through an interpreter because he does not know French. The Englishman believes it was a German voice, though he admits he does not understand German. The Spaniard is certain it was an Englishman, judging only by tone since he knows no English. The Italian thinks it was Russian, but he has never spoken with a native of Russia. Another Frenchman disagrees with the first and is sure it was Italian, though he does not know that language and, like the Spaniard, bases his belief on tone alone. How truly unusual must that voice have been, to draw such testimony—so strange that people from five major parts of Europe could find nothing familiar in its sound! You may say it could have been an Asiatic or an African. Few Asiatics or Africans live in Paris, but without rejecting the idea, I want to emphasize three points. One witness calls the voice “harsh rather than shrill.” Two others say it was “quick and unequal.” None of them could make out words or even word-like sounds.

“I cannot tell,” Dupin went on, “what impression I have made on you so far, but I say confidently that even this part of the testimony—the part about the gruff and shrill voices—allows one honest conclusion that should guide the rest of our investigation. I said ‘honest conclusions,’ but that phrase is not strong enough. I mean that these conclusions are the only proper ones, and that the suspicion follows from them inevitably as the single result. What that suspicion is, I will not yet reveal. I want you merely to remember that, with me, it was strong enough to give a clear direction to my search in the chamber.

“Let us now imagine ourselves inside that chamber. What should we search for first? The path or exit the killers used. Neither of us believes in supernatural events.”"}

