          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"14a281900374e468e7384442\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Naturally he was very entertaining and all that, but I was terribly disappointed; and when I asked him about the coat of mail, he only laughed and said it was far too cold to wear in England. Ah, here comes Mr. Podgers! Now, Mr. Podgers, I want you to read the Duchess of Paisley\u2019s hand. Duchess, you\u2019ll have to take off your glove. No, not the left hand, the other one.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Dear Gladys, I honestly don\u2019t think it\u2019s quite proper,\u2019 said the Duchess, weakly unfastening a rather grimy kid glove.\\n\\n\u2018Nothing interesting ever is,\u2019 said Lady Windermere. \u2018_On a fait le monde ainsi_. But I must introduce you. Duchess, this is Mr. Podgers, my favored palmist. Mr. Podgers, this is the Duchess of Paisley, and if you dare say she has a higher Mount of the Moon than I do, I\u2019ll never trust you again.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018I\u2019m sure, Gladys, there\u2019s nothing of the sort in my hand,\u2019 said the Duchess seriously.\\n\\n\u2018Your Grace is quite right,\u2019 said Mr. Podgers, glancing at the plump little hand with its short square fingers. \u2018The Mount of the Moon is not pronounced. The life line, however, is excellent. Please bend the wrist. Thank you. Three clear lines on the rascette! You will live to a great age, Duchess, and be extremely happy. Ambition\u2014very moderate, line of intellect not exaggerated, line of heart\u2014\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Now, do be indiscreet, Mr. Podgers,\u2019 cried Lady Windermere.\\n\\n\u2018Nothing would please me more,\u2019 said Mr. Podgers, bowing, \u2018if the Duchess had ever been indiscreet, but I regret to say that I see great steadfastness of affection combined with a strong sense of duty.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Please go on, Mr. Podgers,\u2019 said the Duchess, looking delighted.\\n\\n\u2018Economy is far from the least of your Grace\u2019s virtues,\u2019 continued Mr. Podgers, and Lady Windermere burst into fits of laughter.\\n\\n\u2018Economy is an excellent thing,\u2019 remarked the Duchess complacently. \u2018When I married Paisley he had eleven castles and not a single place fit to live in.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018And now he has twelve houses and not a single castle,\u2019 cried Lady Windermere.\\n\\n\u2018Well, my dear,\u2019 said the Duchess, \u2018I like\u2014\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Comfort,\u2019 said Mr. Podgers, \u2018and modern conveniences, and hot water laid on in every bedroom. Your Grace is absolutely right. Comfort is the only thing our civilization truly gives us.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018You\u2019ve described the Duchess\u2019s character perfectly, Mr. Podgers, and now you must tell Lady Flora\u2019s.\u2019 At a nod from the smiling hostess, a tall girl with sandy Scottish hair and high shoulder blades stepped awkwardly out from behind the sofa and held out a long, bony hand with spatulate fingers.\\n\\n\u2018Ah, a pianist! I can see it,\u2019 said Mr. Podgers. \u2018An excellent pianist, though perhaps not quite a musician.\u2019\"}"
