{"request_id":"b37b89d239013312a1a2eb48","rewritten_text":"I really wasn’t worried about her. People called her a remarkable woman, and she could handle things on her own without my help. Honestly, I think she always saw me as a lazy dreamer, good for nothing but building castles in the air, and she was probably relieved to be rid of me. It was a dark night when I said goodbye, and with the three creditors who had caused me so much trouble acting as my assistants, we carried the balloon, along with the car and equipment, by a roundabout route to the station where the other items were stored. Everything was still undisturbed when we arrived, and I got to work immediately.

“It was the first of April. As I’ve said, the night was dark; not a star in view, and a steady drizzle made us miserable. My main worry, though, was the balloon itself. Despite the protective varnish, it was starting to get heavy with moisture, and the powder risked getting ruined. I kept the three debt collectors busy, pounding ice around the central cask and stirring the acid in the others. Still, they pestered me with questions about what I intended to do with all this equipment and grumbled about the brutal work. They couldn’t see, they said, what good could come of getting drenched just to take part in such ghastly rituals. I grew anxious and worked as hard as I could, because I truly believed the fools thought I’d made a deal with the devil, and that what I was doing had crossed the line. I feared they’d abandon me altogether. I managed to calm them with promises to settle every debt in full as soon as I finished this endeavor. They, of course, took those assurances to mean that I expected to get my hands on a vast sum of cash. As long as I paid what I owed—and perhaps a bit extra for their trouble—I doubt they cared what happened to my soul or my body.

“After about four and a half hours, the balloon was inflated enough. I attached the car and loaded all my instruments into it—making sure I included the condensing apparatus, plenty of water, and a large supply of provisions like pemmican, which packs a great deal of nourishment into a small space.”"}

