          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"9da8d422164f76fded26cbd1\",\"rewritten_text\":\"And after forwarding them, I couldn\u2019t stay away from their whereabouts, but felt as though they were more hopeful and less resigned when I was near. In that pointless unease and anguish of spirit, I would wander the streets at dusk, passing those offices and houses where I\u2019d left the appeals. To this day, the tired western streets of London on a cold, dusty spring night, with their lines of severe, shuttered mansions and their endless ranks of lamps, remain sorrowful to me from that association.\\n\\nMy daily visits to him were curtailed now, and he was kept under stricter watch. Seeing, or imagining, that I was suspected of intending to carry him poison, I asked to be searched before sitting by his bedside, and told the officer always present that I was ready to do anything to convince him of the purity of my purpose. No one was severe with him or with me. There was duty to be done, and it was done, though not harshly. The officer constantly assured me he was worse, and the other sick prisoners in the room, along with the prisoners attending them as nurses\u2014criminals, yet not without kindness, thank God!\u2014always echoed the same news.\\n\\nAs the days passed, I observed ever more that he would lie calmly, gazing at the white ceiling, with no light in his face until some word of mine lit it for a moment, only to fade again. At times he could barely speak, or not at all, and would respond with faint pressures of my hand, which I soon learned well enough to interpret.\\n\\nThe count of days had reached ten when I saw a greater change in him than ever before. His eyes turned toward the door and brightened as I entered.\\n\\n\u201cDear boy,\u201d he said when I sat by his bed. \u201cI thought you\u2019d come late. But I knowed you couldn\u2019t be that.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt is just the time,\u201d I replied. \u201cI waited for it at the gate.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou always waits at the gate; don\u2019t you, dear boy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes. So as not to lose a minute.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThank\u2019ee, dear boy, thank\u2019ee. God bless you! You\u2019ve never forsaken me, dear boy.\u201d\\n\\nI squeezed his hand silently, unable to forget that I had once meant to forsake him.\\n\\n\u201cAnd what\u2019s best of all,\u201d he said, \u201cyou\u2019ve been more at ease with me when I lay under a dark cloud than when the sun was bright.\u201d\"}"
