quiet them and asked the prisoner if it was true he had lived many years in England.\\n\\nUndeniably, it was.\\n\\nWas he not then an emigrant? What did he call himself?\\n\\nHe hoped he was not, according to the meaning and intent of the law.\\n\\nWhy not, demanded the President.\\n\\nBecause he had willingly given up a title and position that repelled him and had left his country\u2014he argued that this happened before the word emigrant was used with the Tribunal\u2019s current meaning\u2014to support himself in England by his own labor rather than live on the labor of France\u2019s already overburdened people.\"}"
