          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"d4dd7f2b607993f0c8b8ac26\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The doctor proved to be an elderly fellow; a very pleasant, gentle-looking old gentleman when I roused him. I told him me and my brother had been over on Spanish Island hunting yesterday afternoon, and we\u2019d camped on a bit of raft we\u2019d found, and around midnight he must have kicked his gun while dreaming, because it went off and hit him in the leg, and we wanted the doctor to go over there and patch him up and not breathe a word about it or let anyone find out, since we planned to come home this evening and surprise the folks.\\n\\n\u201cWho are your folks?\u201d he asks.\\n\\n\u201cThe Phelpses, down yonder.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh,\u201d he says. After a pause he asks:\\n\\n\u201cHow\u2019d you say he got shot?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHe had a dream,\u201d I says, \u201cand it shot him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cQueer sort of dream,\u201d he says.\\n\\nSo he lit his lantern, grabbed his saddle-bags, and we set out. But when he spotted the canoe he didn\u2019t like her looks\u2014said she\u2019d do for one person, but she didn\u2019t seem safe for two. I says:\\n\\n\u201cOh, don\u2019t be uneasy, sir, she carried the three of us easy enough.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat three?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, me and Sid, and\u2014and\u2014and the guns; that\u2019s what I mean.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh,\u201d he says.\\n\\nStill, he put his foot on the gunwale and rocked her, shook his head, and said he guessed he\u2019d look for a bigger one. But they were all locked and chained up; so he took my canoe, told me to wait till he came back, or I could keep searching, or maybe I\u2019d better head home and get them ready for the surprise if I fancied. But I said I wouldn\u2019t; so I gave him exact directions how to find the raft, and off he went.\\n\\nI struck on an idea soon after. I says to myself, suppose he can\u2019t patch that leg in three shakes of a sheep\u2019s tail, like the saying goes? Suppose it takes three or four days? What then? Do we sit there till he spills the secret? No, sir; I know what I\u2019ll do. I\u2019ll wait, and when he comes back, if he says he has to go again, I\u2019ll get down there too, even if I\u2019ve got to swim; and we\u2019ll tie him up and hold him, and push off down the river; and once Tom\u2019s through with him we\u2019ll pay him what it\u2019s worth, or everything we\u2019ve got, and then let him reach shore.\\n\\nAfter that I crawled into a lumber-pile to grab some sleep; and the next time I woke the sun was high overhead! I rushed out and headed for the doctor\u2019s house, but they said he\u2019d gone out sometime during the night and hadn\u2019t come back yet.\"}"
