          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"dfe0974d58b2a88c05e575cd\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cStarve me to death? Oh, Mr. Ghost\u2014I mean Sir Simon\u2014are you hungry? I have a sandwich in my bag. Do you want it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, thank you. I never eat anything now. But it\u2019s very kind of you, all the same, and you\u2019re much nicer than the rest of your dreadful, rude, vulgar, dishonest family.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cStop!\u201d Virginia cried, stamping her foot. \u201cYou\u2019re the one who\u2019s rude and dreadful and vulgar, and as for dishonesty, you know perfectly well you stole the paints from my box to touch up that ridiculous bloodstain in the library. First you took all my reds, even the vermilion, so I couldn\u2019t paint any more sunsets. Then you took the emerald green and the chrome yellow, and finally I had nothing left but indigo and Chinese white, so I could only paint moonlit scenes, which are always depressing to look at and not at all easy to paint. I never told on you, though I was very angry, and the whole thing was absurd\u2014who ever heard of emerald-green blood?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, really,\u201d said the Ghost, rather meekly, \u201cwhat else could I do? It\u2019s very hard to get real blood these days, and since your brother started it with his Paragon Detergent, I saw no reason why I shouldn\u2019t use your paints. As for color, that\u2019s a matter of taste. The Cantervilles have blue blood, the very bluest in England, but I know you Americans don\u2019t care about such things.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou don\u2019t know anything about it, and the best thing you can do is emigrate and broaden your mind. My father would be delighted to give you a free passage, and though there\u2019s a high duty on spirits of every kind, there won\u2019t be any trouble at Customs, because the officers are all Democrats. Once you\u2019re in New York, you\u2019ll be enormously popular. I know plenty of people who would pay a hundred thousand dollars to have a grandfather and much more than that to have a family ghost.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t think I\u2019d like America.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI suppose that\u2019s because we have no ruins and no curiosities,\u201d Virginia said sarcastically.\\n\\n\u201cNo ruins! No curiosities!\u201d the Ghost replied. \u201cYou have your navy\u2014and your manners.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGood evening. I\u2019ll go ask Papa to give the twins an extra week off school.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cPlease don\u2019t go, Miss Virginia,\u201d he cried. \u201cI\u2019m so lonely and so unhappy, and I really don\u2019t know what to do. I want to go to sleep, and I can\u2019t.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s ridiculous. You just go to bed and blow out the candle.\u201d\"}"
