          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"a0ef26e428b01e51e22904a0\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Yesterday\u2019s \u201cMus\u00e9e\u201d carried that bitter tirade against Chantilly, where the satirist, making a few disgraceful remarks about the cobbler changing his name when he took to the stage, quoted a Latin line we have often discussed: Perdidit antiquum litera prima sonum. I had told you it referred to Orion, once written Urion; and because there is a sharp joke tied to that explanation, I knew it was impossible for you to have forgotten it. It was obvious you would connect Orion with Chantilly. I knew you had done so from the smile that crossed your face. You were picturing the poor cobbler\u2019s sacrifice. Until then you had been bent over in your walk, but I saw you straighten to your full height. At that moment I was sure you were thinking about Chantilly\u2019s tiny stature. I broke into your thoughts to remark that, since he truly was a very small fellow, he would fit better at the Th\u00e9\u00e2tre des Vari\u00e9t\u00e9s.\\n\\nSoon after, we were reviewing an evening issue of the \u201cGazette des Tribunaux\u201d when the following notice caught our eyes.\\n\\n\u201cExtraordinary Murders.\u2014This morning, around three o\u2019clock, the residents of Quartier St. Roch were jolted from sleep by a stream of terrible screams apparently coming from the fourth story of a house on Rue Morgue. The building was known to belong solely to Madame L\u2019Espanaye and her daughter, Mademoiselle Camille L\u2019Espanaye. There was a delay when the initial attempts to gain entry in the usual way failed, but at last the gateway was broken with a crowbar, and eight or ten neighbors entered, joined by two gendarmes. By then the cries had stopped; yet as the group rushed up the first flight of stairs, they heard two or more rough voices in angry dispute, seeming to come from the upper part of the house. On reaching the second landing, those sounds also ceased, and everything fell perfectly still. The group spread out, hurrying from one room to another. When they reached a large back chamber on the fourth floor, they found the door locked with the key on the inside, so they forced it open. A sight awaited them that shocked everyone with both horror and astonishment.\\n\\n\u201cThe room was in complete chaos. Furniture had been smashed and tossed everywhere. There was only one bedstead, and the mattress had been stripped from it and flung into the middle of the floor. A razor lay on a chair, its blade coated with blood.\u201d\"}"
        }
