          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"b90be8ed621f6840276b9b8f\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The heft of the insect was genuinely astonishing, and, all things considered, I could scarcely condemn Jupiter for his notion of it; yet how Legrand could be in accord with that notion baffled me entirely.\\n\\n\u201cI sent for you,\u201d he began, with a lofty air, once I had finished examining the beetle, \u201cI sent for you to gain your counsel and help in promoting the plans of Fate and of the bug\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Legrand,\u201d I broke in, \u201cyou are truly unwell and would do well to take precautions. You shall go to bed, and I will stay with you for a few days until you recover. You are feverish and\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFeel my pulse,\u201d he said.\\n\\nI felt it and, to be honest, found not the faintest hint of fever.\\n\\n\u201cBut someone may be ill without fever. Let me prescribe just this once. First, go to bed. Next\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou are mistaken,\u201d he cut in. \u201cI am as well as one might expect, given the excitement I endure. If you truly wish me well, you must ease this agitation.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd how is that to be managed?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cQuite simply. Jupiter and I are setting out on an expedition into the hills on the mainland, and for this expedition we need someone we can trust. You are the only person suitable. Whether we succeed or fail, the excitement you see in me will be calmed either way.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019m eager to oblige you in any fashion,\u201d I answered. \u201cBut do you mean this cursed beetle is tied to your trip into the hills?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt is.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen, Legrand, I cannot lend myself to such an absurd enterprise.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI regret it\u2014deeply\u2014for we shall have to undertake it alone.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDo it alone! The man must be insane!\u2014but wait!\u2014how long do you expect to be away?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMost likely all night. We are leaving at once and shall return, in any event, by sunrise.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd will you pledge me, on your honor, that once this whim of yours is concluded and the bug affair (good heavens!) resolved to your liking, you will go home and follow my advice implicitly, as though it came from your physician?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, I promise. Now let us go, for we have no time to waste.\u201d\\n\\nWith a heavy heart I went along with my friend. We set out around four o\u2019clock\u2014Legrand, Jupiter, the dog, and myself. Jupiter carried the scythe and spades, insisting on bearing the whole set\u2014more, it seemed to me, from fear of leaving any implement within his master\u2019s reach than from any particular zeal or docility.\"}"
