          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"02ce60e1379c8628b0f520cb\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWhat\u2019s wrong?\u201d\\n\\nI said,\\n\\n\u201cPap, and Mom, and Sis, and\u2014\u201d\\n\\nThen I choked up. He said,\\n\\n\u201cOh, darn it now, don\u2019t take it so hard; we all have to face trouble, and this one\u2019ll turn out fine. What\u2019s happened to them?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThey\u2019re\u2014they\u2019re\u2014are you the watchman on this boat?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYeah,\u201d he said, sounding downright pleased. \u201cI\u2019m the captain and the owner and the mate and the pilot and the watchman and the head deckhand; and sometimes I\u2019m the freight and the passengers too. I\u2019m not as rich as old Jim Hornback, and I can\u2019t be as blasted generous and nice to Tom, Dick, and Harry as he is, throwing money around like it\u2019s nothing; but I\u2019ve told him plenty of times I wouldn\u2019t swap places with him, because, says I, a sailor\u2019s life is the life for me, and I\u2019ll be darned if I\u2019d live two miles out of town where nothing ever happens, not for all his money and twice that besides. Says I\u2014\u201d\\n\\nI cut in and said,\\n\\n\u201cThey\u2019re in a terrible lot of trouble, and\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWho is?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, Pap and Mom and Sis and Miss Hooker; and if you\u2019d take your ferry boat and head up there\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHead up where? Where are they?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOn the wreck.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat wreck?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, there\u2019s only one.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat, you don\u2019t mean the Walter Scott?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGood heavens! What on earth are they doing there, for goodness\u2019 sake?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, they didn\u2019t go there on purpose.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019ll bet they didn\u2019t! Why, my Lord, they don\u2019t stand a chance if they don\u2019t get off real quick! How in the world did they ever get into a mess like that?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cEasy enough. Miss Hooker was visiting up there in town\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYeah, Booth\u2019s Landing\u2014keep going.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cShe was visiting at Booth\u2019s Landing, and right toward evening she started across with her enslaved woman on the horse ferry to stay the night at her friend\u2019s place, Miss What\u2019s-her-name\u2014I can\u2019t remember\u2014and they lost their steering oar, and swung around and drifted down, stern first, about two miles, and ran aground on the wreck, and the ferryman and the enslaved woman and the horses were all lost, but Miss Hooker grabbed hold and got onto the wreck. Well, about an hour after dark we came drifting down in our trading scow, and it was so dark we didn\u2019t see the wreck until we were right on top of it; so we ran aground too; but all of us were saved except Bill Whipple\u2014and oh, he was the best soul!\u2014I almost wish it had been me instead, I do.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy word! That\u2019s the most unbelievable thing I ever heard.\u201d\"}"
