          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"f83bc2d3db62a227747840a3\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cDo you come back often?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have never been here since.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNor I.\u201d\\n\\nThe moon began to rise, and I thought of that calm face turned to the white ceiling, now gone. The moon rose higher, and I thought of the pressure of his hand when I spoke the last words he ever heard.\\n\\nEstella broke the silence between us.\\n\\n\u201cI have often wanted and planned to return, but many things stopped me. Poor, poor old place!\u201d\\n\\nThe silver mist caught the first moonlight, and the same light shone on the tears that fell from her eyes. Not knowing I saw them, and trying to master them, she said quietly,\\n\\n\u201cWere you wondering, as you walked, how it came to be left like this?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, Estella.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThe ground belongs to me. It is the only thing I have kept. Everything else has slipped away bit by bit, but I held on to this. It was the only thing I fought for in all those miserable years.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWill they build on it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAt last, they will. I came to say goodbye before it changes. And you,\u201d she added, her voice tender to a wanderer, \u201cdo you still live abroad?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cStill.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd are doing well, I am sure?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI work hard enough for a decent living, and so\u2014yes, I do well.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have often thought of you,\u201d Estella said.\\n\\n\u201cHave you?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLately, very often. For a long hard time I kept away any memory of what I had thrown away when I didn\u2019t know its value. But since duty no longer forbids that memory, I have given it a place in my heart.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou have always had your place in my heart,\u201d I replied.\\n\\nWe were silent again until she spoke.\\n\\n\u201cI never thought,\u201d Estella said, \u201cthat I would say goodbye to you while saying goodbye to this place. I am very glad to do so.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGlad to part again, Estella? Parting is painful to me. The memory of our last parting has always been sad and painful.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut you said to me,\u201d Estella answered earnestly, \u201c\u2018God bless you, God forgive you!\u2019 If you could say that then, you won\u2019t hesitate to say it now\u2014now, when suffering has taught me more than anything else, and taught me what your heart once was. I have been bent and broken, but\u2014I hope\u2014into a better shape.\u201d\"}"
