          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"1c23d1c672a29402f88aacc1\",\"rewritten_text\":\"For an instant I was too astonished to reason clearly. I knew my design differed in its particulars from this one\u2014though its general form bore a certain likeness. Soon I took up a candle, and seating myself at the opposite end of the room, examined the parchment more intently. On flipping it over, I saw my own sketch on the reverse, precisely as I had drawn it. My first reaction was simple amazement at the truly striking similarity of outline\u2014at the curious accident that, unbeknown to me, there lay a skull on the other side of the parchment directly beneath my figure of the scarab\u00e6us, and that this skull matched my drawing not only in shape but in dimensions. I declare, the oddity of this coincidence completely stunned me for a while. This is a common effect of such coincidences. The mind strives to forge a link\u2014to find a chain of cause and effect\u2014and, failing, lapses into a kind of momentary numbness. Yet, once I emerged from the stupor, another conviction dawned on me gradually, startling me even more than the coincidence. I began distinctly, unequivocally, to recall that no drawing had appeared on the parchment when I made my sketch of the scarab\u00e6us. I grew utterly certain; I remembered turning up first one side, then the other, searching for the cleanest portion. Had the skull been there then, I must have observed it. Here, indeed, was a mystery I felt incapable of explaining; but even at that early stage, there seemed to flicker, deep in the most hidden recesses of my mind, a glow-worm spark of the truth which last night\u2019s adventure later proved so splendidly. I rose at once, secured the parchment, and set aside all further speculation until I could be alone.\\n\\n\u201cWhen you had left, and Jupiter was sound asleep, I undertook a more systematic inquiry into the matter. First of all, I reviewed the way the parchment had come into my hands. The spot where we found the scarab\u00e6us lay on the mainland coast, about a mile east of the island and only a short distance above the high-water line. When I grasped it, it nipped me smartly, causing me to drop it. Jupiter, with characteristic caution, before seizing the insect, which had flown towards him, looked around for a leaf\u2014or something of the sort\u2014with which to take hold of it.\u201d\"}"
