          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"cfaae879849fe9aecb7b2589\",\"rewritten_text\":\"All this, and much more, I would gladly explain. But to be brief, I must have my reward. I long to return to my family and my home; and in exchange for any further information from me\u2014considering the insight I can offer into many significant branches of physical and metaphysical science\u2014I must request, through the influence of your honorable body, a pardon for the crime I committed in causing the death of the creditors when I left Rotterdam. This is the purpose of the present paper. Its bearer, a resident of the moon whom I persuaded and properly instructed to serve as my messenger to Earth, will await Your Excellencies\u2019 decision and bring back the requested pardon, if it can be obtained in any fashion.\\n\\n\u201cI have the honor to be, etc., Your Excellencies\u2019 very humble servant,\\n\\n\u201cHANS PFAALL.\u201d\\n\\nAfter finishing this extraordinary document, Professor Rub-a-dub dropped his pipe in pure shock, and Mynheer Superbus Von Underduk, having removed his spectacles, wiped them, and placed them in his pocket, forgot both himself and his dignity so completely that he spun around three times on his heel in the purest astonishment and admiration. There was no doubt\u2014the pardon must be secured. So swore Professor Rub-a-dub in a hearty oath, and so decided the illustrious Von Underduk, as he took the arm of his fellow scholar and, without a word, headed straight home to consider what steps to take. However, when they reached the burgomaster\u2019s door, the professor dared to suggest that since the messenger had chosen to disappear\u2014no doubt terrified by the fierce appearance of the burghers of Rotterdam\u2014the pardon would be useless, as no one but a man from the moon would undertake a journey of such distance. The burgomaster agreed, and so the matter was finished. Rumors and theories, however, were far from over. The letter, once published, sparked endless chatter and speculation. Some of the self-important even made fools of themselves by declaring the whole affair nothing but a joke. But \u201choax\u201d seems to be a catchall term for these people, used for anything beyond their understanding. For my part, I do not see what evidence they rely on for such a claim. Let us examine what they say: \"}"
