          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"57bfb30b1823ac1b190f050d\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Soon his voice rang out in something like a halloo. \u201cHow much fudder I got for go?\u201d \u201cHow high up are you?\u201d asked Legrand. \u201cEbber so fur,\u201d the negro answered; \u201ckin see de sky fru de tip ob de tree.\u201d \u201cNever mind the sky\u2014pay attention to me. Look back along the trunk and count the limbs on this side beneath you. How many have you gone by?\u201d \u201cOne, two, tree, four, fibe\u2014I done pass fibe big limb on dis side, massa.\u201d \u201cThen climb one branch higher.\u201d Within a few minutes the voice called again, declaring he had reached the seventh limb. \u201cNow, Jup,\u201d cried Legrand, plainly much agitated, \u201cwork your way out along that branch as far as you can; if anything odd catches your eye, let me know.\u201d Whatever slight doubts I still harbored about my unfortunate friend\u2019s sanity were finally dispelled; I could only conclude he was quite deranged, and began to worry in earnest about getting him home. While I was debating the best course, Jupiter\u2019s voice came once more. \u201cMos\u2019 afeard to go fur on dis limb\u2014him dead limb pritty much all de way.\u201d \u201cYou said the limb is dead, Jupiter?\u201d Legrand cried, his voice shaky. \u201cYes, massa, dead as any door-nail\u2014done for sartin\u2014done depart dis life.\u201d \u201cIn the name of heaven, what am I to do?\u201d Legrand exclaimed in deep distress. \u201cDo?\u201d said I, glad for a chance to intervene. \u201cWhy, come home and go to bed. Come along!\u2014be sensible. It\u2019s late, and you remember your promise.\u201d \u201cJupiter,\u201d he shouted, ignoring me entirely, \u201cdo you hear?\u201d \u201cYes, Massa Will, hear you plain enough.\u201d \u201cThen test the wood with your knife and tell me if it seems very rotten.\u201d \u201cHim rotten, massa, sure nuff,\u201d the negro replied shortly, \u201cbut not so berry rotten as he might be. Could venture little ways on de limb by myself, dat\u2019s true.\u201d \u201cBy yourself?\u2014what are you talking about?\u201d \u201cMean de bug, sir. \u2019Tis _berry_ heavy bug. Spose I drop him down fus, den de limb won\u2019t crack wid only one nigger.\u201d \u201cYou infernal rascal!\u201d Legrand cried, evidently relieved, \u201cwhat nonsense is that? If you let that beetle fall I\u2019ll wring your neck. Look here, Jupiter, do you hear me?\u201d \u201cYes, massa; no need for hollerin\u2019 so at poor nigger.\u201d \u201cVery well, then pay attention! If you will hazard the limb only as far as you judge safe, keeping the beetle secure, I\u2019ll give you a silver dollar the instant you come down.\u201d\"}"
