          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"8c2c8ddc7cbac77aea1e7468\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWhat\u2019s the trouble?\u201d\\n\\nI said, \u201cPap, and Mam, and Sis, and\u2014\u201d Then I broke down. He said, \u201cOh, dang it, don\u2019t get so upset; we all have our troubles, and this one will come out all right. What\u2019s wrong with them?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThey\u2019re\u2014they\u2019re\u2014are you the boat\u2019s watchman?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes,\u201d he said, sounding pretty pleased. \u201cI\u2019m the captain, owner, mate, pilot, watchman, and head deckhand; and sometimes I\u2019m the freight and the passengers, too. I\u2019m not as rich as old Jim Hornback, and I can\u2019t be as generous to Tom, Dick, and Harry as he is, throwing money around the way he does; but I\u2019ve told him plenty of times I wouldn\u2019t trade places. I said, a sailor\u2019s life is the life for me, and I\u2019m darned if I\u2019d live two miles out of town where nothing ever happens, not for all his money and twice more on top. I said\u2014\u201d\\n\\nI cut in and said, \u201cThey\u2019re in terrible trouble, and\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWho is?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, Pap and Mam and Sis and Miss Hooker; and if you\u2019d take your ferryboat and go up there\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cUp where? Where are they?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOn the wreck.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat wreck?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, there\u2019s only one.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat, you don\u2019t mean the Walter Scott?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGood heavens! What are they doing there, for goodness\u2019 sake?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, they didn\u2019t go there on purpose.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019ll bet they didn\u2019t! Why, great goodness, they won\u2019t stand a chance if they don\u2019t get off quick! How in the world did they get into such a mess?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cEasy enough. Miss Hooker was visiting up in the town\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, Booth\u2019s Landing\u2014go on.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cShe was visiting there at Booth\u2019s Landing, and near evening she set out with her Black woman in the horse ferry to stay overnight at her friend\u2019s house, Miss What\u2019s-her-name\u2014I forget her name\u2014and they lost their steering oar, swung around, and floated down stern first about two miles, and slammed into the wreck. The ferryman, the Black woman, and the horses were all lost, but Miss Hooker grabbed hold and got on the wreck. Well, about an hour after dark we came down in our trading scow, and it was so dark we didn\u2019t notice the wreck till we were right on it; so we hit it too. All of us were saved except Bill Whipple\u2014and oh, he was the best creature! I almost wish it had been me instead.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy George! It\u2019s the strangest thing I ever ran into.\u201d\"}"
