          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"3637d0ac1f3ebfcb17605d36\",\"rewritten_text\":\"When the wedding took place about three weeks later, St. Peter\u2019s was packed with a crowd of fashionable people. The Dean of Chichester read the service with great solemnity, and everyone agreed they had never seen a more striking couple than the bride and groom. They were more than attractive\u2014they were happy. Lord Arthur never once regretted what he had endured for Sybil, and she gave him the best gifts a woman can give a man\u2014devotion, tenderness, and love. Their romance stayed alive despite daily life. They always felt young.\\n\\nSome years later, after they had two beautiful children, Lady Windermere visited Alton Priory, a lovely old place that had been the Duke\u2019s wedding gift to his son. One afternoon, she sat with Lady Arthur beneath a lime tree in the garden, watching the little boy and girl running up and down the rose walk like flickering sunbeams. Suddenly she took her hostess\u2019s hand and asked, \u201cAre you happy, Sybil?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDear Lady Windermere, of course I\u2019m happy. Aren\u2019t you?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have no time to be happy, Sybil. I always like the last person introduced to me, but once I really know them I usually grow bored.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t your lions satisfy you, Lady Windermere?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHeavens, no! Lions are only amusing for one season. Once their manes are trimmed, they become the dullest creatures imaginable. Besides, they behave terribly if you\u2019re truly kind to them. Do you remember that awful Mr. Podgers? He was a complete fraud. I didn\u2019t mind that, and I even forgave him when he tried to borrow money, but I couldn\u2019t tolerate his flirting with me. He made me detest palmistry. I\u2019ve taken up telepathy now. It\u2019s much more entertaining.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou mustn\u2019t speak poorly of palmistry here, Lady Windermere; it\u2019s the one topic Arthur doesn\u2019t like people to joke about. I assure you he takes it very seriously.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou don\u2019t mean he actually believes in it, Sybil?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAsk him, Lady Windermere\u2014here he is.\u201d Lord Arthur came up the garden path carrying a large bunch of yellow roses, his two children dancing around him.\\n\\n\u201cLord Arthur?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, Lady Windermere?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou can\u2019t mean you believe in palmistry?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOf course I do,\u201d the young man replied with a smile.\\n\\n\u201cBut why?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBecause I owe all the happiness of my life to it,\u201d he said quietly, as he sank into a wicker chair.\"}"
