rthur felt a curious emotion and could not explain it. There was something in the dawn\u2019s fragile beauty that seemed unbearably sad, and he thought of the days that begin in loveliness and end in storms. These countrymen, too, with their rough cheerful voices and their casual ways\u2014what a strange London they witnessed! A London without the sin of night or the smoke of day, a pallid, ghostly city, a deserted town of tombs. He wondered what they made of it, and whether they knew anything of its splendour and its shame, of its fierce, flaming pleasures and its terrible hunger, of all it creates and ruins between sunrise and nightfall.\"}"
