          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"6bfabdd249f1ae07fcd93bf2\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Tom managed to scrape the cupboard with it and was about to commence on the bureau when a summons came for him to dress for Sunday-school.\\n\\nMary handed him a tin basin of water and a cake of soap, and he stepped outside to the little bench by the door, set the basin down, dipped the soap once, and laid it aside. He rolled up his sleeves, poured the water gently onto the ground, then slipped back into the kitchen to rub his face industriously on the towel behind the door. But Mary snatched the towel away, saying:\\n\\n\u201cNow aren\u2019t you ashamed, Tom. You mustn\u2019t act that way. Water won\u2019t harm you.\u201d\\n\\nTom felt slightly taken aback. The basin was filled anew, and this time he lingered over it, collecting courage; he drew in a great breath and set to work. When he shuffled into the kitchen again with both eyes shut, feeling about for the towel, suds and water provided credible evidence on his face. Yet when he emerged from the towel he still failed inspection: the clean portion halted at his chin and jaw like a mask, while below stretched a gloomy sweep of untouched earth that ran down his front and around his neck. Mary seized control, and when she finished he was a man and a brother, color distinctions swept away; his soaked hair was neatly brushed, its short curls coaxed into a dainty, even arrangement. [He secretly worked the curls out with hard effort and plastered his hair flat to his head, for he thought curls effeminate and his own tormented him endlessly.] Mary fetched a suit that had been worn only on Sundays for two years\u2014simply called his \u201cother clothes\u201d\u2014which tells us all we need about his wardrobe. After he dressed, the girl put him in order: she buttoned his trim roundabout up to his chin, pulled his broad collar down over his shoulders, brushed him off, and set his speckled straw hat atop him. He looked greatly improved and extremely uncomfortable. He felt exactly as ill at ease as he appeared; whole garments and cleanliness pinched him. He hoped Mary would overlook his shoes, but that wish perished; she smeared them well with tallow, as was customary, and brought them forth. He lost his temper and complained that he was forever being driven to do what he least desired.\"}"
