          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"3cac0e531e181ede8d4e398d\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Were our lofty visions destined to vanish thus? Our title had proclaimed us \u201ca little lower than the angels,\u201d and lo, we proved no more enduring than ephemeral beings. We had styled ourselves \u201cthe paragon of animals,\u201d yet behold\u2014only a \u201cquintessence of dust.\u201d We lamented that the pyramids survived the embalmed forms of their ancient builders. Alas! even the humble shepherd\u2019s straw hut we met along the road held within its frail frame a stronger promise of longevity than the entire human race. How could we square this melancholy transformation with our former aspirations and imagined powers?\\n\\nSuddenly an inward voice, distinct and even, seemed to speak:\u2014Thus was it decreed from eternity: the steeds that race with Time bore this hour and this fulfilment linked to them, ever since the void first yielded its burthen. Would you attempt to reverse the immutable ordinances of Necessity?\\n\\nMother of the world! Handmaid of the Almighty! eternal and unchanging Necessity! thou who with tireless fingers art forever weaving the inextricable chain of events!\u2014I will not complain of thy workings. If my mortal mind cannot confess that all that exists is perfect; yet since whatever exists must be, I will sit amid the wreckage and smile. Verily we were born not for delight, but for submission and for hope.\\n\\nWould the reader grow weary if I minutely chronicled our tedious pilgrimage from Paris to Geneva? Were I, day by day, to register in journal form the pressing miseries of our condition, could my hand achieve, or could language supply phrases sufficient, to declare the variety of our unhappiness\u2014the jostling and piling of one woeful event upon another? Patience, oh reader! whoever thou art, wherever thou abidest\u2014whether of spiritual lineage, or descended from some surviving pair\u2014thy nature shall still be human, thy dwelling-place the earth; thou shalt peruse here the deeds of the extinct race, and shalt demand in astonishment whether they who endured what is set down before thee were beings of fragile flesh and tender organization like thyself. Most true, they were\u2014 therefore weep; for surely, solitary one, thou wilt be of kindly disposition; shed pitying tears; yet meanwhile lend thine ear to the narrative, and learn the actions and sufferings of those that came before thee.\\n\\nNevertheless the final occurrences that attended our passage through France were so crowded with uncanny horrors and dismal griefs that I dare not dwell upon them long. Were I to analyze every incident, each fleeting breath of a second would comprise a heart-rending history, whose slightest syllable would freeze the blood in thy young veins. It is fitting that I raise for thy instruction this memorial of the vanished race; but it is not meet that I drag thee through hospital wards or the hidden chambers of the charnel-house.\"}"
        }
