ersuasion weaken her resolve.\\n\\n\u201cYou dance so well, Miss Eliza, that it is cruel to deny me the pleasure of seeing you; and though this gentleman dislikes the amusement in general, I am sure he cannot object to oblige us for half an hour.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMr. Darcy is all politeness,\u201d said Elizabeth, smiling.\\n\\n\u201cHe is, indeed; but considering the incentive, my dear Miss Eliza, we cannot be surprised at his politeness, for who would object to such a partner?\u201d\\n\\nElizabeth gave him an arch look and turned away. Her refusal had not hurt her in Mr. Darcy\u2019s opinion, and he was thinking of her with some satisfaction when Miss Bingley addressed him.\"}"
