          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"9d8bb9afe072bdc411f2afed\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cOne more word, Rose. Dearest Rose, just one more!\u201d Harry pleaded, stepping in front of her. \u201cIf I had been less\u2014less fortunate, as people say\u2014if I\u2019d been meant for some quiet, hidden life\u2014if I\u2019d been poor, sick, helpless\u2014would you have turned away from me then? Or did this doubt come only because of my likely rise to wealth and honor?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cPlease don\u2019t push me to answer,\u201d Rose replied. \u201cThat situation hasn\u2019t come up and never will. It\u2019s unfair, almost unkind, to insist.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIf your answer is what I hardly dare hope it is,\u201d Harry said, \u201cit will cast a ray of happiness on my lonely road and light what lies ahead. It isn\u2019t trivial to do so much, with just a few short words, for someone who loves you above everything. Oh, Rose, in the name of my passionate and steady devotion; in the name of all I\u2019ve suffered because of you, and all you consign me to endure; answer me this one question!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen if your fate had been different,\u201d Rose answered, \u201cif you\u2019d been only a little, but not so far, above me; if I could have helped and comforted you in any modest life of peace and seclusion, and not been a stain and hindrance among ambitious, distinguished crowds, I would have been spared this ordeal. I have every reason to be happy\u2014very happy\u2014now; but then, Harry, I admit I would have been happier.\u201d\\n\\nMemories of her girlhood hopes rushed back to Rose as she said this, but they brought tears with them, as old hopes do when they return dead and gone; and they eased her heart.\\n\\n\u201cI can\u2019t help this weakness, and it only makes my resolve stronger,\u201d Rose said, holding out her hand. \u201cI have to leave you now, truly.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI ask one promise,\u201d Harry said. \u201cOnce, and only once more\u2014within a year, though it might be sooner\u2014I may speak to you again about this, for the last time.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot to push me to give up a right decision,\u201d Rose answered with a sorrowful smile; \u201cit would be pointless.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo,\u201d Harry said. \u201cJust to hear you repeat it, if you will\u2014repeat it for good. I\u2019ll lay whatever position or fortune I have at your feet; and if you still hold to your decision, I won\u2019t try, by word or deed, to change it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen let it be so,\u201d Rose said. \u201cIt\u2019s just one more pain, and by then I may be able to bear it better.\u201d\\n\\nShe held out her hand again.\"}"
