          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"ac092fe42562b27aefc603b7\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cIf I cannot exist on that, I will not ask aid from any man. Is it content?\u201d\\n\\nA tremendous roar of acclamation burst forth, and above it the king cried:\\n\\n\u201cLoose his bonds, give him liberty! Pay him homage, high and low, rich and poor alike, for he has become the king\u2019s right arm, vested with might and authority, and his seat is upon the highest step of the throne! Now chase away this crawling night, bring back the light and gladness, that all the world may bless thee.\u201d\\n\\nBut I answered:\\n\\n\u201cThat a common fellow be humbled before the world is nothing; yet it were dishonor to the king if any who saw his minister unclad did not also see him freed from his disgrace. Might I request that my garments be returned?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThey are unfitting,\u201d the king interposed. \u201cBring raiment of a nobler sort; apparel him as a prince!\u201d\\n\\nMy scheme prospered. I needed things to remain just so until the eclipse reached its height; otherwise they would pester me again to shoo away the darkness, which I plainly could not do. Calling for clothing bought me a bit of delay, though not sufficient. So I devised a fresh excuse: I declared it reasonable to suppose the king might reconsider, might somewhat repent of what frenzy had made him do; therefore I would let the gloom deepen, and if after a proper interval he still held his purpose, the night should be banished. The king disliked it, and so did the rest, but I held fast.\\n\\nIt became ever darker, blacker, while I fought with those clumsy sixth-century clothes. At last the place was in utter blackness, and the crowd groaned with horror as chill uncanny winds stole through and the stars pricked out above. When the eclipse reached its utter fullness I was thankful, though all others suffered, as was only natural. I proclaimed:\\n\\n\u201cThe king, by his silence, yet abides by the compact.\u201d I raised my hands, held them aloft a moment, then intoned with dreadful solemnity: \u201cLet the enchantment melt away and pass without harm!\u201d\\n\\nThere came no immediate answer in that profound gloom, that graveyard stillness. But when the bright rim of the sun thrust forward a breath later, the whole assembly erupted with a colossal cheer and swept toward me like a flood to bury me under blessings and thanks\u2014and Clarence, rest assured, was not the last of the tide.\"}"
        }
