          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"2ae2b556e376c5676eed2e47\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Ever since the night we took him to the stairs and sent him abroad, I had watched carefully for any sign that we were suspected. I saw none. We certainly had not been, and were not then, followed or watched by any boat. If a boat had trailed us, I would have rowed to shore and forced her either to pass on or to show her purpose. But we kept on without any sign of interference.\\n\\nHe wore his boat-cloak and, as I have said, looked like a natural part of the scene. It was notable\u2014though perhaps the miserable life he had led explained it\u2014that he worried least of all of us. He was not careless, for he told me he hoped to live to see his gentleman become one of the best gentlemen in a foreign country. He was not passive or resigned, as I understood it, but he refused to go out of his way to meet danger. When danger came, he faced it, yet he would not bother about it until it arrived.\\n\\n\u201cIf you knew, dear boy,\u201d he said to me, \u201cwhat it is to sit here next to my dear boy and have my smoke, after being shut up day after day between four walls, you\u2019d envy me. But you don\u2019t know what it is.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI think I know the pleasures of freedom,\u201d I answered.\\n\\n\u201cAh,\u201d he said, shaking his head gravely. \u201cBut you don\u2019t know it like me. You\u2019d have to be locked up, dear boy, to know it like me\u2014but I ain\u2019t going to be low.\u201d\\n\\nIt seemed inconsistent to me that he would risk his freedom and even his life for any pressing idea. Yet I thought that perhaps freedom without danger was too far from the life he had always known to be to him what it would be to another man. I was not far off, since he said after smoking a little:\\n\\n\u201cYou see, dear boy, when I was over yonder, on the other side of the world, I was always looking this way; and it grew dull to stay there, even though I was getting rich. Everyone knew Magwitch, and Magwitch could come and go, and nobody would be troubled about him. They ain\u2019t so easy about me here, dear boy\u2014wouldn\u2019t be, at least, if they knew where I was.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIf all goes well,\u201d said I, \u201cyou will be completely free and safe again in a few hours.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell,\u201d he said, drawing a long breath, \u201cI hope so.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd you believe so?\u201d\"}"
        }
