          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"a265733a6c5a41562a55d905\",\"rewritten_text\":\"So I said I needed the watermelon. But he answered that I didn\u2019t need it to bust out of prison with; that was the difference. He said if I\u2019d wanted it to hide a knife in and smuggle it to Jim so he could kill the seneschal, then it would\u2019ve been fine. I let it drop after that, though I couldn\u2019t see the point of representing a prisoner if I had to sit there chewing over a bunch of gold-leaf distinctions every time I saw a chance to swipe a watermelon.\\n\\nAnyway, like I was saying, we waited that morning until everyone was settled down to their tasks and nobody was in sight around the yard; then Tom carried the sack into the lean-to while I stood back a bit to keep watch. Soon he came out, and we went over and sat on the woodpile to talk. He said:\\n\\n\u201cEverything\u2019s set now except for tools, and that\u2019s easy to fix.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTools?\u201d I said.\\n\\n\u201cYeah.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTools for what?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTo dig with. We\u2019re not going to gnaw him out, are we?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAren\u2019t those old busted picks and things in there good enough to dig a slave out with?\u201d I said.\\n\\nHe spun on me, looking so pitying it would make you want to cry, and said:\\n\\n\u201cHuck Finn, did you ever hear of a prisoner having picks and shovels and all the modern conveniences in his wardrobe to dig himself out with? Now I want to ask you\u2014if you\u2019ve got any reason in you at all\u2014what kind of chance would that give him to be a hero? They might as well lend him the key and be done with it. Picks and shovels\u2014why, they wouldn\u2019t hand them to a king.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell then,\u201d I said, \u201cif we don\u2019t want the picks and shovels, what do we want?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cA couple of table knives.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTo dig the foundations out from under that cabin with?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYeah.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDang it, that\u2019s ridiculous, Tom.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt doesn\u2019t matter how ridiculous it is, it\u2019s the right way\u2014and the proper way. And there isn\u2019t any other way I ever heard of, and I\u2019ve read every book that gives information about these things. They always dig out with a table knife\u2014and not through dirt, either; usually it\u2019s through solid rock. And it takes them weeks and weeks and weeks, forever and ever. Why, think about that prisoner in the bottom dungeon of the Ch\u00e2teau d\u2019If, in the harbor of Marseilles, who dug himself out that way; how long do you figure he worked at it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t know.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, guess.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t know\u2014maybe a month and a half.\u201d\"}"
