          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"29e672229bab3160473e7f7e\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Recent reports from Rotterdam say the city is in a frenzy of philosophical excitement. Events there were so unexpected\u2014so new, so completely against accepted beliefs\u2014that I am sure all Europe is now in uproar, physics in turmoil, and reason and astronomy at each other\u2019s throats.\\n\\nOn the \u2014\u2014 day of \u2014\u2014 (I am not sure of the date), a great crowd gathered for unspecified reasons in the large square before the Exchange in tidy Rotterdam. The weather was warm\u2014unusually so for that time of year\u2014with barely a breath of wind. The crowd did not mind being occasionally sprinkled by brief friendly showers that fell from large white clouds, which mottled the blue sky in a restless pattern. Still, around noon, a slight but notable agitation ran through the gathering. Ten thousand tongues began clattering, and a moment later ten thousand faces turned upward, ten thousand pipes dropped from ten thousand mouths, and a shout, compared only to Niagara\u2019s roar, rang long and loud through the outskirts of Rotterdam.\\n\\nThe cause of this uproar soon became clear. From behind the massive bulk of one of those sharply defined clouds emerged, very slowly into a patch of blue sky, a strange, mixed, yet apparently solid object. It was so oddly shaped, so whimsy in construction, that the crowd of strong burghers could neither grasp it nor admire it enough. What could it be? In the name of all the housewives and devils in Rotterdam, what sign could it hold? No one knew, no one could guess; not even the burgomaster, Mynheer Superbus Von Underduk, had the slightest clue to solve the mystery. So, as nothing else could be done, everyone carefully replaced his pipe in the corner of his mouth, cocked his right eye at the phenomenon, puffed, paused, waddled about, grunted meaningfully\u2014then waddled back, grunted, paused, and finally puffed again.\\n\\nMeanwhile the object of so much curiosity\u2014and so much smoke\u2014descended lower and lower toward the admirable city. Within a few minutes it was close enough to see clearly. It seemed to be\u2014yes! it was definitely a kind of balloon; but surely no balloon like this had ever floated over Rotterdam before.\"}"
