          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"2e949022ead1caa6237dc0e3\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cDo you play?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI think, sir,\u201d replied the spy, in his humblest tone as he turned toward Mr. Lorry, \u201cI may appeal to a gentleman of your years and kindness to persuade this other gentleman, so much your junior, that he cannot possibly reconcile it with his rank to use the Ace he speaks of. I grant that I am a spy, and that it is counted a discreditable role\u2014though someone must perform it; but this gentleman is not a spy, and why should he descend to make himself one?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI lay down my Ace, Mr. Barsad,\u201d said Carton, taking up the reply himself and glancing at his watch, \u201cwithout a qualm, in just a few minutes.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI should have hoped, gentlemen,\u201d said the spy, always trying to draw Mr. Lorry into the exchange, \u201cthat your regard for my sister\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI could pay no better homage to your sister than by finally freeing her from her brother,\u201d Sydney Carton interposed.\\n\\n\u201cYou do not think so, sir?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI am completely resolved.\u201d\\n\\nThe spy\u2019s smooth manner, oddly at odds with his ostentatiously coarse attire and likely with his usual behavior, met such resistance from Carton\u2019s impenetrability\u2014Carton who baffled wiser and more honest men\u2014that it faltered and failed him. While he hesitated, Carton resumed his former pose of studying the cards:\\n\\n\u201cAnd indeed, now that I reconsider, I have a distinct impression I hold another strong card uncounted. That friend and fellow-Sheep who mentioned pasturing in the rural prisons; who was he?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFrench. You don\u2019t know him,\u201d the spy answered quickly.\\n\\n\u201cFrench, eh?\u201d Carton echoed, musing, seeming not to notice, though he repeated the word. \u201cWell; perhaps.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHe is, I assure you,\u201d said the spy; \u201cthough it doesn\u2019t matter.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThough it doesn\u2019t matter,\u201d Carton repeated in the same mechanical tone\u2014\u201cthough it doesn\u2019t matter\u2014No, it doesn\u2019t matter. No. Yet I recognize the face.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI think not. I\u2019m certain not. It\u2019s impossible,\u201d said the spy.\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s-impossible,\u201d Sydney Carton muttered, thinking back, toying again with his glass (luckily a small one). \u201cImpossible. Spoke excellent French. Yet I thought like a foreigner?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cProvincial,\u201d said the spy.\\n\\n\u201cNo. Foreign!\u201d Carton cried, striking his open palm on the table as a flash of understanding lit his mind. \u201cCly! Disguised, but the same man. We had him before us at the Old Bailey.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThere, you are rash, sir,\u201d Barsad replied, with a smile that gave his aquiline nose even more of a tilt; \u201cthere you actually put me at an advantage over you.\u201d\"}"
