          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"b652c15ef5cc74fbb77a5781\",\"rewritten_text\":\"But when I saw you become the object of another\u2019s love\u2014when I pictured someone cherishing you not just as a sacred symbol of beauty and virtue, or you loving someone else with a fiercer passion than you felt for me\u2014the fiend inside me awoke. I sent your lover away, and from that instant I have known no peace. I have begged for sleep and rest in vain; my eyes would not close, and my blood never settled. I woke to a new existence like one who dies in hope and finds himself in hell. I will not stain your thoughts by revealing my inner battles, my fury at myself, or my despair. Let a veil cover the unimaginable feelings of a guilty father; the secrets of such a tortured heart cannot be laid bare. Everything became noise, crime, remorse, and hatred, yet also the tenderest love; and what first drove me to vow that I would conquer my passion and restore a father to my child was seeing your bitter, compassionate grief. That is what brought me here: I believed that if I could awaken again the grief I felt at your mother\u2019s death, and revive the many memories of her that had lain dormant for seventeen years, any love for her child would fade. In a burst of heroism I resolved to come alone, to leave you\u2014the very life of my life\u2014and not see you again until I could do so without guilt. But it failed: I overvalued my strength or undervalued my love. I would surely have died if you had not hurried to my side. I almost wish I had been extinguished.\\n\\nAnd now, Mathilda, I must make my final confession. I was wretchedly wrong to think I could overcome my love for you; I never can. The sight of this house, these fields and woods where my first love once lived has only deepened it. In my madness I dared to tell myself\u2014Diana died to bring her child into the world; her spirit passed into her daughter, and you should be Diana to me. The harder I try to cast off this love, the tighter it clings\u2014this guilty passion, more unnatural than hatred, that withers your hopes and destroys me forever.\\n\\nBetter to have fallen in love with despair, and safer to have kissed her.\\n\\nNo stretch of time or distance can tear from my soul what has become part of it. Since I arrived here, not even for a moment has the hell of passion left me, implanted to burn until all is cold, rigid, and dead.\"}"
