          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"758342e0fbb5ddb74191cbff\",\"rewritten_text\":\"He fixed upon Friday, the 17th of August, for his reappearance, and devoted most of the day to inspecting his wardrobe, ultimately favouring a broad slouch hat with a crimson plume, a winding-sheet trimmed at the neck and cuffs, and a rusty dagger. Toward evening a fierce rainstorm burst, the wind blowing so fiercely that every window and door in the old house rattled and shook, precisely the weather that pleased him most. His course of action was arranged thus: he would slip quietly into Washington Otis\u2019s chamber, gibber at him from the foot of the bed, and plunge the dagger into his own throat three times to the accompaniment of slow music. He cherished a particular rancour against Washington, fully aware that he was the one accustomed to erase the celebrated Canterville bloodstain with Pinkerton\u2019s Paragon Detergent. Once the bold, heedless lad had been reduced to utter terror, he would move on to the room of the United States Minister and his wife, lay a clammy palm upon Mrs. Otis\u2019s brow, and whisper into her trembling husband\u2019s ear the dreadful secrets of the charnel-house. Regarding little Virginia, he remained undecided. She had never offended him, and was both lovely and sweet. A few hollow groans from the wardrobe ought, he thought, to suffice, or, should that fail to rouse her, he might claw at the bedspread with palsied twitching fingers. As for the twins, he meant to give them a thorough lesson. First, he must of course sit upon their chests to induce the suffocating sensation of nightmare. Then, as their beds stood close together, he would position himself between them in the guise of a green, icy-cold corpse until they were paralysed with fright, and finally tear away the winding-sheet and creep round the chamber with bleach-white bones and one rolling eyeball as \u2018Dumb Daniel, or the Suicide\u2019s Skeleton,\u2019 a r\u00f4le in which he had on more than one night produced a stunning impression, and which he deemed fully equal to his famed portrayal of \u2018Martin the Maniac, or the Masked Mystery.\u2019\\n\\nAt half-past ten he heard the household retire. For a while the twins\u2019 shrill peals of laughter, the merry mirth of schoolboys amusing themselves before sleep, disturbed him, but by a quarter past eleven all was quiet, and as the clock struck midnight he set out. The owl battered the windowpanes, the raven croaked from the ancient yew-tree, and the wind wandered round the house, moaning like a lost soul; yet the Otis family slumbered unaware of their fate, and above the rain and gale he could plainly catch the steady snore of the Minister of the United States.\"}"
